At the meeting, the Cambodian Permanent Representative to the United Nations issued a statement stating that Cambodia does not participate in the statement made on behalf of any group and considers the Palestinian-Israeli conflict a complex issue. And the most fragile.
In this meeting, the Cambodian representative fully confirmed the following:
1. I am honored to address this meeting on behalf of a country, Cambodia, which has recently been engulfed in the flames of decades of war and the Killing Fields. Becoming oppressive and oppressed, they were engulfed in flames of hatred, revenge, and extremism, leading to the most heinous crime against humanity.
2. My delegation would like to express our deepest condolences for the loss of so many innocent lives, including one Cambodian, from October 7 to the present, as well as in Palestine and Israel. The Palestinian-Israeli conflict is the most complex and fragile issue, so Cambodia would like to state its principled position on this issue, without participating in statements made on behalf of any group.
3. Cambodia condemns all acts of terrorism and violence against innocent civilians, regardless of race, culture or religion. We are deeply concerned about the escalation of violence, misery and loss of life of innocent people, women, children, infants and the elderly on the territory of the current conflict.
5. The President of the General Assembly, let me recap three points that I have already raised during the Security Council's recent open debate.
Third, we call on the international community to unite in a spirit of genuine unity and sincerity to promote meaningful dialogue and dialogue leading to a just and lasting peace.
6. Please stop pointing fingers at each other, please give me a chance for peace, let there be love for all humanity on the planet without racism and religion. Please empower the forces of moderate extremism to allow the people of Israel and Palestine to live side by side in lasting peace, security and harmony.
7. Once again, my delegation commends the dedication and sacrifice of UN staff and humanitarian workers who have endured the risks and dangers of bringing relief to innocent civilians. .
