(Phnom Penh): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of the Environment, has again warned that perpetrators of natural resource crimes are no exception, as they will face the law in force.
Speaking at the program to encourage environmentally friendly operators and award the winners of the "Safe Village-Commune-Sangkat" competition in the 6th Qualification Framework 2023 on October 26, the Minister of Environment stressed that "you You can escape that day, but tomorrow you will not be able to escape! You are not comfortable sleeping because I follow you all the time! You can forget, but I do not forget!
In addition, Dr. Eang Sophalleth confirmed that all cases of crime must be filed to the court to take action in accordance with the law.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth recalled the introduction of four main measures to effectively manage natural resources and conserve biodiversity and for sustainable development. The four measures include:
First. 100% law enforcement and end culture, education, guidance and contracting and release of natural resource perpetrators
Second. Cooperate with Capital-Provincial Administrative Unity Command, especially with local authorities to prevent natural resource crime in protected areas
Third. Cooperation with the Anti-Corruption Unit and the National Gendarmerie Command to suppress and prevent natural resource crimes in addition to the cooperation with local authorities in the past.
And 4. Planting more trees than felling to maintain growth, especially the promotion of afforestation as a priority, increase forest cover by 60% by 2050 in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's Pentagon strategy and improve the livelihoods of people in Community Sustainable Biodiversity Conservation.
Mr. Chhay Duong Savuth, Director of Kratie Provincial Department of Environment, supported the measures put forward by His Excellency the Minister of Environment, stating that he would strive to enforce the law strictly and effectively with the patrol activities like the early rain. According to the natural resource protection area within its jurisdiction.
Similarly, Mr. Sreng Chea Heng, Director of the Stung Treng Provincial Department of Environment, confirmed the position of law enforcement without exception for individuals who commit crimes against natural resources. That is, end the culture of making contracts and releasing them and turning to the rule of law without exception.
It should be noted that by implementing the order of the Minister of Environment on the above four measures, the inspection team of the Ministry of Environment led by Mr. Chea Sam Ang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, on October 24-25, inspected directly on the suspected site. Natural resource crimes occur in the "Prey Lang" wildlife sanctuary in Kratie province.
The inspection, which also involved partner organizations, was carried out after the media reported that a new road had been stolen to transport timber from the protected area.
