Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron: The Ministry encourages students to study hard rather than fail exams and protest the results (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Students should not complain about the exam results because the Ministry has organized the exam process well and the preparation of subjects, versions and other techniques, etc., which ensures transparency and accuracy.
Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron made this statement at a press conference on "Higher Secondary Diploma Examination Process, Exam Session November 6, 2023" at the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the afternoon of October 27, 2023.
Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron said that the Ministry encourages all students to study hard to succeed in the exam, but the Ministry does not encourage students to protest.
He said that in the exam, no country allows students to protest, because the exam is like the entrance exam, if you do not pass the exam can not protest.
He added: "In principle, all exams in other countries are not allowed to protest because of the fact that during this exam, we take all the steps and check the preparation of the subject of the subject to ensure that. Accurate correction, careful correction by revision rate, and also more verification to ensure that this result reflects the ability of students. "But there are always students protesting."
He confirmed that in the past, there have been protests from students of the Ministry, who always check and select samples to check again in case there are any gaps. However, every review never found a problem.
He added that this correction will make the correction tighter and it may lower the student's score.
"Overall, I would like to inform that the technical aspects, we guarantee that this exam is conducted in accordance with the four principles, we are transparent and ensure that the results will be acceptable, both legal principles," he said.
