Prime Minister Hun Manet instructs relevant institutions to rehabilitate flood-damaged infrastructure and study to avoid this impact (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Prime Minister of Cambodia Hun Manet on October 27 The year 2023 has instructed relevant institutions to rehabilitate infrastructure damaged by floods and study to avoid the effects of floods.
During the plenary session of the Council of Ministers, Samdech Hun Sen instructed the relevant institutions to rehabilitate the flood-damaged infrastructure and provide rice seeds to farmers to start planting again.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet advised the relevant institutions to study in detail to avoid the impact of future floods in any area that can be reduced or avoided.
Samdech Hun Sen also thanked the National Committee for Disaster Management and relevant institutions for their timely intervention in rescuing people from the floods and advised to continue to be prepared at all times.
His Excellency Hun Manet's message read: "I am deeply saddened to learn of the death in Shanghai this morning of His Excellency Li Keqiang, Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the Central Committee of the Communist Party. 17th, 18th and 19th China and former Chinese Prime Minister.
The death of His Excellency Li Keqiang is the loss of one of the most prominent political figures in the history of the People's Republic of China, who has directly contributed to the stability of China.
His Excellency Ly Ker Chheang will always be remembered as a friend of Cambodia. As Prime Minister, HE Li Keqiang visited the Kingdom of Cambodia in 2018 and 2022, during which a number of cooperation documents were signed in various fields, including infrastructure, agriculture, energy, health, climate change, customs. Chinese traditional medicine technology and education.
HE Li Keqiang also played an active role in relations with ASEAN leaders during the ASEAN-China Summit and the ASEAN Plus Three Summit.
At this sad time, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, I would like to extend my deepest condolences to His Excellency, the family of the deceased and the Chinese people for the great loss of a great statesman. May the soul of His Excellency Ly Ker Chheang go to his death, do not mourn. "
