(Phnom Penh): Mr. Seng Teak is the founder of the Global Fund for Nature Conservation in Cambodia, a Cambodian intellectual who has spent 25 years in the protection, conservation and conservation of Cambodia's Mekong River dolphins as well as rare wildlife. More with the government, relevant ministries, partner organizations and other target communities. More than 5 tons of frozen meat were arrested by Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police and sent to professional officers
(Kampong Chhnang): A heavy truck transporting illegal frozen meat from Banteay Meanchey province through Kampong Chhnang province was stopped by the Economic Crimes Police of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police and handed over to the Provincial Veterinary Office for legal action.
The case of cracking down on the above-mentioned illegal frozen meat truck took place at 13:30 on October 26, 2023 at Pring Kong village, Cheung Kreav commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province.
According to the Economic Crimes Police of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police, the operation was led by Lieutenant Colonel Nuon Sopheak, Deputy Chief of the Economic Crimes Police Office, under the direct command of Major General Khov Ly, Police Commissioner. Kampong Chhnang Province and under the coordination of Mr. Ek Sunrasmey, Prosecutor of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court.
The police further confirmed that the truck that was stopped by the police was a heavy-duty Mitsubishi BC with license plate Battambang 3A-3253. 28-year-old resident of Kork Khpos village, Doung Chrey commune, Thmor Kol district, Battambang province.
In this case, after consulting with the Major General, the Commissioner and the Prosecutor, the above-mentioned illegal frozen meat truck was handed over to the specialized officer of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Production and Veterinary Office for further action.
He added that for the truck transporting frozen meat that was detained by the authorities, his professional officers found that the truck did not have a certificate of hygiene of frozen meat in the transport, and the transport was wrong and Non-standard, no freezer for refrigeration to maintain meat quality. In this case, the procedure continues, he is asking for principles from the prosecutor of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court to deal with today as well.
Stock Exchange chief and land tycoon tell how to prepare for the economic crisis
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hong So Hour, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange and Duke Dr. Kim Heang, Founder of Vimean Samnang Borey, shared his ideas and experiences related to understanding and preparing for the crisis to the member business owners. Founding Friends Club to keep the business running smoothly and out of the crisis.
On that occasion, Mr. Hong Sochua presented the economic cycle, which shows the normal fluctuations of the economy and the need for business owners to recognize this movement and be ready to lead the business to adapt to this movement.
He said that usually the state of economic growth will cause the conditions for the economic crisis later and the state of the economic crisis will create the conditions for economic growth later. Successful business owners and investors, big and long-term, are the ones who see this movement right. Wrong business or investment decisions can lead to problems or even bankruptcy.
Dr. Kim Heang shared his experience in running his business in the last few years during a time when the Cambodian economy was facing many challenges. He urged business owners to continue to develop their own capabilities, strengthen business management systems, reduce unnecessary costs, strengthen sales, especially to be busy with sales, not busy with other things.
He introduced four principles for doing business in a crisis economy, including: motivating employees, understanding cash management, understanding the economic cycle and business cycle.
He also outlined the strategy of how to make the business survive the crisis, especially cost management.
Please be informed that the program to share ideas and experiences related to understanding and preparing for the crisis was held on October 21, 2023.
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Khuon Sodary, on October 27, 2023, sent a letter of condolence and condolences to Mr. Zhao Leji, President of the National Assembly. The People's Republic of China on the death of Li Keqiang, former Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China.
Former Prime Minister Li Keqiang's noble contribution and tireless efforts to the nation in promoting economic development and promoting international relations are widely recognized. The visionary leadership, unwavering commitment and dedication to strengthening cooperation between our two nations have left an unforgettable identity in our bilateral relations between Cambodia and China. .
The Cambodian people will always remember the efforts of Prime Minister Li Keqiang. Let us all pray and pray with the Chinese people and the family of Prime Minister Li during this sad time. Please pray for His Excellency the President to be strong and feel relieved to remember the memories of His amazing life.
I firmly believe that the legacy of former Prime Minister Li Keqiang will forever be in the hearts of the Chinese people as brothers and sisters, and I pray for the well-being of His Excellency to rest in peace.
Your Excellency, I would like to express my deepest condolences to all of you and inform you that the hearts and hearts of the Cambodian people will always be with you and the Chinese people during the mourning period for the loss of our leader. And this great statesman. ”
