(Battambang): Two drug criminals were cracked down by the Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie together with a total of 25 packages of ice cubes weighing 10 kg and 334.60 grams, a Honda CRV with license plate Phnom Penh. 2AA-9869 Two mobile phones on October 25, 2023 and sent to the provincial court on June 26, 2023.
Gen. Hem Vuthy, Commander of the Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie, confirmed that after a long period of professional investigation into drug trafficking, and in accordance with the direct orders of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief. The National Gendarmerie Command, with the coordination of Mr. Keo Socheat, Prosecutor of the Battambang Provincial Prosecutor's Office, immediately cracked down.
Colonel Rong Pok said that the two suspects who were detained by the police were: Bou Sophat, alias Hul, 63, of Otakham 1 village, Sangkat Toul Ta Ek, Battambang city, Battambang province, and Ly Thearith, 42. Address: Kang Va Village, Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Colonel Rong Pok said that after receiving an order from the Commander-in-Chief, he led a specialized force to arrest the two suspects and confiscate a total of 25 packages of ice cubes. 10 kg and 334.60 g, a Honda CRV with license plate Phnom Penh 2AA-9869, 2 mobile phones on October 25, 2023.
After receiving the confessions from the suspects, General Hem Vuthy and Mr. Keo Socheat, Prosecutor of the Battambang Provincial Prosecutor's Office, Mr. Thou Phea, Deputy Provincial Governor, and Mr. Sok Loo, Deputy Governor of Battambang Provincial Deputy Commander, joined forces. An autopsy on the suspects in front of the suspects observed that the white powder was indeed a drug.
Fears of escalating conflict in the Middle East that could plunge Iran and its allies into the war have helped fuel oil prices in recent weeks, but fears are also driving investors to sell off assets. Active, too risky.
US crude inventories have also risen in recent weeks, signaling a drop in demand. According to the US Energy Information Administration, US crude inventories rose 1.4 million barrels to 421.1 million barrels, beating analysts' estimates in a Reuters poll of 240,000. Barrel.
Data from the International Energy Agency (EIA) showed that crude oil refining in the United States fell 207,000 barrels a day, while refinery utilization fell 0.5 percent to 85 percent. , 56% of total refining capacity.
Macroeconomic concerns continue to weigh on oil demand prospects after a sharp slump this month in eurozone business activity data.
