"Governments, companies and investors need to be behind clean energy shifts rather than hinder them," he added.
However, the IEA also said that in the current situation, fossil fuel demand could remain too high to meet the goals of the Paris Agreement on Climate Change, which limits global warming. The average temperature is 1.5 degrees Celsius.
"This risk not only exacerbates the effects of the weather after the highest temperatures ever, but also undermines the security of the energy system," the energy agency said in a statement. "Made for a colder world with less climate."
