He expressed the hope that the establishment of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution outside the Judiciary would contribute to providing justice and harmonization and resolving disputes to the people, but not to replace the courts, but to complement existing mechanisms.
Samdech Thep Dey considered the establishment of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution outside the Judiciary as an urgent task and must be expedited as soon as possible.
Samdech Mani Hun Sen: The mechanism for resolving disputes outside the judiciary is not forcing people to choose, but to be voluntary (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia The extrajudicial disputes that the Royal Government is currently organizing are not forcing people to choose to use this service, but to provide additional options and to be used voluntarily.
This assertion of Samdech Hun Sen was made at the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers at the Peace Palace this morning, October 27, 2023, by discussing and approving four agendas. In the discussion on the first agenda is the draft Royal Decree on the establishment, organization and operation of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution outside the judiciary.
Samdech hopes that this new mechanism will be able to help the people and calls for widespread dissemination to explain to the people.
It should be noted that this morning, October 27, the Council of Ministers fully approved the draft Royal Decree on the establishment, organization and operation of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution outside the Judiciary.
Establishment of the National Dispute Resolution Authority as a complementary mechanism to the dispute resolution system in Cambodia aimed at improving the quality, efficiency and speed of dispute resolution through out-of-court mediation in order to reduce congestion According to the tribunal, the dispute resolution service should be closer to the local people and ensure harmony and justice in the society.
1. Personal information and educational background
From 1978 to 1982, he was a law student and president of the Peking University Student Union.
1988-1994 Received a master's degree and a doctorate in economics from Peking University.
* September-November 1991: Studied at the Central School of the Communist Party of China.
2. Work history
May 1976 Joins the Communist Party of China
1982-1983: Secretary of the CPC Central Committee of the Communist Party of China at Peking University and member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee
1983-1985: Director of the Department of Education of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China Youth League, Secretary-General of the National Students' Federation of China, Member of the Secretariat of the Communist Party of China Central Committee
1985-1993 Member of the Secretariat of the Central Committee of the Communist Youth League of China and Vice Chairman of the National Youth Federation of China
1993-1998: Chairman of the Secretariat of the Central Committee of the Communist Youth League of China and Dean of the Faculty of Political Science, Youth of China.
1998-1999: Deputy Secretary of the CPC Henan Provincial Committee and Acting Governor of Henan Province.
1999-2002: Deputy Secretary of the CPC Henan Provincial Committee and Governor of Henan Province, and Chairman of the Yellow River Flood Management Command.
2002-2003 Deputy Secretary of the CPC Henan Provincial Committee and Governor of Henan Province
2003-2004: Deputy Secretary of the CPC Henan Provincial Committee and chairman of the Standing Committee of the CPC Henan Provincial People's Congress.
2004-2005: Secretary of the CPC Liaoning Provincial Committee of the Communist Party of China.
2005-2007: Secretary of the CPC Liaoning Provincial Committee and Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Liaoning Provincial People's Congress
2007-2008 Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee
2008-2013 Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Deputy Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China
* 2013-2018 Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China
Li Keqiang remained a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee until October 2022, and his term as prime minister officially expired in March 2023.
