This bilateral meeting is part of the Investment Conservation Mechanism, which was established on 11 August 2009 under the framework of the Agreement between Cambodia and Japan on Liberalization, Promotion and Protection of Investment, signed by Former Cambodian Prime Minister and former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe on June 14, 2007.
The Deputy Prime Minister extended a warm welcome to the presence of the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, representatives of Japanese ministries, institutions, associations, organizations and the private sector in Japan.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister also thanked all Japanese investors who have strengthened and expanded their business operations and investment projects in Cambodia.
He said that this reflects the trust of foreign investors, in general, Japanese investors in the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the maximum opportunity for peace, macroeconomic stability, favorable investment environment. And an open investment regime that is conducive to investment and ensures competitiveness.
The Ambassador congratulated the Deputy Prime Minister on the appointment of the First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia by the Royal Government of the 7th legislature under the leadership of the Prime Minister. We strongly believe that the presence of the Deputy Prime Minister will continue to contribute to the strengthening and expansion of bilateral cooperation in promoting and attracting high quality and standard investment.
At the same time, he praised the Council for the Development of Cambodia and all relevant ministries and institutions for their past efforts to coordinate and provide a gentle response to concerns and concerns. Requests of Japanese investors.
The meeting started to discuss the challenges and requests of the private sector and as a result also received positive solutions to promote further long-term cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the private sector.
Before concluding the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister requested the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, together with the Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO) and the Japan Business Association of Cambodia (JBAC) to cooperate with the Royal Government of Cambodia in organizing programs to Attract investors and promote more positively about Cambodia's investment work and other incentives, explain to potential investors in Japan.
