Senior official of the Ministry of Information warns journalists to abide by the law on journalism, ethics and professionalism
(Siem Reap): Mr. Chea Chanboribo, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information and President of the Electronic Sports Federation of Cambodia, stated that journalists have the role of reporting and writing articles on all topics in order to serve the readers, listeners and viewers of those stories. Adhere to the law on the press, respect the ethics and profession of journalism.
Mr. Chea Chanboribo said this during a press conference on October 26, 2023 at the Siem Reap Provincial Information Department, with the participation of Ms. Mony Rainsy, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap and Mr. Liv Sokhon, Director of the Siem Reap Provincial Information Department. As well as the participation of many journalists.
Mr. Chea Chanboribo said that the writing and reporting of information must be based on the six principles that are the basis for finding the cause of the story, including: who had what happened, when it happened. Where the cause is and how it happens.
At the same time, Ms. Monny Rainsy said that in the digital age, the media sector has played an important role in disseminating information that has both positive and negative effects. Both factors have a profound effect on the audience, the reader and the viewer, because if the information broadcast has a positive content, the society does not have a problem, but if the information published makes it difficult for the recipient and makes Affect the society as well.
In that, before disseminating any information, it must be thoroughly examined and must be implemented in accordance with the profession of journalists to avoid any impact on society, as Samdech Techo gave the slogan, "Do not violate the rights of journalists. Do not distort the truth "to strengthen the professionalism and trust of the public.
She also commended and thanked the leaders of both public and private institutions in the field of information, as well as a large number of journalists who have taken care to perform their duties in accordance with the code of ethics and professionalism in reporting. Information on local events to disseminate widely and disseminate information to local people.
