1,668 Families in Kandeang and Pursat Provinces Receive Rice Seed from Head of Government After Flood Damage
(Pursat): 1,668 families from Kandeang district and Pursat city, each family received 100 kg of rice seeds from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Disaster Management Committee of Cambodia for rehabilitation after Saliva.
The handover ceremony was held on the afternoon of October 26, 2023 at the Provincial Stadium under the chairmanship of Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, Mr. Kong Kea, Advisor to the Ministry and Director of the Rice Department of the Ministry. Agriculture, forestry and fisheries will be attended by the deputy governors, departmental leaders and the three armed forces.
Mr. Khoy Rida said with a message of greetings from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, to the 1,120 families to receive rice seeds, as well as people throughout the province, which Samdech always cares. Take care to solve the food and rice seeds for the people affected by the floods in late September and early October 2023 throughout the province in a timely, transparent, efficient and reliable.
The provincial governor said that the food and rice seeds provided in the past as well as now are a testament to the high level of concern of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia on the living conditions of the affected people. Due to the flood, this is a rice seed for recovery after the flood and facilitate your life without allowing any family to lack food.
At the same time, he advised the officials of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology and local authorities to increase efforts to grow crops, which is the daily food needs of farmers throughout the province.
At the same time, he also encouraged farmers to work hard to grow livestock and increase other occupations in order to jointly rehabilitate and increase the family economy in order to reduce poverty. He would like to congratulate the people of Pursat province who continue to support the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia and get the first place in the country in the 7th legislative election is very proud.
Pursat Mayor Chap Neang reports that Kandeang and Pursat districts were affected by floods in late September and early October 2023, affecting schools, homes, pagodas and infrastructure. .
There are 1,322 hectares of farmland to be rehabilitated, equivalent to 1,668 families, of which Pursat has 3 communes, 9 villages, 548 families, and 355 hectares of rehabilitated area, and Kandeang district has 8 communes, 76 villages. 1,120 families and 967 hectares of rehabilitated land.
