Ministry of Water Resources announces weather condition in Cambodia for October 27, 2023
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for October 27, 2023.
The Ministry states that the Kingdom of Cambodia is affected by low pressure in the South China Sea. The high pressure system covering Thailand and the South China Sea is weakening. While southwesterly and southerly winds bring moisture from the Gulf of Thailand to the coast, while gusts from the east and southeast bring moisture from the South China Sea. On Cambodia.
On October 30, there will be another high pressure system from China covering the northern part of Thailand extending to the South China Sea. Meanwhile, winds from the north and northeast will intersect with the southeasterly winds, which contain the moisture of the South China Sea, forming rain clouds over Cambodia.
Such a situation will make:
From October 27 to 29, in some coastal provinces and some provinces in the central lowlands, including Phnom Penh, there will be moderate to moderate rain mixed with thunder and gusts. On an area of 40% to 50%. Some provinces in the highlands will receive light to moderate rainfall, covering 30% to 40% of the land area.
From October 30 to 31, there will be light to moderate rainfall over the coastal and upland areas, covering 30% to 40% of the land area. The central lowlands will receive moderate rainfall, thunderstorms and gusts over 40% to 60%.
