(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 27, 2023, Samdech Moha Bovathip Hun Sen presided over a plenary session of the Council of Ministers at the Peace Palace to discuss four agendas.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Pen Bona, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, confirmed that the meeting was discussed to pass the following agenda:
* First, the draft Royal Decree on "Establishment, organization and operation of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution outside the Judiciary."
* Second: The draft law on finance for management 2024.
* Third: The draft law on the payment of the general state budget for management in 2022.
* Fourth: Other issues, request for approval from the Council of Ministers for approval by the legislature on the draft law on the approval of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the United Arab Emirates. .
