Pursat Women's Association Branch Donates to Pregnant Women and General Patients at Bakan Referral Hospital
(Pursat): A delegation from the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development in Pursat province, led by Ms. Ang Socheata Khoy Rida, Honorary President of the branch, on the afternoon of October 26, 2023, continued her humanitarian mission to visit pregnant women, women and children. Postpartum and a total of 87 general patients at Bakan Referral Hospital.
On that occasion, Ms. Ang Socheata brought greetings from the leaders of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, especially from Samdech Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who always thinks about the well-being of the people in all circumstances.
She also urged women and their families to continue to pay attention to their health and life and to their unborn and newborn children to adhere to a clean diet, clean drinking and clean living. Thank you to the team of doctors who take care to use professional ethics to help ensure that all women give birth safely.
Ms. Ang Socheata stated that now, as in the past, the sub-branches of the Women's Association Movement at all levels throughout the province have taken care to implement the policy of gender equality in promoting the role and status of women in society and Access to health care and humanitarian work.
In fact, this afternoon, the Provincial Women's Association also organized a visit to 87 pregnant women, women with childbirth and postpartum and general patients, each of whom received a sarong, a scarf, a blanket, a pillow and a mosquito net. 1 and a budget of 20,000 riels. In addition, health workers, sanitation workers and the People's Defense Forces also received the required armbands.
On the same day, the delegation also continued to visit and bring gifts to the Chief of Sangkat Lolok Sor, Pursat City and Dr. Director of Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital, who is being treated at home in Sangkat Lolok Sor and Sangkat Roleap.
It should also be reminded that recently, on the occasion before and after Kan Ben, Pchum Ben, the Women's Association under the support of both budget and material from leaders and members of all levels, as well as philanthropists also organized a series of donations. Relieve the elderly, homeless, widows, poor families, pregnant women and patients in Pursat city, Phnom Kravanh district, Talo Sen Chey district, Krakor district and continue to other districts in Pursat province.
The Cambodian Association of Housing Developers has requested that the Royal Government review the legal aspects in order to allow foreigners the legal right to purchase houses and land in Borey.
(Phnom Penh): Three important topics were discussed by the leaders of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and the Cambodian Housing Developers Association in an emergency meeting.
The meeting "Discussing the situation of the construction sector in Cambodia" was held at the Ministry of Land Management on October 23, 2023 under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
In addition to discussing the current state of the construction sector in Cambodia, which is facing current challenges, and discussing the financial situation to raise funds to support and support the construction sector in Cambodia, there was also a discussion on legal aspects to allow foreigners to Legal right to purchase houses and land in the Borey project as well. This is according to the Cambodian Housing Developers Association.
During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Say Samal also added that the Ministry has prepared a number of additional proposals and policies to submit to the head of the Royal Government to support the construction sector.
Tycoon Ly Hour, President of the Cambodian Housing Developers Association, told Fresh News on October 25, 2023 that this is just a proposal to find a way to solve the problems that housing developers face. However, we need to study Cambodia's laws and constitution, as well as our neighbors and other countries where possible.
