EU leaders meet to find Middle East war solution while maintaining support for Ukraine
(Brussels): EU leaders meet on Thursday to discuss the conflict between Israel and Hamas, and also to show continued support for Ukraine in the fight against Russian aggression. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on October 26, 2023.
The summit in Brussels will be the first direct meeting of the 27 EU leaders since the October 7 deadly attack on Israel by Palestinian Hamas, which prompted Israel to drop bombs and blockade. Gaza Strip.
While the European Union strongly condemned the Hamas attack, the leaders tried to adhere to a similar message, with some emphasizing Israel's right to self-defense and others emphasizing concern for the people. Palestinian Civilization.
Ahead of the summit, EU countries discussed whether to call for a "humanitarian ceasefire", with some seeing the measure as important in providing aid to Gaza, while others said it Can determine Israel's ability to defend itself.
Diplomats said the EU appeared to be compromising on calls for a "humanitarian ceasefire" as it meant a short break in fighting for specific tasks such as releasing hostages or carrying convoys. Aid rather than a formal ceasefire.
While the European Union has had little influence in the conflict, officials have expressed concern that conflicts in the Middle East could have serious consequences for Europe, including rising inter-communal tensions and the influx of refugees. Attends the 5th ASEAN-Japan Smart Cities Network Summit and Continues to Meet with the Mayor of Tsukuba, Japan
