Articles and pictures by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, Preah Mayanurak, Kou Sopheap and many psychologists as guest speakers on World Mental Health Day tomorrow
The World Mental Health Day of the Royal University of Phnom Penh tomorrow morning will bring important events in the field of mental health to raise awareness of mental health issues in Cambodia, especially the mental health of young people.
Students and the public are invited to attend at any time throughout the morning of the program to hear expert presentations and video screenings on mental health, psychological education, poster presentations, yoga exercises, and mental problem solving exercises. By drawing or participating in some fun activities such as: Art therapy and gaining experience with face-to-face meetings in counseling.
It should be noted that there are three main causes of mental problems:
* First: Biological factors: Factors that are inherited, according to studies show that if the parents have mental health problems, the rate of children who can get mental health problems is up to 40% to 50%. % If in that family, both parents have mental health problems, children can face up to 70% mental health problems.
* Second: Psychological factors: is related to self-thinking and self-esteem, comparing yourself with others too much can also have psychological problems.
* Third: Social factors: related to activities and situations in society, sometimes due to stress in society, such as in a family full of violence, children will suffer from psychological problems. A young man accused a group of Kampong Leng district police of using violence against him, causing injuries, the district governor said to summon both parties for questioning
