General Meas Virith Instructs Officers to Strengthen Chemical Efficiency
(Phnom Penh): After its operation for 2 days from October 24-25, 2023, training course on strengthening the effectiveness of drug control for drug law enforcement officers in border provinces. Many companies and factories use chemical compounds, Customs and Excise of Cambodia, the border gates of the Autonomous Port were closed on the evening of October 25, 2023.
Lt. Gen. Uy Rat, Director of the Research and Inspection Department, reported on the good cooperation between the trainees and the trainers, making the training a success.
On that occasion, General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said that Cambodia is in a situation where it is suffering from the smuggling of chemicals to process synthetic drugs, which requires law enforcement officers to Continue to pay more attention to thorough inspection.
* First, the Customs and Excise Department, which is responsible for working in the border area, must check and verify all licenses, relevant documents and the amount of actual chemicals imported by companies, factories and enterprises.
* Second, to promote the regular exchange of information on the transit of chemicals across the border into the country among the relevant units or officials, especially between customs and excise officials working at the gates. Boundaries and provincial authorities that import companies, factories and enterprises use those chemicals.
* Third, to continue to strengthen and expand good cooperation between front line officers in the border areas, ports and relevant law enforcement officers to exchange information on the activities and directions of chemical transportation in Cambodia.
* Fourth, the relevant competent forces must enhance cooperation, monitor and control all companies, factories, enterprises using chemical compounds located in their territory.
* Fifth, all drug law enforcement officers must continue to pay attention to enhance the capacity building of additional knowledge and skills to serve the promotion of activities, monitoring, investigation, research, prevention and suppression of drug offenses and other crimes related to The drug is timely and highly effective.
Forest crime near Prey Lang in Stung Treng and Kratie provinces has been severely restricted
(Kratie-Stung Treng): The Ministry of Environment has tightened the Law on Protected Areas in the management of protected areas, natural resources and biodiversity conservation for sustainable development and for future generations.
In fact, in the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary, some of Cambodia's natural reserves, which are rich in natural resources, have also been carefully restricted by rangers in collaboration with relevant local authorities. All levels of the community and the people living near the protected areas are united in their commitment to prevent natural resource crime.
Regarding the protection of natural resources, Mr. Hul Soeung, Chief of Boeung Char Commune, Sambo District, Kratie Province, which is adjacent to the "Prey Lang" Wildlife Sanctuary, confirmed that in the past, park officials and his community like "mouth and teeth" are Collaborated to pay attention to the participation in protecting natural resources in the Prey Lang Nature Reserve.
The commune chief added that for his Boeung Char commune, there are more than 2,000 families, most of whom are engaged in agriculture, and some of them are benefiting from their work on plantations. Some of them continued to work in Phnom Penh.
In addition, Mr. Hul Soeung pointed out that for the people living in Boeung Char commune, they have their own land by adding other crops around the house.
Responding to this case, Mr. Sreng Chea Heng, Director of the Stung Treng Provincial Department of Environment, claimed that in the past, for Prey Lang geography, which is controlled by the Stung Treng Provincial Department of Environment, there was no crime of large-scale deforestation, but the activities of his people. For materials and small houses only.
The director of the Stung Treng Provincial Department of Environment confirmed that from today onwards, there are no exceptions for individuals who commit crimes against natural resources. The authorities will take action according to the procedure of the law sent to the court to the perpetrators.
According to Mr. Chhay Duong Savuth, Director of the Kratie Provincial Department of Environment, there is no information related to the theft of the Prey Lang entrance for timber export, and the false image of the road is the old road. "It has long been abandoned as park rangers from the provincial environment department, along with relevant authorities, have been working hard to patrol and enforce the most strict laws against natural resource offenders."
According to the director of the Kratie Provincial Department of Environment, the road from Prey Lang to SingbioTech is an old road that people use to find tar in the dry season, which can only be reached on foot and by motorbike.
Mr. Chhay Duong Savuth emphasized that after receiving the order of Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, which set out four measures, the rangers tried to enforce the law more effectively, they continued to patrol like rain. Rolim in protected areas under its jurisdiction.
Please be informed that Lang Wildlife Sanctuary is located in Kratie, Stung Treng, Kampong Thom and Preah Vihear provinces. According to Sub-Decree No. 181, dated July 17, 2023, "Prey Lang" Wildlife Sanctuary covers an area of 489,663.00 hectares.
Please be reminded that in order to effectively manage natural resources and conserve biodiversity and sustainable development, the Ministry of Environment has introduced four main measures, including:
First, the Ministry of Environment promotes the implementation of the law 100% and ends the culture of education, guidance and contracting and release of natural resource perpetrators.
Second, the Ministry of Environment cooperates closely with the Capital-Provincial Administrative Unity Command, especially with local authorities at all levels to prevent natural resource crime in protected areas.
Third, cooperate with the Anti-Corruption Unit and the National Gendarmerie Command to suppress and prevent natural resource crimes in addition to the cooperation with local authorities in the past.
And 4: Promote tree planting more than felling to maintain growth, especially the promotion of afforestation, which is a priority goal to increase forest cover by 60% by 2050 in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's Pentagon strategy and promote Community livelihoods, including sustainable biodiversity conservation.
