(Banteay Meanchey): Sadly, a man because he was too poor agreed to go into the forest to pick vegetables to cook on the Cambodian-Thai border, but unfortunately stepped on a landmine, causing serious injuries.
The incident happened at 2 pm on October 25, 2023 in the forest near the Cambodian-Thai border in Samaki village, Kork Romiet commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Colonel Long Samnang, Commander of the 807th Border Police, told reporters that the victim was 28-year-old John Chung, a resident of Samaki Village, Kouk Romiet Commune, Thmor Puok District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Colonel Long Samnang further stated that before the incident, the victim after lunch, the victim went into the forest to pick vegetables at the scene, especially to pick mushrooms and dig grapes, but unfortunately. Walking on landmines left over from the war erupted, causing amputation of his left leg.
In connection with this case, General To Sith Loh, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, appealed to the people living along the border who are looking for non-timber forest products not to enter the forest that is suspected of having mines or dangerous signs because it can lead to danger. Life or eventual injury.
Kandal Provincial Governor Inaugurates 1,000-Meter Concrete Road for Srah Po Village, Phnom Bat Commune, Ponhea Leu District
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, officially inaugurated the 1,000-meter-long, 6-meter-wide and 0.15-meter-thick concrete road for the residents of Srah Po village, Phnom Bat commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province.
This program was held on October 25, 2023. On that occasion, Mr. Kong Sophoan said that this is a great new achievement with many other achievements of Phnom Bat commune, Ponhea Leu district in the field of socio-economic Aesthetics, comfort, equity and environment in accordance with the pentagonal strategic policy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly under the leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
He instructed the district authorities to continue to build more achievements, strive to serve the people well, and all citizens together to maintain this achievement for a long time.
