(Phnom Penh): The Koh Pich bridge over Koh Nora has played an important role in reducing traffic congestion on National Road 1 and Norodom Boulevard. The bridge was opened to traffic on both sides on October 23, 2023.
The bridge cost $ 38,000,000 to build by the Cambodian Overseas Investment Company (OCIC). The construction of Koh Pich-Koh Nora bridge was started on October 26, 2020 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The bridge is 824 meters long and 24,506 meters wide, with four lanes, two lanes for cars, one lane for motorbikes and one lane for pedestrians.
