Mr. Kuong Lo said that meeting with people who are farming on the outskirts of Prey Lang now is very difficult because of the rainy season, the road is difficult to travel, some places can drive by car, some places to ride a bullock cart. And cross streams, canals, cut through the forest to reach. In particular, to visit people is to know their lives about the challenges of various diseases, especially malaria, because they go with their families, including children.
The director of the Department of Health has educated people living in malaria areas to take Pyramax anti-malarial drug once a day for three days a month, they can be protected from malaria for 28 days. . If they take medicine for 3 months, it can prevent malaria for up to 4 months (meaning take 3 months, take 1 month off. He said that this kind of medicine has no side effects for them, just do not take it. Alcohol for 3 days.
Kuong Lo claimed that the reason they were given the anti-malarial drug was because their farm was in the forest and there were so many malaria vectors here that they could be at risk of contracting the disease. Malaria.
