National Police Commissioner Supports Russian Federal Security Agency for Anti-Technology Training Program for Cambodian Police
(Phnom Penh): The National Police Commissioner General expressed his support for the request of the Russian Federal Security Agency to send Cambodian police to study a number of key skills to jointly prevent and combat technological crime in Cambodia and the ASEAN region.
The meeting was held between the National Police Commissioner General, His Excellency General Sar Thet, and the Head of the Regional Representative Office of the Russian Federal Security Agency, Mr. Sim Sovev Khengny, at the Ministry of Interior on the afternoon of October 25, 2023.
To begin with, the head of the regional representative office of the Russian Federal Security Agency, Sim Soveyev Keng Nhy, congratulated General Sar Thet on his appointment as King of the National Police.
The Russian Federal Security Agency intends to increase cooperation with the Cambodian National Police, especially the National Police Commission, and the Russian side will always welcome cooperation on enhancing technological skills in the fight against cybercrime. To the Cambodian police.
In response, the National Police Commissioner, General Sar Thet, expressed support for the request to assist Cambodia in training new techniques and skills for the Cambodian police, especially in the fight against cybercrime.
The National Police Commissioner General added that in the past, Cambodia has already sent the National Police to study various skills in Russia, and in the field of technology crime will continue to send the Cambodian police to receive more training.
Please be informed that Cambodia and Russia established the first diplomatic relations in 1956 and restored relations in 1979, and the Ministry of Internal Affairs of the Russian Federation became an ASEAN Nabul dialogue partner in 2014.
