Two Vietnamese arrested for cutting down flooded forest in Boribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, people request the authorities to increase protection of flooded forest
(Kampong Chhnang): Two Vietnamese nationals and three boats for towing flooded forest trees were arrested after the media and villagers found them stealing flooded forest in the protected area Tied up by a reserve boat and dropped into the river to catch fish and immediately reported to the competent authorities.
The case of cracking down on the crime of deforestation of flooded forest in the conservation area to be used as a catch for the above fish occurred at 8:00 pm on October 24, 2023 at Prek Thlan (a conservation canal) Fish species) is located in Damnak Reach village, Kampong Preah Koki commune, Boribo district.
Tat Sihak, Director of Kampong Chhnang Fisheries Administration, said this morning, October 25, after receiving reports from the media and the people, his Fisheries Administration Force immediately arrived at the scene. He arrested two Vietnamese offenders and three boats for towing flooded trees. The two perpetrators are:
The exhibits confiscated by the police at the time of the crime include: 3 boats, 2 of which were wooden boats and 1 a barge, along with 15 large trees that were cut down in the conservation area and tied to the boat. , From a 30-liter water tank without a lot of water, which is used to tie a floating tree trunk to make it easier to tow water, and many ropes are used to tie a tree.
Mr. Tat Sihak, Director of Fisheries Administration of Kampong Chhnang, said that the two perpetrators were charged under Article 98, point 1 of the Fisheries Law, which is punishable by 3 to 5 years in prison, and the exhibits were confiscated. State property for the case and the two suspects will be sent to court today as well.
According to the villagers, this month is the season when some fishermen need to fish in the river to catch fish for three or four months, then they will be surrounded by nets to catch fish. As for Samras, most of them cut down the flooded forest and put it together as Samras.
