(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, this morning, October 25, 2023, signed an agreement to form an alliance between the Cambodian People's Party and 27 other political parties in Cambodia. The ceremony took place at the 7 January Palace, the headquarters of the Cambodian People's Party.
Cooperation agreement between all political parties with 28 participating parties with 8 points:
1. Strengthen good cooperation with equality, equal rights, respect for the independence and autonomy of each party for the benefit of the nation and the people of Cambodia.
2. Commitment to uphold the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, defend the monarchy based on the Constitution, promote liberal democracy, pluralism, guarantee human rights, respect for law and social justice, and strengthen national unity to build an independent, peaceful, free, democratic, neutral and progressive Cambodia. Society in accordance with the motto of the nation, religion, king.
3. Commitment to protect the independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity of the Kingdom of Cambodia to protect peace, political stability and security, social order to ensure the process of sustainable socio-economic development and improve the lives of all people in harmony in society.
4: Collaborate to prevent and eliminate extremist politics from the Kingdom of Cambodia. Absolutely oppose the tactics and actions of any medium that seeks to destroy national unity, destabilize society, destroy democracy, and attempt to bring about any change that is unconstitutional and unconstitutional.
5. Good cooperation to ensure that the election process in accordance with the principles of liberal, multi-party democracy, both nationally and sub-nationally, both globally and globally, is conducted in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution and the laws in force. Free, accurate, fair and secure.
6. Honestly implement and take the national interest as the principle of alliance and cooperation, support each other, do not oppose each other in any way, including not campaigning against each other during the election campaign and not ally with any political party or Any political group that opposes a partner in its alliance.
7. Build and strengthen cooperation to implement to achieve good results in the content of this agreement. In case of problems, a representative shall be assigned to meet and discuss and resolve the issue peacefully.
8. Open to other legitimate political parties that support and wish to join the cooperation and alliance between political parties in Cambodia in the spirit of this agreement. This Agreement is effective from the date of signing.
Key Remarks by Samdech Maniphea Hun Manet on the Occasion of Meeting with More Than 120,000 Workers in Kampong Cham Province
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 25, 2023, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, met with approximately 12,060 workers at 14 factories based in Prey Chhor and Kampong Siem districts. Kampong Cham Province.
These 14 factories are 7 garment factories, 5 shoe factories, 1 garment printing factory and 1 textile factory. This is the sixth time that His Excellency Hun Manet has met with workers in various factories and enterprises as the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia after the Royal Government of the seventh mandate was formed in August 2023.
