NEC Holds a Maintenance Course on the Importance of Elections to Political Parties, Non-Governmental Organizations, Deputy Directors, Youth Schools and Relevant Authorities in Keo Seima District, Mondulkiri Province
(Mondulkiri): The National Election Committee (NEC) on October 25, 2023 organized an educational, dissemination and awareness raising session on the importance of elections to political parties, non-governmental organizations, directors and directors. Deputy Youth School and relevant authorities in Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province.
The course was led by the Voter Training and Education Department of the General Department of Education, Information and Public Relations of the General Secretariat of the NEC in collaboration with the Mondulkiri Provincial Election Secretariat under the chairmanship of Mr. Sum Bunhong, Director General of the General Department of Education, Information and Public Relations. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen affirms that the spirit of the coalition agreement between the CPP and the 27 parties is open to other parties to join this alliance (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, on the morning of October 25. This 2023 states that the spirit of the alliance agreement between the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) and 27 other Cambodian political parties is open to other legitimate political parties to join the alliance.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen affirmed this on the occasion that Samdech invited to sign the alliance agreement between the Cambodian People's Party and 27 other political parties in Cambodia. The ceremony took place at the 7 January Palace, the headquarters of the Cambodian People's Party this morning, October 25, 2023.
He stressed that this agreement will be open to other legitimate political parties that support and wish to participate in allied cooperation between political parties in Cambodia in the spirit of this agreement. And the decision to allow other parties to join or not to join will not be decided by the CPP alone, there must be a compromise by choosing a consensus or 50 plus one or two-thirds majority.
After signing this agreement, Samdech Techo introduced the preparation of another internal order. The CPP will send the chairman of the party's organizing committee to draft the rules and regulations, and ask the parties to send their representatives to participate in the preparation of the rules.
The rules of procedure will include meetings, meeting locations and meeting times.
This statement was made by Samdech Techo President during the signing ceremony of the alliance agreement between the Cambodian People's Party and 27 other political parties in Cambodia at the 7 January Palace, the headquarters of the Cambodian People's Party on the morning of the 25th. October 2023.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all political parties are equal partners, equal rights and not under the CPP, but all political parties are willing to cooperate with each other to The common interest for the Cambodian nation, even if the CPP is leading the country.
Samdech Techo said, "The CPP, although it has a lot of human resources and financial resources, but the CPP does not look at other parties as an unequal party as its partner, despite the form. "Whoever has any resources."
It should be noted that in the agreement signed with the 28 political parties, there are points that require the protection of constitutional populism, because in recent years, opposition groups have abused and insulted the King, including demanding The king abdicated and so on.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the interpretation of some opposition groups and foreigners to violate the reality of the Paris Agreement, now Cambodia only respects the Constitution (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party on October 25, 2023 This statement considers the interpretation of some opposition groups and foreigners regarding the Paris Agreement of October 23 is a violation of the practical aspects of the Paris Agreement.
Samdech stated that people who misinterpret the truth of the Paris Agreement do not know the history of this agreement, but consider themselves experts in interpretation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that now is not the time to implement the Paris Agreement, now is the time to abide by the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, because all inputs have already been gathered into the Constitution.
Samdech warned the opposition that the desire to take the Paris Agreement to suppress the Constitution is not possible, must study the Paris Agreement carefully.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks during the signing ceremony of the alliance agreement between the Cambodian People's Party and 27 other political parties on the morning of October 25, 2023 at the 7 Makara Palace.
"What is ridiculous and not ridiculous is that on October 22-23, the 32nd anniversary of the Paris Agreement, I do not understand what human interpretation is," he said. "Some of the Paris Agreement, even where the history of the Paris Agreement came from, is unknown, but he is a great expert on the interpretation of the Paris Agreement."
"I do not look down on anyone, but what I want is to respect the truth of the history that has gone through," he said. "Some foreigners are also misinterpreting. At this time, Cambodia only respects the constitution, the spirit of the Paris Agreement is respected, but it has already entered into the Cambodian constitution and laws."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that no one wants to forget what they have achieved for the Paris Agreement. Paris, and then without Samdech's decision from Phnom Penh, the Paris Agreement would not have been possible.
Please be reminded that some of the historical events of Samdech Tramram's negotiations led to the Paris Agreement of October 23, 1991, which had four signatories: Samdech Techo Hun Sen representing the Cambodian government, the FUNCINPEC movement represented by Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh, National Front for the Liberation of the Khmer People, represented by Ta Son San, and the Democratic Kampuchea Movement (Pol Pot), represented by Khieu Samphan.
This historic agreement has three main objectives: First, to restore peace in Cambodia through the implementation of a ceasefire and disarmament of the four Cambodian conflicting parties. The foundation of democracy in Cambodia through the holding of elections to the Constituent Assembly; and third, to protect the sovereignty, independence, integrity and inviolability of the territory, neutrality and national unity of Cambodia.
The agreement has become the subject of opposition groups attacking the Cambodian government, accusing it of violating the spirit of the Paris Agreement. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered that those people were expressing their opinions incorrectly and were not in the same situation as Samdech.
