(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan will provide a grant from the Government of Japan amounting to 1.338 million yen (approximately US $ 9.7 million) to implement a project for the construction of a permanent satellite measuring station network throughout Cambodia.
The signing ceremony of the grant will be held on October 26, 2023 by Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Inter-Cambodian Cooperation and Mr. UENO Atsushi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Foreign.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the purpose of this project is to accelerate the cadastral survey and strengthen administrative services related to land registration through the installation of permanent satellite measuring stations to contribute to the promotion of the project. Infrastructure.
The ministry added that this generous gesture demonstrates Japan's unwavering commitment to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's ongoing efforts to promote economic and social development. The assistance contributes to expanding cooperation in all fields and strengthening the "comprehensive strategic partnership" between the two countries, which is celebrating the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations.
Spain seizes nearly $ 64 million worth of antique gold jewelry stolen from Ukraine
MADRID (Reuters) - Spain has seized 60 million euros ($ 63.6 million) worth of gold artifacts stolen from Ukraine after police arrested a group of thieves trying to sell them, police said on Monday. In Madrid. This is according to the release by Reuters on Tuesday, October 24, 2023.
Police say the 11 items, mostly jewelry such as necklaces, bracelets and earrings, date back to the Greek period between the 8th and 4th centuries BC. The artifacts were forged to appear to belong to the Ukrainian Orthodox Church.
Three Spaniards and two Ukrainians have been arrested in an investigation that began in 2021 after a piece of gold headband with a sheep's head was put up for sale at a private sale in Madrid.
Plan International Cambodia, in collaboration with the Ministry of Education and relevant partners, organizes a workshop to disseminate documents supporting the implementation of the "Child Friendly School Program"
(Phnom Penh): On October 24, 2023, Plan International Cambodia, in collaboration with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Children's Rights Fund and relevant partners, organized a national outreach school on supporting documents for the implementation of the "Child Friendly School Program" focusing on Implementing a safe school framework.
Through this collaboration, Prudential plays an active role in making a positive impact on the lives of Cambodian children by ensuring their safety and making them thrive in a safe educational environment. By implementing school safety guidelines in schools, the aim is to encourage teachers, parents and community members to pay attention and focus on the well-being of children and prevent risks and dangers.
With support from the Prudential Foundation through Plan International Hong Kong, Plan International Cambodia has been implementing the “Promoting School Safety Initiative in Cambodia” project since 2016 with the aim of supporting children living in vulnerable communities. Disaster in Cambodia to adapt to disasters and have a safe learning environment through the support of the Royal Government.
He added that we have received funding from the Prudential Foundation to implement the Phase 3 School Safety Initiative in Cambodia, which builds on the achievements of the first and second phases and sets out a contextual and effective model for school safety from the target schools. 60 schools in Stung Treng to 36 new schools in Siem Reap and Ratanakiri. This project will strategically address gaps and key challenges that arose in the implementation of the previous sections.
In addition, this guideline has been adopted and is being implemented by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to address emerging and inclusive disasters in the field of education. In addition, this document has three main purposes:
* Protect students, educators and staff from death, injury, violence and harm to schools and other educational institutions.
* Develop a plan for continuing education for prevention and reduction of disruptions to children's learning in order to adapt to all kinds of trauma, stress, danger and threats. * Improve the knowledge and skills of students and staff, contribute to risk reduction, resilience and sustainable development.
