(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has set out major measures in collaboration with relevant ministries and institutions and authorities at all levels to effectively manage natural resources to ensure 60% increase in forest cover by 2050.
In fact, on October 24, 2023, Mr. Chea Sam Ang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, chaired a meeting to strengthen natural resource management in Kratie province. The meeting was attended by Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, leaders and officials of the Ministry of Environment, Department of Environment, relevant departments, HE Prosecutors of the Provincial Court, relevant district governors and park rangers.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Sam Ang mentioned the establishment of various mechanisms to ensure the sustainable protection and conservation of natural resources through the implementation of four measures to prevent natural resource crimes set by the Minister. Ministry of Environment.
Please be reminded that in order to effectively manage natural resources and conserve biodiversity and sustainable development, the Ministry of Environment has introduced four main measures, including:
1) The Ministry of Environment promotes the implementation of the law 100% and ends the culture of education, guidance and contracting and release of natural resource perpetrators.
2) The Ministry of Environment cooperates closely with the Capital-Provincial Administrative Unity Command, especially with local authorities at all levels to prevent natural resource crime in protected areas.
3) Cooperate with the Anti-Corruption Unit and the National Gendarmerie Command to suppress and prevent natural resource crimes in addition to the cooperation with local authorities in the past.
4) Promote the planting of trees more than cutting to maintain growth, especially the promotion of reforestation, which is a priority direction to increase forest cover to 60% by 2050 in accordance with the Pentagon strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia and improve livelihoods People in communities, including sustainable biodiversity conservation.
Through this, the Ministry of Environment has launched a campaign on October 10 to provide and plant at least 1 million trees per year from 2024. This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen signs an alliance agreement between the Cambodian People's Party and 27 other political parties
