* Second: At the time of trial, the four evils must be avoided: will, will, punishment, delusion, and delusion, and must adhere to the five virtues: morality, justice, integrity, justice, morality, and wisdom.
* Third: To continue to strengthen the capacity of subordinates and relevant law enforcement officers by all means, prepare the composition of officers to receive further training, and all officials in the field of justice must also strengthen their capacity on a regular basis.
* Fourth: To improve the quality of the preparation of the verdict / judgment by having a clear and reasonable and fair and just law in accordance with the law in force, and also request the competent authorities to cooperate to ensure that the court's decision is correct. Fully and effectively implemented.
* Fifth: Adhere to the five noble approaches of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: "Mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, healing and surgery" and the approach related to the four reforms of the Prime Minister: "Clear vision, commitment Highly participate with honesty and dedication "in the performance of its functions and duties, especially all preparations to participate in the implementation of the three main campaigns that will be launched by the Ministry of Justice in the near future.
