Please be informed that the Health Equity Fund refers to the social health protection financing mechanism to enable the target population to access or use free health care services at public health facilities, with the Royal Government in charge.
The fund was piloted in 2000, then continued to cover poor households with equity in 2015 and a series of target groups. The Health Equity Fund extends its reach to vulnerable families, which was officially launched by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia on October 24, 2023.
