The Constitutional Council unanimously decided that the law on the establishment of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation "unconstitutional"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, October 24, 2023, the Constitutional Council held a plenary meeting chaired by Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, to review and decide on the request of the National Assembly President Khuon Sodary. Examine the constitutionality of the Law on the Establishment of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation.
As a result of this meeting, the Constitutional Council unanimously decided that "the law on the establishment of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation was declared unconstitutional", according to a statement from the Constitutional Council.
The Law on the Establishment of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation was approved by the National Assembly on October 9, 2023 at the 1st Session of the 7th Legislature and the Senate reviewed and gave unanimous opinion on the form and concept of the law without amendment at the 11th session. The fourth legislature on October 17, 2023.
With the direct support and guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodian Civil Aviation has developed like neighboring countries and the region in terms of infrastructure and air transport with safety, security and confidence to all types of travelers. And economic, especially the protection of the air integrity of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Law on the Establishment of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation was drafted with 11 articles and was approved by the Plenary Session of the Council of Ministers on September 20, 2023.
