(Phnom Penh): In the morning of Tuesday, October 24, 2023, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the inauguration ceremony of "National Techo Santepheap Hospital" and announced the official implementation of the program. The first of the six priority policies is to "expand the scope of equity funds for vulnerable families."
With the official inauguration of the "Techo Santepheap National Hospital", a major achievement of the Cambodian health sector, Samdech Mani will also announce the official implementation of the first program of the six priority policies. The first phase of the pentagonal strategy of the government of the seventh mandate. The first priority is to expand health care services towards global health coverage.
The six priority policies of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate have been implemented immediately to help the poor and the truly affected people, including:
First, expand health care services towards universal health coverage, that is, when there is an illness, civil servants, the armed forces and the people, especially the poor and vulnerable, must have access to health care services for everyone.
Second, young people who are the children of the poor and vulnerable will receive vocational training so that they can easily earn a living. This training is free of charge and even sponsored during the additional training.
Third, the poor and vulnerable people will receive warmth through the National Social Assistance Program, which will be strengthened into a strong national program, that is, when people face crises or other risks, the National Social Assistance Program will wait. Remember to help them effectively.
Fourth, informal workers will receive attention and they can also receive the same benefits as system workers when they face crises or other risks.
Fifth, farmers will receive protection through the establishment of coordination mechanisms and financing programs (lending for agricultural activities), in particular, to obtain appropriate protection of agricultural prices without losing farmers. No.
Sixth, the Royal Government will send agricultural technical officers to help farmers in all communes where people are engaged in agriculture and establish farmers' communities throughout the country to protect the interests of farmers.
