32nd anniversary of the October 23 peace agreement! Students, young researchers believe that peaceful negotiations for the reconciliation of the Khmer nation, one cause, one development for the nation in all fields
Young students and researchers believe that the Paris Peace Treaty has two parts: first: the end of all wars in Cambodia and the withdrawal of troops from Cambodian territory, and second: the restoration of democracy, human rights, development, and the establishment of elections. Globally, the country is now at peace, especially the content of some treaties has been incorporated into the constitution and some laws to continue to lead the treaty in accordance with the treaty and develop.
At the same time, a group of students and young researchers would like to pay tribute to the heroism of the great Khmer people, Samdech Preah Bat Preah Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, initiated with the aim of seeking peace, leaving more than 500 wars and chronic conflicts. Year to the motherland and the nation as a whole, at that time, 18 governments have signed the peace agreement, plus four other Cambodian parties.
Through this agreement, it was also possible to continue to hide and lead Cambodia through peaceful negotiations to unite and reconcile the nation from a multilateral split into a single one in the spirit of "one Khmer, one cause, one opportunity and one fundamental foundation." Important for the restoration and development of the nation to grow in all areas. "No war can end with the use of weapons, but war can end with negotiations for peace."
The young researchers praised the Royal Government of Cambodia for maintaining the implementation of the Paris Peace Accords and incorporated a number of principles into the national rule of law to ensure effective implementation. To date, the country has developed in all fields. Spokesman of the General Commission: 426 vehicles were inspected and fined on October 23, 2023
