The book "Samdech Techo Hun Sen, The Drawer of Cambodia's Destiny" was written by Mr. Keo Ba Phnom, Chairman of the CPP Historical Research Committee and Minister of Delegation to the Prime Minister, and published in 2022 with 601 pages.
In the past, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has leaked that secrets in the life of Samdech's national leadership, as well as about 70 to 80 percent of politics that no one ever knew, will be revealed through this book. Samdech also recommended the publication of 50,000 copies of this book and arrange for an English translation for foreign friends to know.
According to Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia, the English translation has four main factors, including:
First, because this book is the most important historical document, especially related to the life and politics of Samdech Techo himself, as well as the history of Cambodia. As a matter of history, Cambodia and the future destiny of the entire nation after the Khmer Republic is deeply connected with the life of Samdech Techo.
Second, from the time of the Prince from 1977 until there was complete peace, prosperity and development, this is a very important historical turning point that needs to be widely disseminated among national and international readers.
Fourthly, in the past, some foreigners did not understand how Cambodia miserably revived the genocidal regime and how it tried to build peace and how Cambodia developed the nation and how Cambodia came to be. Both its current position.
This book provides enough information for foreign readers to find out about Samdech Techo Hun Sen in particular and Cambodia in general, as well as the regional and global political context.
