(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has decided to appoint Mr. Ouk Seiha as an advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party.
The appointment was made on October 20, 2023. The appointment of Mr. Ouk Seiha as an advisor to Samdech Techo is an opportunity for him to contribute to accompany Samdech Techo in serving the Cambodian People's Party to stand strong in the battle for democracy in Cambodia.
Please note that Mr. Ouk Seiha is a loyal descendant who has served Samdech Techo Hun Sen since 1978. Especially at a time when Cambodia was struggling to resist the return of Khmer Rouge forces, Ouk Seiha was a sharp commander fighting against Khmer Rouge forces.
Ouk Seiha used to work as a river base commander and later as a marine base commander. He is a fighter who has built and left many achievements in the field of defense. In particular, on the protection of Cambodia's territorial integrity and territorial waters.
Despite stepping down from maritime management, Ouk Seiha was entrusted by the Royal Government led by Samdech Manipur Hun Manet to the King to appoint him Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of National Defense to contribute to the national service. The defense sector continues.
On October 24, the Constitutional Council will review the constitutionality of the Law on the Establishment of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On October 24, 2023, tomorrow, the Constitutional Council will hold a meeting to review the Constitution on the Law Establish a Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation. The meeting will be chaired by Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council.
The Kingdom of Cambodia first established a civil aviation office in 1955 and became a member of the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) in 1956. After a series of developments, the Civil Aviation Authority was renamed the Civil Aviation Authority, established in 1993.
