China's largest tire maker announces possibility of opening tire factory in Cambodia
After completing the mission to accompany Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to attend the "Belt and Road" forum, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol has not yet returned to Cambodia. The Deputy Prime Minister is continuing to visit major Chinese companies to persuade and encourage them to invest in Cambodia.
During the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister mentioned the steel relationship between Cambodia and China, which this year marks the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries. In order to encourage companies to invest in Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol highlighted Cambodia's economic growth over the past 20 years, which averaged 7% annually under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. There was an outbreak of Kovid 19 disease.
After listening to the explanation of the Deputy Prime Minister, the Deputy Director of the company expressed his satisfaction with the rapid growth of the Cambodian economy, especially the construction of many physical infrastructure to support the development of Cambodian society. Seeing the overall progress of Cambodia and responding to the encouragement of the Deputy Prime Minister, the company decided to study in detail to establish a tire factory in Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol warmly welcomed the intention to select Cambodia to invest in the construction of a tire factory. The Deputy Prime Minister announced to facilitate the study of the company so that the company can start investing in the construction of factories and tire production in Cambodia as soon as possible.
Please note that there is currently a large Chinese company is in the process of manufacturing tires in Cambodia. The factory is running their production chain in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
More than 400 houses in Takhmao city were flooded by Stung Prek Tnaot, Kandal provincial leaders inspected the situation and visited the affected families
(Kandal): Mr. Hak Sok Makara, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province and First Vice Chairman of the Party Working Group for Sangkat Takdol, Takhmao City, and the Working Group visited 404 families in Prek Long Village, Sangkat Takdol, Takhmao City. Accident due to rain on the afternoon of October 22, 2023. The floodwaters flowed from the side of Phnom Penh through a 60-meter canal and flooded into this location.
On the occasion of this visit, Mr. Hak Sok Makara sent a message from Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, who is always concerned about the well-being of the people when they are in trouble, regardless of political affiliation.
He instructed the people to be very careful about living, especially to be careful of all kinds of poisonous animals, electricity and hygiene, live clean, eat clean, drink clean, protect small children, especially fear of drowning or other diseases. If you feel unwell, please be sure to go to Takhmao Victory Department immediately for free treatment.
Mr. Hak Sok Makara told the people that if they have a difficult life and want to go to a safe place, he will provide a suitable place to stay in a safe place above the village for the comfort of the people and please immediately report to the authorities if there is Ask for something.
Please be informed that if the flood does not decrease, the Kandal Provincial Authority will arrange a safe place to help people to stay temporarily, as well as the supply of food, medicine to meet the needs of people. Appropriately until the floodwaters recede.
The leaders of Kandal province, especially Mr. Hak Sok Makara and Mr. Kong Sophoan, the provincial governor, always consider and care about the well-being of the people, no matter in Takhmao city or any location, as long as there are difficulties, there is always a class Lead the province to help in time so far and move forward.
