General Commissioner of the National Police presents the results of General Sar Thet's participation in the 41st ASEAN Napole Conference in Laos
(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police presented the results of the 41st ASEAN Napoleonic Conference of General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police in Vientiane, Lao PDR, from October 16 to 20. 2023.
After receiving permission from His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and His Excellency Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, led a high-level delegation of the National Police Commission to attend the conference. The 41st ASEAN Napoleo will be held from October 16-20, 2023. The conference was held under the theme "Strengthening Partnerships to Promote Peace, Stability and Security."
On October 17, 2023, the 41st ASEAN Napoleonic Conference was officially opened under the chairmanship of General Villalak Khafong, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Public Security of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, accompanied by the Heads of Delegation of ASEAN Member States. Discussion partners and observers, representatives of ambassadors, ambassadors of ASEAN member countries to Laos and a total of 336 distinguished guests.
In the busy mission of attending the 41st ASEAN Napoleonic Conference and in the spirit of enhancing relations with regional and international cooperation partners, General Sar Thet met with the heads of delegations of countries and institutions such as the National Agency. Japanese Police, Australian Federal Police, Lao Police Force, United Kingdom National Crime Agency (NCA).
On the morning of October 19, 2023, General Sar Thet, Head of the Delegation of the General Commission of the National Police of Cambodia, together with the Chiefs of the National Police Delegates of the Member States and the Executive Directors of the ASEAN-Napole Secretariat, were paid a courtesy call and Report to Sonexay Siphandone, Prime Minister of the Lao People's Democratic Republic.
After reviewing the contents of the report on the themes of each Commission, the Heads of Delegation of the Member States unanimously agreed to include the main contents in the draft Joint Statement of the 41st ASEAN-Napole Conference as a basis. For the professional team, continue to practice in the next year.
The Heads of Delegation of the ASEAN Member States have officially signed the Joint Statement of the 41st ASEAN-Napol Conference to document the joint commitment to prevent and combat all types of transnational crime. The theme of "Strengthening Partnerships to Promote Peace, Stability and Security" and the vision of the ASEAN Police is "Together to Secure ASEAN".
Following the program, the 41st ASEAN Napole Conference was officially closed under the chairmanship of Major General Kham King Phulam Monivong, Deputy Minister of Public Security of Laos and Chief of the Lao Police Force. The Myanmar Police Force, which will host the 42nd ASEAN Napole Conference in 2024.
After completing a four-day mission in Vientiane, Lao People's Democratic Republic on October 20, 2023, General Sar Thet led the delegation to return home safely and bring honor and achievement. Bilateral and international cooperation to the General Commission of the National Police and the Ministry of Interior.
