(Phnom Penh): Economists and social media users have responded to criticisms of the difficulty of spending dollars on substandard dollars, stating that it is a critique without clear consideration and suggestions to encourage consumption. Riel instead.
As of the morning of October 22, this post has been shared more than 1,900 times, 569 likes and 347 comments. This statement has received some support, but at the same time, most people who use social media say that this is an unreasonable criticism, not based on consideration and without nationalism.
Mr. Sok Roeun, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Microfinance Association (CMA), said that the solution to the above problem should explain and encourage foreign tourists to exchange the riel and spend the riel, which is the national currency of Cambodia. He said that in general, the reception of the US dollar is more restrictive than the national currency because the US dollar banknote is not printed in Cambodia.
He said: "That is why banks and microfinance institutions in our country always promote and encourage people as well as tourists to use the riel banknotes widely, because no matter how old the banknote is torn or dirty. "They are still accepted because our riel banknotes are printed and controlled in our country."
The US dollar circulated in Cambodia along with the riel The riel was officially re-introduced on March 20, 1980, after the fall of the Pol Pot regime, but due to the prolongation of the civil war until the end of 1998. Confidence in the riel is still low.
In 1992-1993, large amounts of US dollars flowed into the Cambodian economy through the United Nations Transitional Authority in Cambodia (UNTAC) to hold the first general elections and to bring the people as well as the private sector into consideration. Quickly take and use US dollars directly.
Dollarization in Cambodia also started from then until now. Many Cambodians have become accustomed to the use of the dollar, although the Royal Government and the National Bank of Cambodia have consistently worked to improve and sustain the use of the riel, as well as improve the quality and aesthetics of the riel.
Not only that, the branches of the National Bank of Cambodia in the provinces always try to promote the use of the riel by meeting the needs of the riel at the local level and accept the exchange of old riel banknotes torn free of charge.
Data from the National Bank of Cambodia shows that the use of the riel in the economy has increased significantly from about 563 billion riel in 1998 to 31 trillion riel today, an increase of 19.2% on average. One year. However, as the Cambodian economy grows, the proportion of the use of the riel in economic activities is not large enough.
While the National Bank of Cambodia has maintained a stable riel and improved the quality and aesthetics of the riel, social media users and economists have argued that the Cambodian public should use the riel more widely and encourage tourism. Foreigners spend in riel in Cambodia.
