(Phnom Penh): Mango is one of Cambodia's potential agro-industrial crops that the Royal Government has been promoting exports to international markets, especially to China, and is increasing its market share and capturing new markets.
Cambodia started exporting fresh mangoes to China for the first time in 2021 after a protocol on phytosanitary requirements for exporting Cambodian fresh mangoes to China was signed in June 2020 between the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development. General Administration of Customs of China (GACC).
Exporting fresh mangoes to the Chinese market is a valuable opportunity for Cambodian mango farmers.
In order to expand the export market of fresh mangoes to the Chinese market, the General Department of Agriculture has outlined four steps to invest in mango cultivation and export, especially new exporters.
* Step 1 - Registration of mango growers and packaging locations with the General Department of Agriculture:
Step 2: Certification and Standards: Fresh mangoes can be exported to China only after quality control and phytosanitary certification from the Department of Crop Protection, Sanitation and Hygiene, General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture.
At the same time, China also needs proof to verify that there are no products with contaminants, and that they will need other information about the product, such as steam treatment or hot water treatment before export. Exporters must provide additional documentation to clarify this issue, requiring differences from one product to another.
It takes 10 to 120 hours to obtain a phytosanitary certificate from the Department of Crop Protection, Sanitation and Hygiene of the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
Another important point is that exporters must have a certificate of origin, which is an important document used in international trade to prove that goods made in Cambodia are exported. For this letter, the exporter applies to the Ministry of Commerce. A certificate of origin must be signed by the exporter and the Ministry of Commerce.
* Step 4 - Mango delivery and payment
Products targeted for the export market require rigid packaging, and products shipped by air require special packaging, package sizes, and insulation. The packaging must present and provide useful information about the product. First, the information to be provided includes product name, brand, size, seed classification, weight, unit number, grower, shipper, and country of manufacture.
Currently, direct shipping routes from Cambodia to China are limited, Cambodia does not have a border with China, and as a result, Cambodia has to rely on the port of Ho Chi Minh City as its fruit transport hub to China. .
The four main routes for transporting fresh mangoes to China are by land, sea, river and air. Prices for transportation through these four routes vary greatly. The four shipping options and routes are as follows:
Shipping by sea: From Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville-Shanghai. Currently, this route takes 14 days and requires stopping at another port on the way.
Please be informed that currently the total area for mango plantation in Cambodia is more than 124.3 thousand hectares. Annual production volume reaches 1.44 million tons. Thirty-seven plantations officially recognized by China's General Administration of Customs and five packaging factories, including two steam-spraying mango processing plants and three hot water-spraying plants, are also growing. Quickly, new processing facilities are being set up.
