(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophorn, Governor of Kandal Province and Chairman of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, on the evening of October 20, 2023, led the relevant departments of Kandal Stung and Takhmao District Authorities and all kinds of armed forces to inspect the flood situation. Rainfall at Dam 7 Makara and Canal 96.
The provincial governor instructed all municipal and district authorities to make clear plans to prepare for possible floods in the future, he said: "Because this is very important if we do not "If we take precautionary measures, we will face many problems and difficulties in our locality, so as the authorities do, we must have a clear plan to deal with it in a timely manner."
Mr. Kong Sophoan added that the main issue that all municipal authorities need to pay attention to the flood is the provision of safe places for the affected people, temporary accommodation and for animals to have clean water. For use, be prepared by a doctor to help them when they have a health problem, and another major problem is to be prepared to save food and other supplies.
In addition, the provincial governor reminded and urged all district authorities to expedite the provision of challenge data and report regularly on the flood situation to the provincial administration to take timely action.
On that occasion, the Governor of Kandal Province also called on the people to continue to be very careful about the safety of their families, especially young children, to be prepared for floods and to take care of their health through eating. Clean, drink clean and live clean.
