(Kampong Speu): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, accompanied by the technical officers of the Ministry and the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Speu Province, on October 21, 2023, inspected the water condition in Stung Prek Tnaot delta. Kampong Speu Province.
Minister Thor Chetha inspected the water condition of Stung Prek Tnaot in a number of large reservoirs, such as Peam Khlai station in Tum Pum Meas commune, Rolaing Chrey sluice gate in Kaheng commune, Samrong Tong district, Ta Sal dam sluice gate in Ta Sal commune, Oral district. Kampong Speu Province and 7 Makara Dam in Kandal Province.
According to the Minister, the water level of Stung Prek Tont in the upper part of Kampong Speu province is gradually decreasing as of 11:00 am today, Peam Khlai Tuek station is 5.35 meters high and 7.50 meters above the alert level. The construction of the sluice gate is 7.68 meters high with a height of 7.50 meters, while five sluice gates are 1 meter high.
The Minister confirmed that all the sluice gates of the Tasal Dam were completely closed, the water level was 19.15 meters, and the alert height was 19.50 meters.
The minister said that according to the forecast, the water level in the upper part will start to decrease, which will take 12 to 36 hours for the lower part to start to decrease. Under this situation, in a few days, the water of Stung Prek Tnaot will return to normal.
At the same time, the Minister also instructed all leaders and technical officials, especially the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to cooperate with local authorities to continue to monitor carefully and with the highest responsibility.
