Ministry of Environment does not exempt natural resource crimes to ensure the effectiveness of environmental protection and natural resource management
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has set out absolute and clear measures to protect natural resources. In the seventh term of the Royal Government, Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, has set out to enforce the law without exception for natural resource perpetrators to ensure the effectiveness of environmental protection and natural resource management.
In fact, on October 19, 2023, the culture of education, guidance and contracting and release of perpetrators in protected areas was governed by the Law on Protected Areas. Pursat Provincial Court has issued a temporary detention order for a person who encroached on forest land to take ownership of the land.
The implementation of the Law on Protected Areas, which Article 62, point 1, stipulates that those who commit the act of clearing, encroaching on forest land, clearing, burning and clearing forest land for land ownership shall be punished with imprisonment from one to five years and A fine of 15 million to 150 million riels. Anyone who conspires or facilitates the commission of a crime shall be punished as a perpetrator.
It should be noted that in order to effectively manage natural resources and conserve biodiversity and sustainable development, the Ministry of Environment has introduced four main measures, including:
First, the Ministry of Environment promotes 100% law enforcement and ends the culture of education, guidance and contracting and release of natural resource perpetrators.
Second, the Ministry of Environment cooperates closely with the Capital-Provincial Administrative Unity Command, especially with local authorities at all levels to prevent natural resource crime in protected areas.
Third, cooperate with the Anti-Corruption Unit and the National Gendarmerie Command to suppress and prevent natural resource crimes in addition to the cooperation with local authorities that have been implemented so far.
And 4: Promoting tree planting more than felling to maintain growth, especially the promotion of afforestation, which is a priority direction to increase forest cover by 60% by 2050 in accordance with the Pentagon strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia and promote Community livelihoods, including sustainable biodiversity conservation.
Through this, the Ministry of Environment has launched a campaign on October 10 to provide and plant at least 1 million trees per year from 2024. The Ministry of Water Resources confirms the water level situation at various hydrological stations in Cambodia on October 21!
