International Analysis: Why Egypt and Other Arab Countries Do Not Want to Accept Palestinian Refugees?
As Palestinians in the Gaza Strip seek refuge and escape the relentless Israeli bombing campaign in retaliation for the October 7 attack on Hamas, there are serious questions. An important question is why Egypt and other Arab countries in the region, such as Jordan, refuse to accept Palestinian refugees?
Concerns about Hamas At the same time, Egypt says a large-scale expulsion of Palestinians from Gaza could open the door for Hamas or other Palestinian militants to enter its territory. If this happens, instability could erupt in the Sinai Peninsula, where the Egyptian military has been fighting for years to crush militants accused by Egypt of backing Hamas.
Egypt has supported Israel's blockade of the Gaza Strip since Hamas took control of the Gaza Strip in 2007 and tightened border controls. Egypt has also destroyed a network of subways under the border area used by Hamas and other Palestinian militants to transport weapons.
