Battambang province will hold the Water Festival at the end of October, today the provincial governor chaired a meeting to discuss preparations
(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province and Chairman of Battambang Provincial Water Festival and Floating Festival Organizing Committee 2023, in the morning of October 20, 2023, chaired a working meeting on the progress of organizing Water Festival. Boats and lanterns, Battambang province, 2023.
The meeting was attended by the Chairman of Battambang Sub-Committee on Water Festival and Lantern Festival 2023, District Governor, Chairman and Deputy Director of Provincial Departments and other stakeholders at Meeting Hall B2, Battambang Provincial Hall.
Mr. Sok Lou also instructed the planning team to look at the decoration of roads, trees, gardens and bridges, as well as to prepare and distribute forces according to the location to be determined. Emergency in case of fire or any accident.
The provincial governor said that the location is divided into two parts, the upper part of the water and the upper part of the land to make it easier for people to watch the boat race and see the product exhibition in District as well.
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Lou added that the water problem in the Sangker River must be kept constant so that the boat race is equivalent to the spectators and the other must set the time for the boat race. Clear as set to make it easier for people to visit.
In addition, the provincial governor said that the competent forces must tighten the work of protecting public order to have good security, because when there is a large public, it can also cause some insecurity, such as acts. Stealing, violence, drug trafficking, drug use and so on.
Mr. Sok Loo added that for sending bicycles, motorcycles and cars, there must be a specific and appropriate price that people can accept, there is no exploitation or opportunity to increase the price of sending, because this problem is also In part, it slowed down the growth of tourists during festivals.
At the same time, the provincial governor also encouraged each department, unit and district to have their own ark to compete during the Water Festival or other festivals to preserve the traditions of Khmer, and to take the work for the department, unit or district as well.
Mr. Sok Lou called on all people to come and visit the Water Festival and Floating Lanterns in Battambang in large numbers. At the same time, the public from all walks of life to help clean the environment and manage waste before, during and after the Water Festival, for the beauty and comfort for the province as well as the people living in Battambang.
Gold prices rise as risk of war spreads
BANGKOK: Analysts say gold could be trading at $ 1,950 to $ 1,960 an ounce as the Middle East war intensifies and hopes remain. Diplomatic talks have stalled after an attack on a hospital in Gaza.
The Bangkok Post reported that gold in the spot market traded sharply on Wednesday, rising nearly 0.8 percent from $ 1,924 to $ 1,938 an ounce, the highest level in four weeks after a drop. A bomb blast at a hospital in the Gaza Strip has killed hundreds of people and forced Arab leaders to withdraw from a planned meeting with US President Joe Biden during a visit to the region.
Wednesday was the third straight day that gold traded above $ 1,915 an ounce.
Gold traders say the threat of escalation of the conflict continues to push up bullion prices, which have risen by about 6 percent since Hamas' surprise attack on Israel on October 7.
