(Preah Vihear): An 11-kilometer-long red gravel road connecting Ta Seng Kandal village, Ranasir commune, Sangkum Thmei district, Preah Vihear province to the border of Kampong Thom province in Sakram commune, Prasat Balang district, was damaged by heavy rains. Preah Vihear Provincial Rural Development opens a site for repair and maintenance to facilitate people's travel and transportation of goods.
Mr. Mop Thirith, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Rural Development, said that on October 20, 2023, the road maintenance team of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Rural Development was repairing a red gravel road from Ta Seng Kandal village. Ranasir commune, Sangkum Thmey district to Sakram commune, Prasat Balang district, Kampong Thom province, after this road was damaged by rain during the previous rainy season.
The director of the department said that the repair and maintenance of the red gravel road now, the team has added soil and stone mix by facilitating watering, grinding, compacting, so that people can travel and transport goods to Going to the market is easy, fast and saves time.
Mr. Mop Thirith said that under the guidance of Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, and Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, the Department of Rural Development of Preah Vihear Province took care to repair and maintain the roads managed by the Department to prevent nests. Chicken to facilitate people's travel, and he also apologized to the people that some roads have not been repaired by the team.
