Articles and pictures by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio People in the informal economy are happy to see the opening of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport and believe that more visitors will come to Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Informal economy people selling goods in front of Angkor Wat temples and tuk-tuk drivers are happy after Siem Reap Angkor International Airport officially opened for flights from October 16, 2023.
Chea Chun, a tuk-tuk driver who has been transporting tourists for many years, said that in his opinion, more tourists will visit Siem Reap than ever before due to the newly opened Siem Reap Angkor International Airport. These are beautiful and attractive, have a large area and can receive direct flights from all over the world.
Moeun Raya, who also runs a tuk-tuk, said he was happy that he expected more tourists to visit Siem Reap than ever before in the Kovid crisis. But there are currently no major direct flights from other countries.
He said that in the near future, there will be direct flights from countries around the world to land at Siem Reap Angkor International Airport for all people to have jobs and boost the national economy. .
In particular, Ms. Lan Sovanna, a clothing seller in the Angkor Wat area, said that she hopes that more national and international tourists will visit Siem Reap as before, because Siem Reap has a beautiful infrastructure and recently. Open more Siem Reap Angkor International Airport.
Reang Samnang, a vendor in the Angkor Wat area, said that according to his observations during October, there were many tourists visiting Angkor Wat and recently the Siem Reap Angkor International Airport did not open again. In the long run, Siem Reap will have more tourists than ever before.
Please be informed that after opening since October 16, 2023, Siem Reap Angkor International Airport has received a lot of attention from the people, they came to visit the new airport in large numbers with a happy face. With new achievements coming from the right leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The new international airport was built on a total area of 700.06 hectares at a cost of 1,100 million US dollars in Kriel Pong village, Popel commune and Praval village, Tayek commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province, 40 km and 51 km from Angkor Wat. From Siem Reap.
