The world's first pepper mill museum officially opens in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): The world's first La Plantation Pepper Mill Museum has officially opened in Phnom Penh with the participation of officials from various ministries.
The Pepper Mill Museum will be part of the promotion of Kampot products of Cambodia around the world to be better known as pepper is grown and has a long history in Cambodia, especially pepper. Kampot has been recognized by PGI (Geographical Indication) since 2010 and is recognized as the best pepper in the world.
The Pepper Mill Museum, inaugurated on October 18, 2023, is located on the first floor of La Plantation behind the newly opened Toul Tompong Market in Phnom Penh. Visitors can taste, buy all kinds of spices and sauces directly, just like buying directly from the farm.
Guy Porré stated that starting from a trip to Cambodia with his wife made them fall in love with the favorable nature of Cambodia, especially knowing the fame of Kampot pepper, he and his wife decided Invest in pepper cultivation in Kampot province and collect pepper from the people who grow pepper there to export abroad, first to France, then more than 40 countries in the world.
The official opening of the Pepper Mill Museum also attracted the attention of Cambodian food expert and renowned chef Lu Meng, who said that the Pepper Mill Museum has introduced a long-lasting pepper mill equipment. Many years ago, some over 200 years ago, it was very important for our Cambodian children to know more about the history of use from our ancestors or chefs hundreds of years ago who used this device to grind coffee.
