Mr. Kim Virak said that the wind conditions will continue to be moderate in the first nine months of 2023. There were 263 tornadoes across the country, causing 1,956 houses to collapse and 12,664 houses to be severely damaged, with nine people dead and 169 injured in 91 school roofs.
In addition, 27 landslides occurred in 8 provincial capitals, 31 houses were damaged and 175 houses were submerged and 175 houses were demolished.
