Constitutional Council Spokesman: The Soul of the Paris Agreement has entered into the 1993 Constitution under all legal requirements.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhra, Spokesman of the Constitutional Council and Acting Secretary General of the Constitutional Council, emphasized that Cambodia currently implements the Constitution, not the text of the Paris Agreement, because the soul of the Paris Agreement Entered into the 1993 Constitution, all legal conditions have been met.
Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhra said this at a training workshop on the implementation of planning functions on the FMIS system held in Siam under the cooperation between the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council and the Ministry of Economy and Finance this morning. October 20, 2023.
As October 23, 2023 is the anniversary of the Paris Peace Agreement, in this morning's ceremony, Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhra highlighted the aspects of the Paris Peace Agreement and the Constitution of Cambodia.
"The Kingdom of Cambodia is a liberal, multi-party democracy, so we should talk about the special law, the constitution, which is the supreme law that guarantees protection in all areas, without any text of the agreement that I want," he said. "Refers to the text of the Paris Agreement, replacing the Constitution as the supreme law and forcing all state actors to implement it."
"We enforce the Constitution, not the text of the Paris Agreement, because the soul of the Paris Agreement has entered into the 1993 Constitution in all its legal terms," he added.
