The following is a press release from the Cambodian People's Party: The Minister of Agriculture calls on the people to participate in the protection and conservation of dolphins, while there are currently 90 Mekong dolphins.
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Dith Tina, said that the Ministry will continue to increase the conservation activities of dolphins in order to increase the number of dolphins, which he expects to increase the number of dolphins in Cambodia for another 10 years. Will increase by about 30 percent in addition to the current number.
Speaking to the media at the inauguration of the photo exhibition on "Cambodian Mekong Dolphins" on the evening of October 18, 2023, Mr. Dit Tina noted that the results of dolphin conservation in 2023 have improved significantly. Significantly, the number of newborn dolphins is remarkably high, while the number of dead dolphins is small.
He hopes that the conservation and protection of dolphins will continue to have good results next year and increase the number of dolphins to be a treasure for the next generation.
According to Dith Tina, there are currently 90 dolphins in the Mekong River, up from seven this year. Four dolphins died, one due to old age and three trapped by nets.
He encouraged the public to participate in preventing and reporting information when they encounter and see illegal fishing offenses occurring in dolphin sanctuaries, as the issue of dolphins is gaining more and more attention from the government, civil society organizations and partners. Involved to jointly preserve as a natural treasure for all generations to know.
