Dengue fever: Because this year is the cycle of dengue fever, which caused the disease situation to increase twice compared to the same period in 2022. In the first nine months of 2023, there were 19,000 cases of dengue fever nationwide, causing 34 deaths.
Fires: There were 472 fires across the country, including 524 houses, flats, 79 stalls, 9 factories and handicrafts. The fire damaged 57 hectares of rubber plantations, cashew nuts and acacia.
