(Phnom Penh): Acting Prime Minister Dr. Neth Savoeun called on all stakeholders to continue to encourage and provide opportunities for people with disabilities to participate in both public and private sectors.
Remarks by Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun on the occasion of representing Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the closing ceremony of the 3rd Global Conference on the Relief of Landmine Victims and Explosive Remnants in the Context of Disability Rights in Cambodia This evening, October 19, 2023.
Dr. Neth Savoeun also called on all relevant ministries, institutions and units to take all national and international legal documents related to persons with disabilities, including victims of landmines and explosive remnants of war, to implement them effectively and efficiently.
He stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has launched the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2018-2023, with careful consideration of addressing economic, employment and employment opportunities for people with disabilities.
At the same time, the Royal Government has issued a sub-decree on setting rates and procedures for the recruitment of persons with disabilities, including 2% for the public sector and 1% for the private sector. 3,748 people (23% female) work in 37 ministries, institutions and 5,839 employees in private institutions with disabilities (66% females) work in 291 private institutions.
In addition, the rights of persons with disabilities are promoted in society, along with political life, social activities, culture, sports and activities that demonstrate non-discrimination against persons with disabilities in Cambodia.
