BEIJING (Reuters) - Chinese President Xi Jinping told Egypt's prime minister on Thursday that Beijing wanted to work with Egypt to bring "stability" to the Middle East as Israel's conflict with the group, state media reported. Hamas has disturbed the surrounding area. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on October 19, 2023.
The Chinese president also pointed out that the global and regional situation is currently undergoing profound and complex changes, and the world is undergoing the greatest change in a century.
Xi stressed that Beijing is also willing to work with Cairo to "jointly safeguard international justice and common interests and the common interests of developing countries."
Since the outbreak of hostilities between Israel and Hamas this month, Egypt has closed most of its borders with the Gaza Strip, where the humanitarian situation is deteriorating. But Cairo said on Thursday it would allow humanitarian aid to cross the Rafah Strait on a "sustainable basis".
