The meeting was held on the morning of October 19, 2023 at the meeting hall of the Council of Ministers, Friendship Building of the Office of the Council of Ministers to review and discuss three main tasks, including:
* First: Amendments to the Law on the Press * Second: Amendments to the Sub-Decree on the Organization and Functioning of the Ministry of Information
The Law on the Press was approved by the National Assembly in 1995. This law regulates the press and guarantees freedom of the press and freedom of the press. As of now, the law on the press is 29 years old. For the past 29 years, the media sector in the world as a whole and in Cambodia, in particular, has made great progress, and freedom of expression and freedom of the press in Cambodia have been recognized as well-developed and well-respected.
Therefore, for this meeting, it is also a contribution to turn the Law on the Media Regime, which is planned to be amended in accordance with the evolution of the media sector in Cambodia and in the world.
Minister Neth Pheaktra stated that "The Ministry of Information plans to implement the professional standards of journalistic ethics to be implemented throughout the country to improve the value of journalists and the quality of journalists in Cambodia to join the Royal Government in increasing human resources through dissemination. "The information is really fast and has good content."
"The Ministry of Information's joint code of conduct for journalism must be supported by journalists to improve the quality of journalism in Cambodia," he said.
Minister Net Pheaktra emphasized the important role of journalists in society, helping society to participate in the development of the national economy through the dissemination of accurate, accurate, high-quality information to the people.
The Ministry of Information plans to launch a professional training institute for journalists and public relations to promote the development of human resources in the field of information to provide journalists with more capacity, knowledge, quality and diversity to meet the needs of the labor market in the context of Digital society.
