General Knowledge: Which countries recognize the King of the United Kingdom, Prince Charles, as their Head of State?
(Phnom Penh): The head of state of a country is the highest representative of that country, but may or may not be the head of government. In monarchical countries, the king or queen is the head of state, such as the Kingdom of Cambodia, the United Kingdom, and in a republic, the role of head of state falls on the president, such as the United States, the People's Republic of China. China and so on.
