Kampong Thom Provincial Council Chairman Reminds Sandan District Authorities to Crack Down on Gambling Crimes
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chhun Chhon, Chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial Council, reminded the Sandan District Authority to crack down on gambling offenses.
Kampong Thom Provincial Council received some suggestions from the consultation forum with the people in Sandan district on two main points, including:
* First: the crackdown on gambling * Second: drugs and forest crime.
These proposals and suggestions were made at the dissemination and consultation forum of the third mandate 2023, which was held at Sandan District Hall on October 19, 2023, with the participation of Mr. Nhek Ban Kheng, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province and It was attended by more than 300 members of provincial councils, government officials, provincial officials, Tang Kork district officials, the armed forces and people's representatives.
Through the above council forum, the people have requested the proposal and cracked down on and eliminated gambling such as: suffixes, lotteries, drugs and all kinds of forest crimes that cause insecurity in the local area.
Mr. Chhun Chhon said, "These insecurities are a major challenge for the livelihood of the local people, so the district administration must crack down and monitor traffic on crime. Forests caused by criminals will seriously affect our natural resources. Therefore, on behalf of the Kampong Thom provincial administration, please strongly impose regulations on the district administration to cooperate in this work effectively and transparently.
He added that the provincial council will gather all opinions, challenges and suggestions to discuss clearly and transparently and lead to effective and timely solutions.
Mr. Nhek Ban Kheng said that leaders at all levels must work together to solve the best for the people and must work actively for security, social order, implementation of village and commune safety and traffic safety, local development and Both the provision of administrative services by sub-national administrations.
He also urged the specialized departments and stakeholders to review and resolve various mechanisms according to the actual needs of the people. At the same time, he will monitor the resolution of these issues very carefully.
Please be informed that this forum is also an opportunity to disseminate about the roles and responsibilities of the provincial council and board of governors, as well as the important results that the provincial administration has achieved and raised in the forum, there are 46 questions, including 32 proposals.
