He explained, "20 tons of pure seed to farmers can get more than half a million tons of rice. If we consider the average of 3 tons per hectare. So far, we have pushed farmers to use in some provinces. As for the distribution of the institute, we do not make a wide distribution, we provide to the community or the private sector or farmers' association that he needs for the cultivation of this variety.
He also said that in addition to distributing the seeds to communities, associations or the private sector wishing to grow the new rice variety, CARDI, along with development partners, also disseminated to farmers the variety and cultivation techniques of this rice variety. In some provinces, such as Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham, Prey Veng, Takeo, Kampot, Kampong Thom, Oddar Meanchey and Banteay Meanchey, as well as further cooperation to increase outreach to farmers in other provinces.
In April 2023, Cambodia and Australia officially announced the launch of the new fragrant rice variety "Champis 70" after a nine-year study and experiment on the fields of about 80 farmers in both dry season and Rainy season.
