(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, delivered a speech on "Digital Economy as a New Source of Growth" at the Belt and Road Forum.
The following is the content of the speech of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, unofficially translated into Khmer:
First of all, I would like to congratulate the Government of the People's Republic of China and the countries participating in the Road and Belt Initiative (BRI) on the 10th anniversary of this important initiative that has connected the world to prosperity through monetary connectivity. Hubs, both software and hardware.
I sincerely commend the People's Republic of China for fulfilling this great responsibility and exercising its global leadership.
Over the past decade, digital technology has been rapidly evolving and has become a key factor in promoting greater global economic and social connectivity, bringing us closer and more interdependent. . With digitalization gaining momentum in various economic activities across all spheres, the digital economy has been growing rapidly.
To realize the full potential of the digital economy requires a comprehensive approach, including the development of favorable policies and regulations, to open up infrastructure and other necessary conditions that can support innovation, protect intellectual property and promote digital literacy.
In this regard, I welcome key partners in both the public and private sectors to explore the many opportunities that Cambodia can offer in the digital economy.
Finally, I would like to sincerely thank all the participants for their commitment to this important dialogue.
Let us seize the opportunity before us, seize the digital revolution and pave the way for a new era of growth and prosperity through the digital economy.
