The workshop was attended by Ministry leaders, Mr. Sem Van Sim, Deputy Governor of Stung Treng Province, Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Director of Post and Telecommunication Department of 5 provinces, including Stung Treng, Mondulkiri, Ratanakkiri, Preah Vihear and Kratie Provinces, as well as service operators. Total post office about 50 people.
Speaking on the occasion, Secretary of State Khay Khun Heng said that the participants who participated today were activists involved in ending HIV / AIDS and preventing the use, trafficking and trafficking of drugs to control and restrict the receipt of packages that the company. It is serving postal services and has asked you, as a representative of the postal operator, to take this knowledge to continue to support social activities through sharing.
(Kandal): Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, Minister of Interior, expressed concern about the situation of more than 100 prisoners being sent to prison per day, while only 10 to 20 were released. . In addition, the current number of inmates in the prison exceeds the prison capacity of more than 10,000.
This expression of concern was made during the awarding ceremony of the honorary doctorate degree in command of the National Police Force and the honorary doctorate of the Police Academy of Cambodia to the winners on the morning of October 19, 2023.
"The drug problem is a common concern of society and can not be solved by the authorities alone, that is, with the cooperation of all citizens, parents and guardians," said the Deputy Prime Minister.
At this point, the Minister of Interior will discuss further with the National Authority for Combating Drugs in order to reduce the drug problem by at least 20 to 30 percent in the Royal Government of the seventh legislature.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister also expressed concern about the situation of prisoners in the prison, which has more than 100 new prisoners every day. Only 10 to 20 people were released after serving their sentences. "Cambodia's prisons can only hold less than 30,000 inmates, but currently there are more than 40,000 inmates," he said.
The Minister of Interior said, "Now I am worried that more than 152,153 inmates enter the prison every day, but less than 10 to 20 people are released. Normally, prisons are now available." The more than 41,000 people that our Cambodian prisons currently receive, the maximum is just under 30,000, so we have more than 10,000, so it is very difficult for us. ”
Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha also said that he had discussed with the Minister of Justice, Mr. Keut Rith, to review the legal aspects of any level of mediation for the above issues. According to Sar Sokha, most of the prisoners currently being sent to prison are involved in drug trafficking.
At this point, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha requested the Capital-Provincial Governors and the Capital-Provincial Commissioners to pay more attention to the effective suppression of drug crimes.
