Battambang province is affected almost every year by floods, droughts, wind, lightning and other disasters. However, the Disaster Management Committee of the provinces, districts, communes and sub-branches of the Cambodian Red Cross in Battambang province has given high priority to disaster management work, overcoming all obstacles to fight on all battlefields in all aspects and circumstances.
Ms. Men Neary Sopheak also stated that today, on behalf of the Cambodian Red Cross, with Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk as the Honorary President and Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen as the President, it is a great pleasure to come. Participate in the celebration of the National Day for Disaster Management under the theme "National Investment for Community Resilience" organized by the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee of Battambang Province in Banan District.
The celebration of the National Day in conjunction with the ASEAN Day for Disaster Management and the International Day for Disaster Reduction is the implementation of the Royal Government of Cambodia's directive, in general, and in particular, for the Cambodian Red Cross is the implementation of the statement. Phnom Penh, the 20th Leaders Meeting of the National Association of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies in Southeast Asia on September 21-22, 2023.
In a joint journey towards a prosperous future, the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, has launched the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, which continues to give high priority to disaster management by linking disaster management to local development. How to ensure a smoother flow of resources to disaster management at the sub-national level for resilience and sustainable development and well-being of our compatriots.
Responding to the call of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, Head of the Royal Government in the message sent to the compatriots on the occasion of the National Day for Disaster Management, October 13, 2023, the Cambodian Red Cross, as an assistant to the Royal Government in the field of humanitarian, is obliged It is essential to work with relevant ministries / institutions, stakeholders and development partners to implement the priority directions set out in its 2021-2030 strategy as follows:
1: Continue to build the capacity of branch / sub-branch executives, volunteers, youth and poor people in the community to share knowledge, skills and experience in disaster risk reduction in an environmentally friendly manner.
2: Continue to strengthen the participation of all stakeholders, especially increase cooperation with sub-national officials, the private sector and people in the community to educate, disseminate, raise awareness of disaster prevention / reduction, continue to strengthen capacity to understand disaster risk Disaster through monitoring of danger signs, forecast information and early warning of incidents and possible accidents.
3: Pay more attention to climate change adaptation, promote public health and mental health care, promote primary health education, safe migration, and promote women's participation in Building disaster resilience and sustainable development.
4: Continue to educate and promote positive attitude change, join forces to create a society with fresh air and green environment, live clean, eat clean and hygienic through tree planting, planting mixed crops, improve livelihoods and be together Reduce the use of plastic bags.
Please be informed that in the above day, there is also a Q&A program which was attended by 16 students, youths and volunteers, and as an encouragement, these 16 participants received souvenirs from the Cambodian Red Cross, each of whom received a handkerchief. 1 hand wipe, 1 packet of soap, 1 bar of soap and 20,000 Riels.
On that occasion, the students also showed interest and commitment to participate in reducing disaster risk by planting trees and not cutting down trees, especially to preserve the environment and disseminate to families, friends and in the community.
