Senior NEC official: Political parties legally registered with the Ministry of Interior have the right to request a copy of the initial voter list, but must pay a fee.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hal Sarath, Member of the NEC, stated that political parties registered in accordance with the Law on Political Parties at the Ministry of Interior have the right to request a copy of the initial voter list, but must pay a fee.
Mr. Hal Sarath confirmed this on October 19, 2023, when he chaired a meeting with stakeholders to update and provide some information related to the registration process and registration. Commune / Sangkat Election 2023, which was implemented from the first day until October 19, 2023.
At the same time, Mr. Hal Sarath added that this price is only for the cost of production. In particular, so far the NEC has not received any complaints regarding voter registration.
He said that during the 19 days of the voter list and voter registration process in the commune, the NEC and NEC officials at all levels, especially the voter registration team, were ready and ready. Properly follow the laws, regulations and procedures as well as other legal documents that make the process of checking the voter list and voter registration in 2023 run smoothly.
In addition, the senior official of the NEC confirmed that the relevant parties actively participated at the invitation of the NEC, BEC, Commune / Sangkat Council and their respective duties. Citizens are highly educated and actively involved in the voter list and voter registration process.
(Kandal): Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, Minister of Interior, said that according to the report from the Capital-Provincial Police Commissioner, the problem of gangsters has increased significantly in recent years, which needs to be studied to find out the roots. Of the problems to solve effectively and the drug problem is also a concern, so please continue to crack down on drugs effectively.
The Deputy Prime Minister said this during the awarding ceremony of the honorary doctorate in command of the National Police Force and the honorary doctorate of the Police Academy of Cambodia to the winners on the morning of October 19, 2023 at the Police Academy of Cambodia in Kien Svay district. Kandal Province.
On this occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha said, "Regarding the gangsters, we have seen in recent days, through the report of the Capital-Provincial Commissioner who fired into the group, we have seen a significant increase, sometimes not. "Knowing that his magic is included, his purpose is just to cut the motorcycle or cut the motorcycle license plate or throw it to the river."
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha also instructed the competent authorities to study the causes of the increase in gangs and take effective action.
In addition, the Deputy Prime Minister urged to crack down on the drug problem effectively, as it is seen that most of the inmates today are smokers and drug dealers, while more than 100 inmates a day, and the total number of current inmates. There are more than 40,000 inmates, and the prison can only hold more than 30,000, which causes overcrowding in the prison, thus seeing an increase in inmates.
It is noteworthy that in the last few months of 2023, the number of gangsters has increased significantly, which is disturbing as well as causing anarchy in society. Separately, the case of killing wives and children in Kandal Stung district in the past was also partly due to the effects of drugs, combined with jealousy.
However, the competent authorities also took a series of repressive measures.
After completing their mission in Beijing, President Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Bandith and the delegation have not returned to Cambodia, but will continue their journey to Riyadh, Saudi Arabia to attend the ASEAN-Gulf Cooperation Council Summit. ASEAN-GCC Summit).
During the summit, the President will hold bilateral meetings with a number of foreign dignitaries in Riyadh to promote bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and the Gulf Cooperation Council member countries.
It should be noted that Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav led the delegation to work abroad for the fourth time at the beginning of the new legislature on October 16, 2023.
The President and his entourage and the delegation traveled to Beijing to attend the "Belt and Road" forum, an important forum in response to the invitation of Chinese President Xi Jinping.
The second visit to China as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen has many work programs during these four days and also bring great benefits for the nation and the people of Cambodia.
These agreements will further contribute to Cambodia's development of infrastructure, energy, technology and trade.
The following are the main articles of Hun Manet's working visit to China:
The meeting took place at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing, China. This morning's meeting with Xi Jinping is the second in his capacity as Prime Minister Hun Manet as Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The first meeting was held on September 15, 2023 during the President's official visit to China.
It should be noted that during his current visit to China, Hun Sen also met with Chinese Premier Li Keqiang and Cai Qi, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and chairman of the General Affairs Bureau. Of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China.
This initiative was raised by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, during a meeting with Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit this morning, Thursday, October 19, 2023 in Beijing, China, where the President and Head of State of Laos attended. The third "Belt and Road" forum.
During the meeting, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit expressed his pleasure to meet with the President in Beijing on this occasion and also congratulated the President on the support of the new government.
The head of state of Laos also expressed confidence that under the leadership of the President, relations between Cambodia and Laos will continue to grow. Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit also congratulated Cambodia on its success in hosting the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits and Related Summits in 2022, as well as the 1st Southeast Asian Games. 32 and the 12th ASEAN Para Games in 2023.
In response, President Hun Manet thanked for the opportunity of the meeting and praised the progress of cooperation in all fields between the two countries.
For the future direction, Samdech Hun Manet supported the continued implementation of the "Joint Trilateral Exercise on Disaster Relief Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam" as organized in September 2022.
During the meeting, the President of Laos invited Samdech Manet to pay an official visit to Laos. The Prime Minister gladly accepted the invitation and will set an appropriate date for his visit to Laos.
Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Oddar Meanchey Provides Loans to 50 Poor Families in Anlong Veng District
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Khin Nhean, Permanent Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee, Oddar Meanchey Province, on the afternoon of October 18, 2023, led the working group to provide loans, which are the budget of the Cambodian Red Cross to provide poor families, families with disabilities and 50 widows in Anlong Veng district.
On that occasion, Mr. Khin Nhean sent a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and Mr. Pen Kosal, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee in Oddar Meanchey Province, who always pays attention to the well-being and Livelihoods of the people, especially the poor, widows, the disabled, the elderly, the homeless, the orphans, as well as the people affected by various natural disasters.
Mr. Khin Nhean stated that, in fact, today, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Oddar Meanchey province provided loans, which are the budget of the Cambodian Red Cross, as small loans to 50 disabled families, widows and poor families in Anlong Veng district, including 26 cases from Anlong Veng commune and 24 cases from Trapeang Tao commune, each case can get 1 million Riels without interest.
Mr. Khin Nhean further stated that the loan provided to the poor people for various occupations at this time is not a gift and you can borrow for up to one year without interest and repayment. Return every 6 months with 1 million Riel to be repaid twice, the first time for 6 months, 500,000 Riels and the second time for 6 months, another 500,000 Riels for the Red Cross Cambodia will continue to provide loans to the poor.
He also called on our people after receiving this loan and to strive to expand businesses such as agriculture, animal husbandry ... to improve family life.
