Putin called the attack on a hospital in Gaza, which killed hundreds, a "terrible disaster" and called for talks.
BEIJING, Oct. 18 (Xinhua) - Russian President Vladimir Putin said on Wednesday that an attack on a hospital in the Gaza Strip that had killed hundreds of Palestinians was a "terrible catastrophe" that marked the conflict. Between Israel and Hamas should be concluded through negotiations. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on October 18, 2023.
"Regarding the attack on the hospital, the tragedy that took place there was a horrific event," Putin said after talks with Chinese President Xi Jinping in Beijing.
Russia, which has ties to Iran, Hamas and the Arab powers, as well as to Palestine and Israel, has repeatedly said that the United States and the West ignore the Palestinian demands for an independent state for them. They have no boundaries in 1967.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Keut Rith, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Justice, urged all court officials and officials involved in the judiciary in Kampong Thom province to pay more attention to strengthening the quality of justice for the people and speeding up the resolution of cases in a transparent manner. And integrity.
This instruction was made during the inauguration ceremony of Mr. Ros Saram, Prosecutor of Kampong Thom Provincial Court, replacing Mr. Sin Virak, who moved to Kampong Speu Province on the morning of October 18, 2023.
Mr. Sin Virak reported that the Kampong Thom Provincial Court has accelerated the search for justice as well as enhanced the capacity of the judiciary to provide justice services and reduce overcrowding in prisons, with the remaining 25 criminal cases before February 25, 2020. 299 stories.
Mr. Keut Rith stressed that the Ministry of Justice has set the direction of reform in the field of justice as a priority for the next five years, the two pillars of reform:
* First. Strive for reform in the judiciary and develop new mechanisms to reform the Cambodian land dispute resolution mechanism to resolve disputes out of the court system through mediation.
* Second. Priorities in the implementation of the reform policy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature, the establishment of non-judicial dispute resolution mechanisms, the promotion and expeditious settlement of congested court cases and the resolution of irregularities in the courts in order to help resolve justice To the people and to promote transparency, integrity and fairness in law enforcement and court proceedings.
Mr. Keut Rith urged all officials to be united in order to achieve the reform of the Royal Government, especially judges, prosecutors, clerks, clerks must be more careful in handling the case seriously and transparently.
He added that officials related to all judicial institutions in Kampong Thom province, the judiciary police force should also pay attention to cracking down and enforce the law on drug offenses effectively.
Mr. Ros Saram, Prosecutor of Kampong Thom Thmey Provincial Court, is committed to directing and coordinating the work of the Judicial Police in order to prevent and suppress criminal offenses within its jurisdiction in order to achieve the goals of the Ministry of Justice and the Royal Government. Dr. Kao Kim Hourn Attends the Opening Ceremony of the 3rd Belt and Road Forum for International Cooperation and Addresses the High-Level Forum in Beijing
BEIJING, Oct. 18 (Xinhua) - The Secretary-General of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, attended the opening ceremony of the Third Belt and Road Forum for International Cooperation on October 18, 2023 in Beijing.
Leaders and dignitaries from countries in the region and around the world came together to celebrate the 10th anniversary of the Belt and Road Initiative.
Then, on the afternoon of October 18, 2023, in Beijing, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn addressed the High-Level Forum on Connectivity as part of the Third Belt and Road Forum for International Cooperation.
On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General emphasized the importance of strengthening connectivity within ASEAN and beyond the region towards further promoting the integration of the ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan 2025, the ASEAN Vision on the Indo-Pacific Region. And the Belt and Road Initiative.
