BEIJING: China's economy grew faster than expected in the third quarter of this year, while consumption and industrial activity in September also rose, indicating that new policy measures are helping to boost growth. Economic recovery. According to Reuters.
The second-largest slowdown in economic growth since the second quarter has prompted authorities to step up their economic support measures, with data on Wednesday showing that stimulus measures are just beginning. Demonstrates influence Although the real estate crisis and other issues continue to pose risks to the economic outlook.
China's gross domestic product (GDP) rose 4.9 percent in the third quarter from a year earlier, Reuters reported citing data released by the National Bureau of Statistics on Wednesday. Analysts had expected growth of 4.4 percent in a Reuters poll. However, economic growth in the third quarter was lower than the 6.3 percent achieved in the second quarter.
Compared to the same quarter and quarter in the same year, economic growth in the third quarter rose 1.3 percent, up from 0.5 percent in the second quarter and higher than the forecast. 1 percent growth.
