WASHINGTON, Oct. 7 (Xinhua) - Palestinian militant group Hamas, which controls the Gaza Strip, launched a surprise offensive in the southern part of Israel, one of the deadliest attacks in Israeli history. Israel immediately declared war on Hamas with a deadly retaliatory bombing of Gaza, home to more than 2 million Palestinians.
As violence escalates, international humanitarian organizations have called for immediate humanitarian assistance to enter the Gaza Strip and the creation of a humanitarian corridor for refugees.
On October 12, the Israeli energy minister confirmed that electricity, fuel and water would not be re-supplied until more than 199 hostages were released by Hamas.
Indonesia, Malaysia join global condemnation of Gaza hospital attack (Video inside) (Jakarta): Indonesia and Malaysia on Wednesday joined the global condemnation of last night's Israeli airstrikes on the hospital. A doctor in the Gaza Strip has killed hundreds of Palestinian civilians. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on October 18, 2023.
At least 500 people were killed on Tuesday in an Israeli airstrike on the Ahli Arab hospital in central Gaza, with images shared on social media showing extensive damage. Seriously, the fire engulfed buildings and scattered bodies.
The attack comes as Israel continues its offensive against civilians in the Gaza Strip, which has quickly drawn international condemnation from both Saudi Arabia, Jordan and the United Arab Emirates.
"Indonesia strongly condemns the Israeli attack on the Al-Ahly Al-Arabi hospital in the Gaza Strip, which killed hundreds of civilians," the Indonesian Foreign Ministry said in a statement. The attack is a clear violation of international humanitarian law. "And the International Security Council must take immediate action to end the attacks and violence in Gaza."
"Injustice against the Palestinian people has lasted too long," the ministry said, adding that it was time for the world to "prioritize peace for Palestine."
Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim also called for an end to the attacks. He said he would discuss the situation in Gaza during his visit to Riyadh for the first joint summit between the Association of Southeast Asian Nations and the Gulf Cooperation Council on Friday.
