Tourism experts applaud the opening of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport with the expectation of attracting more international tourists
(Phnom Penh): A group of business people and experts in the field of tourism have expressed their congratulations to the Royal Government of Cambodia for the new achievement is the opening of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport.
The experts expressed hope that the new airport, which receives landings from large aircraft, could bring tourists and investors to Cambodia as well.
Ho Vandy, President of the Council of the Cambodian Tourism Association, told Fresh News on October 18, 2023 that Siem Reap Angkor International Airport can attract a lot of international tourists because it is a kind of international airport that provides confidence. Many airlines around the world are looking at and bringing in big planes to bring tourists from different regions to Cambodia.
He said that the Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport can not only attract and receive tourists, but also move towards trade through the transportation of goods, which is another factor in the recovery of the national economy.
He added that in order to receive international tourists, Cambodia also needs to strengthen and prepare more, such as strengthening the hospitality sector, both public and private sector, provide comprehensive services and warmth to guests, in addition, should be encouraged legally. Such as visa waivers, tax exemptions and incentives for investors in the short or long term, these factors make Cambodia able to recover the economy and tourism.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Cambodian Tourism Association, said that Siem Reap Angkor International Airport will be able to attract more international tourists through its ability to accommodate large aircraft, and this is another new interest for the airline. Those who do not want to fly through other countries can fly directly to Cambodia and land at these Siem Reap Angkor International Airports and expect that Cambodia may receive more tourists.
"What is even better is to benefit the national economy by providing employment opportunities to the people from the beginning of construction until its launch, in addition to attracting investment and attracting tourists," she said. "Flights because of direct flights save a lot of time for tourists, which leads guests to have enough time to continue to visit other provinces or regions in Cambodia."
She stated that in addition to providing benefits to local people, either working or doing business, etc., because the Siem Reap Angkor International Airport is far from Siem Reap, so people living near the airport can do business. Business to serve customers.
She said that with the influx of tourists on behalf of the Cambodian Tourism Association is ready to organize tour packages for tourists. In addition, Cambodia has actively participated with associations in ASEAN countries to introduce new products, new tours and the emergence of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport to attract more tourists to Cambodia.
Thuon Sinan, President of the Asia-Pacific Tourism Association in Cambodia, also mentioned the advantages of having a country with an airport capable of accommodating large aircraft as part of receiving international tourists.
