(Kandal): Mr. Hak Sok Makara, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, this morning, October 18, 2023, led a working group to inspect the case of flooding on National Road No. 3 at km 30 of the provincial border. Kandal and Kampong Speu provinces, as well as ordered the excavation machine to open one more drain across National Road 3 and one more drain in front of a total of two places to drain into the canal. To Tonle Bati.
The inspection was attended by the Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport, the Governor of Kandal Stung District, the Deputy Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, the Deputy Governor of Kong Pisey District, representatives of the Provincial Police and other relevant working groups.
Mr. Hak Sok Makara said that after the team used machinery to drain the water to release water, now the water situation is continuing to decline. The flood point is located at the border of Kampong Speu province (Phean Sar village, Preah Nipean commune, Kong Pisey district) and Kandal province (Prey Toteung village, Trapeang Veng commune, Kandal Stung district) at the 30 km point on National Road 3.
