Congratulations! The construction project of "Funik Techo Canal" has taken another step, the Royal Government of Cambodia signed an agreement for a Chinese company to study in detail before reaching a negotiation agreement for a construction agreement
(Beijing, China): The most exciting thing right now is the construction of "Funan Techo Canal", a project to connect the river between the river to the sea of Cambodia, has taken another step forward by the Royal Government of Cambodia. The agreement allows Chinese companies to study the project in more detail before reaching a final agreement on construction.
The signing ceremony for the Chinese company to study in detail on the above important project was held on the evening of October 17, 2023 in Beijing under the presidency of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said with excitement and joy, "Today's signing is a step towards another success on Cambodia's major transport project." The Deputy Prime Minister expressed the expectation that the project could open in 2024 if nothing changes.
The "Funan Techo Canal" project aims to expand the potential use of water transport to contribute to the promotion of socio-economic activities to a further level and provide appropriate solutions to problems. Challenges and obstacles of the water transport sector that we have been facing today.
According to the study, the Funan-Techo canal is 180 km long from Takeo canal on the Mekong River, passing through Ta Ek canal of Bassac river, then entering Ta Hing canal of Bassac river, Koh Thom district and continuing to the sea. Kep passes through four provinces, including Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep, with a total population of 1.6 million people living on either side of the waterway.
The waterway is 100 meters wide at the top and 80 meters wide at the bottom and 5.4 meters deep (navigation depth 4.7 meters and safety gap 0.7 meters). 2 lanes can get in and out and avoid each other safely.
