This important event was held on October 17, 2023 during the "One Belt One Road" forum in Beijing, marking the beginning of a strategic partnership between Cambodia and Alibaba, focusing on promoting E-Commerce
The signing of this Memorandum of Understanding marks an important time in the ongoing partnership between Cambodia and Alibaba. This important step demonstrates Cambodia's commitment to boosting economic growth and technological innovation, opening up new opportunities for economic growth and technological advancement in Cambodia, further strengthening the partnership between Cambodia and Cambodia. Alibaba.
Global e-Commerce (eWTP) is an innovative initiative of Alibaba and was created to promote global business, especially e-commerce, using the potential of digital technology and e-commerce. eWTP aims to reduce trade barriers and increase the efficiency of international trade through cross-border trade facilitation, especially for small and medium enterprises (SMEs).
It should also be noted that eWTP cooperation in Cambodia started on December 27, 2019 with the first visit of a representative of Alibaba e-commerce talent training team in Cambodia.
This cooperation is also widely supported by the Ministry of Commerce, and has the active participation of key stakeholders including: Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Forestry, Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, Ministry of Tourism, National Committee for Promotion One Village, One Product Movement (OVOP), Entrepreneurship Development Fund (CSF) of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Battambang National University.
According to the Xinhua News Agency, the leaders of the forum are Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Sen, Thai Prime Minister Sethak Thaksin Shinawatra, Indonesian President Joko Widodo and Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung. Thuong and the head of state of Laos, Thongloun Sisoulit.
The third "Belt and Road" forum is held under the theme "High Quality Belt and Road Cooperation: Working Together for Joint Development and Prosperity."
During the meeting, Mr. Vavanthoeung congratulated Samdech Thipady on receiving support to lead the new Royal Government. The Vietnamese head of state expressed optimism that under the leadership of the Prime Minister, Cambodia will successfully implement all policies set out in both the national and international frameworks.
Mr. Vann Thuong also stated that Vietnam still maintains close ties and cooperation with Cambodia for the common benefit of both nations and peoples.
President Hun Manet thanked for the meeting and recalled the meeting with the Vietnamese President four years ago, which was an opportunity for discussions to strengthen and expand cooperation between the two countries.
The Prime Minister happily noted the development of relations in all fields. The volume of bilateral trade and the number of tourists between the two countries have also been steadily increasing, and cooperation in the field of defense and human resource training has also been active.
