Senior NEC official: In the future, if the local authorities control the mobility of citizens, there may be no voter registration, but prepare the first voter list and post it publicly.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mean Sati, a member of the NEC, said that in the future, if the local authorities can control the movement of the people, there may be no voter registration, but prepare the first voter list and post it. In public.
This is according to Mr. Mean Sati quoted in the press release on the results of the meeting to disseminate the voter registration and the correction of the voter list for the 5th legislative election of 2023 in the morning. October 17, 2023.
Mr. Mean Sati said that Cambodia is implementing two non-universal elections for this voter list: the election of senators and the election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council. Globally, preparing a voter list like this saves a lot of money.
Mr. Mean Sati also mentioned about the preparation of voter lists in other countries in the general election that there is no voter registration, local authorities are the first to prepare the voter list and post it to complain. Court or complain to the National Election Committee. NEC Releases Press Release on Voter Registration Meeting for the 5th Senate Election
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a press release on the meeting to disseminate information on voter registration and voter list correction for the 5th Senate Election 2023. .
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Mean Sati, a member of the NEC and chaired the meeting on the morning of October 17, 2023.
He added that the resolution of complaints must be carried out from the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (NEC) at the NEC level and must end at the Constitutional Council. He said that for the 5th Senate election, the constituencies will be organized and divided into 8 zones with a total of 58 seats (plus 2 senators appointed by the King and 2 more). Elected by the National Assembly by a majority vote).
Regarding the voter list, Mr. Mean Sati said that it was prepared in each provincial capital, including commune councils and deputies of each provincial capital, and the NEC had to summarize the election results in each province. Each of the eight districts across the country.
He added that the registration of voters for the election of senators must be done by extracting the names of eligible voters, adding them to the list separately for each constituency and sending them in hierarchical order to the NEC. On time.
Mr. Mean Sati added that the General Secretariat of the National Assembly must prepare a list of deputies in the position, and then the Secretary General of the National Assembly shall sign and seal the General Secretariat of the National Assembly with the approval of the President of the National Assembly and send it to the NEC. By the due date. This list shall be prepared separately according to the deputies in the positions of each capital and provincial constituency.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has given priority to environmental sustainability, as stated in the Pentagon Strategy Phase 1 of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is the main condition stated in the motto "Employment Growth, Equity, Efficiency and Sustainability".
The Ministry of Environment has identified four main measures for effective management of natural resources and biodiversity conservation and for sustainable development, including:
* First, the Ministry of Environment promotes 100% law enforcement and ends the culture of education, guidance and contracting and release of natural resource perpetrators.
* Second, the Ministry of Environment cooperates closely with the Capital-Provincial Administrative Unity Command, especially with local authorities to prevent natural resource crime in protected areas.
* Third: Cooperate with the Anti-Corruption Unit and the National Gendarmerie Command to suppress and prevent natural resource crimes in addition to the cooperation with local authorities in the past.
* 4: Planting more trees than cutting to maintain growth, especially the promotion of reforestation as a priority direction to increase forest cover by 60% by 2050 in accordance with the Pentagon strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia and improve people's livelihood. Citizens in communities, sustainable biodiversity conservation.
Through this, the Ministry of Environment has launched a campaign on October 10 to provide and plant at least 1 million trees per year from 2024.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, welcomed and encouraged all local and foreign partner organizations to contribute to the ministry's priority work, including planting bamboo and palm trees, to achieve the common goal of expanding forest cover and In particular, encourage people who want to contribute to the protection and conservation of forests, improve people's livelihoods and have made significant contributions to solving global problems on climate change.
