EU allows Cambodia to use raw materials or bicycle components from Vietnam to produce and export to its country
(Phnom Penh): The European Union has allowed Cambodia to use raw materials or bicycle components (bicycles) of Vietnamese origin to produce bicycles in Cambodia for export to the European Union. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Commerce.
All bicycle manufacturers or exporters must apply for a permit from the Ministry of Commerce on the quantity of raw materials or components imported from Vietnam on a semi-annual basis and report quarterly on the consumption of raw materials or components. The Ministry of Commerce for the Ministry has the basis to notify the EU.
Speaking to Fresh News on October 17, 2023, Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed that this permission will make the Cambodian bicycle export market more convenient due to Ease of sourcing raw materials from neighboring Vietnam.
In the nine months from January to September 2023, Cambodia earned more than $ 424 million from bicycle exports, a decrease of more than 42% compared to the same period in 2022 of more than $ 742 million. . This is according to the report of the Ministry of Commerce.
The main markets for Cambodia's bicycle exports are the United States, Germany, Belgium, the United Kingdom and the Netherlands, while Cambodia re-imports bicycles from Japan, China, Vietnam, Thailand and the United States.
