Articles and pictures by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio More than 34 tons of rice seeds were provided by Tbong Khmum provincial governor to 342 target farmers affected by floods in Tbong Khmum district
(Tbong Khmum): Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, on October 17, 2023, brought 34,200 kg of rice seeds with the assistance of the Royal Government to distribute to 342 target farmers who damaged their rice crops with water. Flood in 2023 to rehabilitate in Boeung Proul and Peam Chiling communes in Tbong Khmum district.
The handing over of rice seeds took place at Wat Peam Mongkul, also known as Wat Peam, in Peam Chiliang commune, Tbong Khmum district, with the participation of a delegation from the Ministry of Agriculture, the National Committee for Disaster Management, the deputy governor, the three armed forces, the director / deputy director of the surrounding department. Provinces, local authorities, farmers and many other stakeholders.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan has received a message from Samdech Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, always thinking of the well-being, responding and solving in time to the people at the local level.
The provincial governor confirmed that the provision of rice seeds to farmers at this time is by seeing the hardships of farmers affected by floods, floods affect farmers' rice crops.
