(Phnom Penh): This morning, October 17, 2023, the National Election Committee (NEC) held a meeting with stakeholders on commune / sangkat voter registration at the National Assembly, hierarchical confirmation and submission to the NEC for the election. Election of Senators for the 5th term in 2025.
The meeting was held in the presence of Mr. Mean Sati, a member of the NEC, and was attended by representatives of the Embassy in Cambodia, representatives of ministries, institutions, representatives of political parties and NGOs, national and international media.
The senior NEC official said that for the 5th Senate election, the constituency was organized and divided into 8 zones with a total of 58 seats (plus 2 senators who were elected). Appointed by the King and two others elected by the National Assembly by a majority vote).
At the same time, he added that the voter list was prepared in each capital-province, including commune councils and deputies of each capital-province, and the NEC must summarize the results. Vote in each of the eight constituencies across the country.
Mr. Mean Sati added that the registration of voters for the election of senators must be done by extracting the names of eligible voters into the list separately for each constituency and sending them in hierarchical order to the NEC. To meet deadlines.
At the same time, he said that the General Secretariat of the National Assembly must prepare a list of deputies in office, then the Secretary General of the National Assembly will sign and seal the General Secretariat of the National Assembly with the approval of the President of the National Assembly and send it to the NEC. By the due date. This list shall be prepared separately according to the deputies in the positions of each capital and provincial constituency.
Commune / Sangkat Councils shall prepare a list of all Commune / Sangkat Councilors in their positions, and sign the Commune / Sangkat Council and Commune / Sangkat Chiefs and sign the Commune / Sangkat Administration with the approval of the Municipal, District and Khan Governors and the Board of Governors. Relevant capitals and provinces and send to the NEC by the due date.
Speaking to reporters at the welcoming ceremony for the first commercial flight to Siem Reap Angkor International Airport (SAI) on October 16, 2023, he said that this new achievement is an important catalyst in promoting The vision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, has become a reality in the transformation of Siem Reap, a former conflict zone, into a development and prosperity zone in the future.
He added that Siem Reap Angkor International Airport is a huge economic force, not only to promote tourism, but also to benefit agriculture, technology and other sectors, especially as a major air freight destination. Also important because some industrial goods are also transported by air.
He added that the opening of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport was in line with the open-air policy set by former Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the past, with no controls or restrictions on flights for anyone. Anyone who wants to travel to Cambodia is allowed. This openness is very attractive for tourism and commercial transport.
"A lot of doors, a lot of doors, a lot of imports, but when we put the door too small, it does not enter because our country is still poorer, less attractive if we restrict the flight, it is not attractive. No, so to this day we see that this open sky policy is the right strategy. "We continue to do more to attract both tourism and investors and international trade."
He said that in the past, most of the international passengers and tourists who came to Cambodia came from neighboring countries because the old airport was able to accommodate only small aircraft, but the new airport is large. Large can receive direct flights from remote areas, which is a big attraction for tourists and investors.
