Kampong Thom Provincial Council and Provincial Administration Receive Some Requests from Consultation Forum with Citizens in Taing Kork District
(Kampong Thom): Kampong Thom Provincial Council and Kampong Thom Provincial Administration received some requests from the consultation forum with the people in Taing Kork district, such as the request to repair the road, the request to issue a title deed as a system to suppress fishing crimes, gambling, and the request to rescue the affected situation. Floods, requests for expedited identification and birth certificates.
These proposals were raised by the dissemination and consultation forum of the third mandate 2023, which was held at Tang Kork District Hall on October 17, 2023 under the chairmanship of Mr. Chhun Chhon, Chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial Council, Mr. Nhek Ban Kheng, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, and more than 300 members of provincial councils, government officials, provincial hall officials, Tang Kork district officials, the armed forces and people's representatives.
Through the above council forum, the people have proposed to repair the road, request to issue a title deed as a system of fishing offenses, crack down on gambling such as suffixes, lottery numbers, drugs, expedite the issuance of lost or damaged ID cards and birth certificates.
In the future, the people have asked the Kampong Thom Provincial Council and the provincial administration to help alleviate the situation affected by the floods, such as damage to rice crops, plantations and other infrastructure.
Mr. Chhun Chhon said that the provincial council will collect all opinions, challenges and suggestions to discuss and clarify clearly, transparently and lead to effective and timely solutions.
Mr. Nhek Ban Kheng urged the specialized departments and stakeholders to review and resolve various mechanisms according to the actual needs of the people. At the same time, he will monitor the resolution of these issues very carefully.
