Preah Vihear Governor Takes Violent Measures to Detect and Settle Homes
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, used hot measures to order the police to detain 12 people after they started clearing and burning people's houses in Srong Yong Cheung village, Sroyong commune and Kulen Tbong village, Kulen commune. Tbong, Kulen District, Preah Vihear Province.
Kim Rithy's use of force came after a woman named Toun Chantrea led her party to clear the crops and homes of nine families in the area described above.
According to information from local authorities, Mr. Kim Rithy said that the above nine families have been living and cultivating for more than 10 years. At the same time, fruit trees have grown large enough to bear fruit. This is proof that the nine families have been occupying this land for many years.
Mr. Kim Rithy pointed out that the root of the problem is one thing, but the use of violence to clear people's crops and houses without the knowledge of the courts and provincial authorities is illegal and unacceptable.
Currently, a woman named Toun Chantrea and her party have been temporarily detained by Mr. Kim Rithy, waiting for the police to find out the truth about this later. Mr. Kim Rithy claimed that he would search for the truth in this matter by not allowing any violations of the law and causing any harm to innocent people.
Mr. Kim Rithy's hot measures on the above case received a lot of attention and praise from the people at the scene. The nine families expressed their deep gratitude to the governor. They consider this action to show the willingness of the provincial governor to consider and protect the interests of the people from the abuse of corrupt people. During the 15 days of Kanben, there were 24 fires
