(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Climate Change Meeting 2023 (CCCS23) is scheduled to be held on November 2 and 3 in Siem Reap, bringing together key stakeholders and experts from around Southeast Asia to Discuss the issue of climate change at the highest level in the history of the meeting.
The meeting will be held at the Borey Angkor Hotel, focusing on key topics such as climate financing, the role of renewable energy, entrepreneurship in the energy sector, natural solutions, water security, innovation in agriculture, sustainable tourism and regulatory compliance. Various.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, will deliver the keynote address at the meeting, highlighting key points, as well as speeches from representatives of the Australian Embassy, US Embassy and other institutions.
"I am very pleased that Australia is the official partner of the 2023 Cambodia Climate Change Meeting," said Justin Wyatt, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia.
"Australia is committed to working with Cambodia to strengthen its resilience to climate change, build a clean energy sector and help Cambodia achieve its carbon neutrality goal by 2050."
"CAPRED will hold discussions on climate-sensitive agriculture, the road to climate change resilience, and climate financing," added Justin Wyatt.
The SDC-sponsored Sustainable Solutions Expo will highlight climate change initiatives and products.
Markus Bürli, Director of SDC, said: "We need to make sure that all existing technologies and services that are designed to mitigate and adapt to climate change are implemented. The Sustainable Solutions Expo will showcase those technologies and services as well as how they are being implemented in Cambodia. ”
The Cambodian Climate Change Meeting has been held annually since 2021. The meeting to be held in 2022 is the first conference in Cambodia with carbon neutrality and the meeting to be held in 2023 is the first program to achieve carbon neutrality through carbon credit payments .
The Cambodia Climate Change Meeting 2023 will be free to attend and thank you for your support. Attendees are encouraged to register as soon as possible through cccs23.org to get a place to join. Those wishing to attend the event need to register first and due to limited space they will be contacted back to see if they can attend.
The public is warmly welcomed to attend the Sustainable Solutions Exhibition, which will run from 9am to 3:30 pm on November 2nd and 3rd in the lobby of the Borey Angkor Hotel. Participation in the exhibition does not require registration.
