The Minister in charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation emphasized this during the welcoming ceremony for the first commercial flight to Siem Reap Angkor International Airport (SAI) on October 16, 2023.
At the beginning of October 2023, the average number of domestic and international passenger and air cargo operations was 850 flights per week, departing and entering the three international airports, and 30 domestic and foreign airlines. The company is also reconnecting flights from eight ASEAN countries, China, South Korea, Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, Taiwan and Qatar.
"Even though the current daily flight traffic is only 34 flights, or 32% of 2019, we still hope that the brand new infrastructure of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport will be sufficient to attract the airline flights," he said. "Domestic and foreign, especially flights from China, may return to normal soon."
He added that the Siem Reap Angkor International Airport will also contribute to the long-term sustainable growth of the Cambodian economy, especially to increase Cambodia's competitiveness in the context of Cambodia's economic integration into ASEAN and the world.
He said that with natural resources and investment in other important physical infrastructure in the near future, the city-airport area will become an important economic pole for the development of Cambodia, especially as an important "catalyst". To promote the recovery and development of tourism potential.
At the same time, the development of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport (SAI) and the surrounding area not only contributes to economic growth, job creation and poverty reduction, but also an invaluable achievement in Supporting regional and global integration, especially promoting the attractiveness of tourism and the image of Cambodia to another level.
At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia will increase its efforts to speed up the resolution of structural problems in order to seize the opportunities and utilize the full potential of the tourism sector to contribute to the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
This was stated by Mr. Mao Havannal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation during the welcoming ceremony for the first commercial flight to Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport (SAI) on the morning of October 16, 2023 under the chairmanship of the Deputy Prime Minister. Kar Vongsey Visoth, Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
