Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Arrive Safely in Beijing (Video inside) (Beijing, China) Her Excellency Pech Chanmony Hun Manet led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to Beijing, China safely.
The arrival of His Excellency and His Excellency at the Beijing Capital International Airport in China was warmly welcomed by senior Chinese government and Cambodian officials in China, including Minister Tang Renjlan. Agriculture and Rural Affairs, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, Cambodian Ambassador to China and other key leaders.
It should be noted that at around 8 this morning, His Excellency Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to attend the 3rd Belt and Road Forum for International Cooperation in Beijing, China.
The invitation to attend the forum was made at the invitation of Chinese President Xi Jinping. The Third Belt and Road Forum (3 BRF) for International Cooperation will be held from October 17 to 18, 2023 in Beijing under the theme "High Quality Belt and Road Cooperation: "Together for common development and prosperity."
Accompanying the President were Mr. Sun Chanthol, Deputy Prime Minister and First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, as well as senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia and private sector leaders. Well.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, at the Belt and Road Forum, the President will deliver a keynote address on "Digital Economy as a Source of New Growth."
During the forum, the President will hold talks with President Xi Jinping and other Chinese leaders to discuss bilateral and multilateral cooperation, as well as separate meetings with other foreign dignitaries. Also.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs emphasized that the President's participation in the Third Belt and Road Forum will reaffirm Cambodia's support for the Belt and Road Initiative, which underscores Cambodia's commitment to close cooperation. With China to promote high-quality belt and road cooperation for common growth, peace and sustainable development in the region and internationally.
