During the talks and press conference, Minister Ly Thuch said that Cambodia is proud to host the 3rd Global Conference on Mine Rescue and welcomed the presence of Prince Mired. Raad Zeid Al-Hussein and a delegation from the Ottawa Convention Support Team, who took the time to provide important information and co-organize the entire Third World Conference.
At the same time, the senior minister praised Prince Mired's dedication to spending 19 years in promoting mine action towards a landmine-free world.
He added that during the third global conference, which was attended by representatives of 45 countries and many experts, the results and challenges in the implementation of the past conventions will be discussed and discussed. Promote better implementation of the Convention on the Relief of Landmine and Explosive Ordnance Victims and the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.
The conference will develop a five-year action plan for further implementation of the Convention. The entire conference will also discuss future goals for Cambodia to chair and host the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on Mine Action in December 2024.
On behalf of Cambodia as the chair of the 2024 Summit, the Senior Minister outlined four priority action plans to be discussed, including: First, the promotion of the implementation of the Ottawa Convention; and second. Promote mine clearance work towards a landmine-free world. Third: Promote South-South Partnership and Cooperation;
Special Envoy of the Ottawa Convention Prince Mired Expresses Satisfaction with Hosting and Attending Cambodia's Third Global Conference and Prince Confirms Attendance at the Siem Reap-Angkor World Summit Mine-free in December 2024 as well.
