Understand the business: Japanese tilapia fish farmers expect to be able to export to Japan and Europe next year
According to Zhao Soursdey, the farmed tilapia raised by the farm is a local species, with a breeding period of six months. The fish caught per head weighs between 500 and 600 grams, leaving no larger size, because if it is too large, the meat will be too fat and too watery, which can make the fish meat. Loss of taste.
In particular, before taking the fish to be processed for meat, the fish must be caught from the pond and then kept in clean water for 3 days to get rid of the smell of soil and the smell of fish feed before processing.
The farm also has freezers and disinfectants imported from Japan. That is why fish meat is high quality and safe and can be eaten raw.
At present, the farm has 21 fish ponds, each pond is about 40 meters x 40 meters, and each pond raises about 10,000 tilapia fry and yields about 3 tons in each pond.
The aquaculture farm is supported by the Post-Harvest Fisheries Development Project (CAPFISH), a program that promotes sustainable and environmentally friendly fisheries growth and aims to support technical capacity, strengthen the private sector, and improve the competitiveness of food standards in Cambodia. To meet national and international needs.
