President Hun Manet said that the safety of Cambodian students in Israel is the highest priority of the Royal Government.
Samdech Hun Manet said that there are currently 452 Cambodian students present in Israel and so far all of them are safe, with strict protection by the relevant authorities and Israeli forces in In the area where they live as well as from the farm where they are staying and training.
He added that due to the changing situation in Israel, especially in the Gaza Strip, it was still unclear and to prepare for the event, he assigned the task force of the Royal Government of Cambodia to set up a temporary safe haven. In the south of Israel, it borders Egypt and Jordan, nearly 300 km from the Gaza Strip.
For students who wish to leave the area where they are staying and train for a while to safety, the Royal Government has provided transportation as well as responsibility for the accommodation and meals of all students there. .
The Royal Government team has informed all the students who are present in Israel. For students who wish to relocate to a temporary safe haven, please register online and confirm their volunteering.
As a result: As of 10:00 am on October 14, 2023 in Cambodia (which is 7:00 am in Israel), 422 students have registered online, 422 of them have decided Continue to stay in the area where they live and work normally and do not think it is necessary for them to relocate to a safe place provided by the Royal Government.
The Royal Government team will continue to monitor the situation in Israel as well as keep in touch with the students on a regular basis and be ready to assist you to ensure the safety of all of you, including mobility. From risk areas to safe areas as needed.
He reiterated his call on all Cambodians in Israel, especially students, to adhere to the instructions of the authorities there to ensure their personal safety.
Please keep in mind that the Royal Government of Cambodia does not leave you, but instead the Royal Government always strives to pay attention to your well-being by taking the necessary measures as much as we can. And in good cooperation with the Israeli authorities.
Finally, on the occasion of this traditional Pchum Ben, I would like to wish all my compatriots, especially the students who are present in Israel and their families, peace, safety and success in all endeavors. All.
