Samdech President Hun Manet calls on his compatriots and all stakeholders to take action to reduce disaster risk (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia October 13, 2023: Call on 4 points to compatriots and all stakeholders to participate in disaster risk reduction activities.
Samdech President Hun Manet appealed to the following compatriots:
First, continue to pay attention to contribute to the Royal Government in maintaining economic growth through smart investment, improve housing, business location to be safe, expand sustainable business to maintain stability, normal life in a new way with clean living. Good environment and safe villages and communes, as well as adherence to a shared culture.
Second, to promote a culture of transfer, acceptance and sharing of knowledge, skills and experience in disaster prevention and mitigation, and to continue to strengthen the capacity to understand disaster risk through attention, risk monitoring, forecasting information and Announce in advance about incidents and possible accidents.
Third, ministries, state institutions at both the national and sub-national levels must identify disaster management as their core work and strengthen the Disaster Management Secretariat, which is responsible for ensuring human resources, materials for work, and resources for responding and Post-disaster recovery.
And fourth, ministries, institutions and authorities at all levels continue to strengthen existing mechanisms, policies, strategies, programs, plans and activities by integrating disaster management and climate change to strengthen economic, social, health and environmental benefits.
