The Governor added that the temporary commissioning of the new cable-stayed bridge has been approved by the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration with the approval of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathip Hun Manet.
It should be noted that this bridge is 824 meters long, 24,506 meters wide, with 4 lanes, 2 lanes for cars, 1 lane for motorcycles and 1 lane for pedestrians.
The construction of Koh Nora Bridge was started on October 26, 2020, with an estimated cost of 35 months to build and at a cost of about 38 million US dollars, built by the Cambodian Overseas Investment Company OCIC under the management of the Capital Administration. Phnom Penh.
The bridge facilitates the movement of people from Chbar Ampov to the center of Koh Pich and to the center of Phnom Penh, which has been congested daily, although Phnom Penh City Hall has put a ferry for passengers to the bridge. This up to 4 units are still congested.
