According to the historical records of Cambodia, the Pchum Ben festival has existed since ancient times. But honestly, in the past it was not called Bon Pchum, in this ceremony they are divided into two classes. The first stage is to start from the 1st day until the 14th day, it is to find Phat (Phat follows the day) in a row.
The other class is held on the 15th of Roch, which is called Bon Pchum. These two festivals are now combined and called the Ben Pchum Festival.
In ancient times, this festival was held to prepare monks for the rainy season in the pagoda for three months from the day of the rainy season to the day of the rainy season.
According to ancient records, during the rainy season, heavy rains make it difficult for monks to roam. That is why the Buddhists organize this ceremony to supply the monks daily until the rainy day.
