(Phnom Penh): The Chinese-Cambodian Traditional Medicine Research Center of Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Preah Kosomak was officially inaugurated on October 12, 2023 under the chairmanship of Prof. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health. Mr. Wang Wintian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia and Ms. Yu Yanhong, Director of the National Administration of Traditional Chinese Medicine and other high-level delegates of the People's Republic of China.
The Minister expressed his gratitude to the Government of the People's Republic of China for initiating the establishment of this Chinese-Cambodian Traditional Medicine Research Center for the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Preah Kosomak after 19 months of construction.
On this auspicious occasion, the Professor expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of the People's Republic of China for building this noble achievement, and to the Director General of the National Administration of Traditional Chinese Medicine and His Excellency The Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia, as well as all delegates, have made every effort to encourage and fully support this work.
Ms. Yu Yanhong also pointed out that 2023 is the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations and the year of Cambodia-China friendship, China and Cambodia jointly celebrated and celebrated. In this context, the official launch of the China-Cambodia Traditional Medicine Research Center has become more meaningful after the recent joint statement between the Chinese government and the Royal Government of Cambodia last month.
She added, "On behalf of the National Administration of Traditional Chinese Medicine, I would like to extend a warm congratulations to the recipients of this center on both the Chinese and Cambodian sides. We would like to sincerely thank all the colleagues who have contributed and supported the traditional medicine cooperation between China and Cambodia, and would like to sincerely extend our sincere respect to the distinguished guests who attended this event.
In this context, the establishment of the Chinese-Cambodian Traditional Medicine Research Center not only helps to understand the important work of building new models and routes for Chinese Traditional Medicine Centers abroad, but also to deepen and contribute to the Sino-Cambodian friendship. Build a common destiny of Cambodia and China in the new era.
"Traditional Chinese medicine is a medical science that has been continuously developed and developed by people of all ethnic groups in China during life, production and long-term struggle against disease," she said. The Chinese government has always paid close attention to the development of traditional Chinese medicine.
