(Phnom Penh): About 70 Chinese business delegates representing 54 major companies from Shenzhen, Guangdong Province are interested in investing in tourism in Cambodia, especially in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap. There is a need for investment in new tourism products to attract more tourists.
On that occasion, Mr. Wang Xue and the Chinese business delegation from Shenzhen said that they are interested in investing in tourism in Cambodia, especially in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville as well as Siem Reap, while the Chinese business delegation also Visited these destinations for several days.
Mr. Wang Xer stated that the idea of wanting to do business, invest and establish cooperation in Cambodia was born out of the visit of His Excellency Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who visited China during the month. September 2023, in which the Prime Minister inspired investors and businessmen in China to seek investment opportunities in Cambodia.
He also asked the Chinese delegation to prioritize investment and increase tourism products and to help promote tourism destinations in Cambodia to Shenzhen and China as well as other international markets. Contribute to attracting more national and international tourists to Cambodia.
The Chinese delegation in Shenzhen supported Minister Sok Soken's request to promote Chinese tourism to Cambodia, requesting joint cooperation to promote Cambodia's tourism potential to Chinese people living in Shenzhen.
The Chinese delegation also requested the Minister and a delegation from the Ministry of Tourism to visit Shenzhen to strengthen tourism and strengthen cooperation between Cambodia and Shenzhen.
In response, the Minister will also push for the full operation of the Cambodia Tourism Promotion and Marketing Council to increase the participation of the private sector and other tour operators.
The Cambodian side also proposed connecting flights from Shenzhen to Cambodia, which is an important way to attract and transport tourists to Cambodia-Shenzhen, while Shenzhen destinations also have Chinese tourists. Visited Cambodia a lot, which ranks fifth among Chinese tourists visiting Cambodia.
