An agreement between the Export-Import Bank of China and Sri Lanka reached an agreement late last month, but the ministry did not provide details of the deal, Bloomberg reported. Agree this.
Officials from two creditor countries, who asked not to be identified, told Bloomberg they had not been informed of the terms and details of an agreement reached between Sri Lanka and China.
One of the two sources said the preliminary agreement between Sri Lanka and China was not expected to change the efforts of the official creditors' committee in trying to reach a debt agreement in Marrakech. Will include safeguards to prevent payment terms that are favorable to China.
An Indian official who attended the debt talks said New Delhi has been pushing for fair and equitable treatment of debt restructuring plans and hoped all creditors would be transparent in their approach. They.
According to IMF estimates, Sri Lanka owes China about 40 percent of its bilateral debt and India 16 percent. An early agreement with creditors will allow Sri Lanka to continue to receive funding from its $ 3 billion bailout program with the IMF.
The Ministry of Health recommends that private health professionals strictly adhere to professional ethics and request the capital-provincial authorities to help eliminate unauthorized health services.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has issued a new press release instructing all private health professionals to strictly abide by the Code of Professional Conduct and the Law on the Management of Health Professionals. Either avoid exaggerating or distorting the facts.
At the same time, the Ministry of Health has asked the capital-provincial authorities to help eliminate the provision of health services without permission from the Ministry.
A press release obtained by Fresh News this morning (October 12) states that the Ministry of Health has noticed the publication of health professionals by some individuals who do not have a medical science background and are accredited by the Ministry. The health or health professional body has been undermining the professional ethics of the health professionals and the public health.
In order to eliminate illegal health services, the Ministry of Health calls for the following:
* All private health professionals who open clinics, clinics, polyclinics must strictly adhere to professional ethics and the law on the management of health professionals properly and avoid exaggeration or Distort the truth.
* Each health professional committee must strengthen the management of relevant health professionals in accordance with its competencies set out in the Law on the Management of Health Professionals and strengthen the code of ethics for health professionals for the honor and dignity of Dignity of health professionals.
Local authorities in all capitals and provinces participate in instructing and preventing the provision of health services without permission from the Ministry of Health and commercial advertisements within the framework of health professions that do not have a clear scientific basis, exaggerate the facts, and cause confusion. To the people.
The Ministry of Health strongly hopes and believes in the careful participation of private health professionals and relevant authorities in preventing these inactions in order to avoid harm to the health and well-being of the people. Cambodia is highly responsible. World Vision Supports Positive Ministry of Environment Initiative on Changing Children's Behavior in Waste Management
Support for this initiative of the Executive Director of World Vision was made during a courtesy call on Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of the Ministry of Environment on the afternoon of October 11, 2023.
