Funan Techo Canal Project Discussed Between Inter-Ministerial Commission and Chinese Bridge and Road Corporation
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Peng Po, Minister of Public Works and Transport, as well as institutional leaders of the Inter-Ministerial Commission and technical officials from a number of Chinese bridges and roads corporations.
The revised Framework Agreement (FA), which is currently under review and signed, will further define the potential of the Funan Techo canal project through in-depth study on all relevant aspects. All economic and social benefits.
The Funan-Techo Canal Project is designed to expand the potential use of inland waterway transport in order to contribute to the further development of socio-economic activities and to provide appropriate solutions to challenges. And the obstacles of the waterway transport sector that we have been facing today.
Studies have shown that the Funan-Techo canal is 180 km long from the Takeo canal of the Mekong River, through the Ta Ek canal of the Bassac River, then into the Ta Hing canal of the Bassac River, Koh Thom district, and extends to the provincial sea. Kep passes through four provinces, including Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep, with a total population of 1.6 million people living on either side of the waterway.
The waterway is 100 meters wide at the top and 80 meters at the bottom and 5.4 meters deep (navigation depth 4.7 meters and safety gap 0.7 meters). 2 lanes can get in and out and avoid each other safely.
