The meeting also presented the project of the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon Ok Ambok this year, according to the plan of this year's Royal Ceremony will have more than 300 boats to race (Phnom Penh. There are more than 40 boats), there are about 20,000 players in the boat and more than 20 lanterns participated.
The accommodation for boaters is divided into two locations, one in the former depot in Russey Keo district and one in the east of the Tonle Sap in the OCIC development land north of the Neang Mcha roundabout, Chroy Changva district. These two will have a well-organized water, electricity and toilet network. "Water supply and flood reduction project in Prek Niel" worth about 100 million dollars will help improve the lives of people in Svay Rieng
(Phnom Penh): Meeting to review and discuss the draft report on the feasibility study of "Prek Niel Water Supply and Flood Reduction Project" in Svay Rieng province, supported by a grant from the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) in Cambodia. ) Was held on October 10, 2023 at Sofitel Phnom Penh to discuss the interim report of the feasibility study by collecting input from stakeholders.
Feasibility study of "Prek Niel Water Supply and Flood Reduction Project" supported by the Republic of Korea through KOICA with a grant of $ 2 million for two years from 2021 to 2023, while the cost of construction is About $ 100 million.
The workshop focused on key stakeholders and shared knowledge, experience and perspectives on agricultural water management, while the main agenda of the meeting included project costs and initial environmental and social impact assessments.
According to Mr. Ponh Sach, the report will be finalized at the end of next month and may meet again to discuss the report or submit it to development partners for approval and submit the report to K-Exim Bank. In the investment budget to be a loan contract.
"Svay Rieng is a resource-poor province, so we have to help with this project, otherwise people will migrate to find work," said Ponh Sachchak. So this project helps to create his business, he has irrigated land that he can farm twice a year. "His livelihood will be better because there is no water to harass him in the rainy season and enough water in the dry months to increase yields."
The Prek Niel Reservoir Water Supply and Reduction Project aims to reduce flood and drought damage, supply irrigation / household / industrial water supply, and increase agricultural productivity and efficiency.
Mr. Kim Savuth, Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, said that the project has a construction cost of 100 million dollars, study in 2023-24 and start implementation in 2025.
