Banteay Meanchey Provincial Armed Forces Sent a Suspect to Provincial Court for Proceedings Related to Illegal Storage and Use of Drugs
(Banteay Meanchey): On October 9, 2023, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Local Force, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Municipal Gendarmerie Local Commander, conducted an operation to crack down on cases of illegal possession and use of drugs. The body of a suspect with some exhibits at the Paramic Casino in Kbal Spean 2 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that before the crackdown on the Poipet City Gendarmerie, he received a report from the security guard of the Paradise Casino that there was a case of storing and using drugs immediately. The above suspects arrested the suspects and seized drug exhibits and brought them to the Poipet City Military Police Base for questioning and processing.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspect admitted that he had indeed stored and used illegal drugs. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the suspect was sent by the Municipal Gendarmerie to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command for further action.
Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of anti-drug work, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated the procedure. From Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
