Pchum Ben is an important Buddhist festival that Cambodians who are Buddhists always celebrate every year from the 1st of Roach to the 15th of Roach, divided into two classes. From the 1st of Roach to the 14th of Roach, the lunar month is Kan Ben and the 15th of Roach is the day of Pchum Ben.
Pchum Ben Ceremony All relatives, whether near or far, always travel to meet, especially parents in their hometown to prepare food and soup to give to the monks who live in the pagoda, these are A custom that has been practiced by Cambodians for a long time.
Samdech Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An and Mrs. Hang Pheary Im Sethy and the people invited to pay homage to the ancestors of the veterans who sacrificed their lives for the national cause and to the merits of the 7 relatives who passed away. He will pray for happiness at all times. Brother-in-law: The end of Duke Chheang Roth's life may be due to a mental crisis that broke up the family.
(Phnom Penh): The news of the death of Duke Chheang Rath, husband of Nuon Suntory, commonly known as Srey Oun, is a natural beauty that is shaking social media and leading to great shock and grief with the family of the deceased.
Authorities have confirmed that 40-year-old Duke Chheang Roth committed suicide by hanging himself at 2:50 pm on October 11, 2023 at 142, Street R12, Roseville Borey Peng Huoth Project, Veal Sbov Village, Sangkat Veal Sbov, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
Mao Sivorn, the brother-in-law of Duke Chheang Rath, described that before the incident, at 8:10 on October 11, 2023, he and his family went to celebrate in Prey Veng province, while his brother-in-law was Duke. Chheang Roth did not go with him, claiming to be busy going to Kampong Cham to see a Chinese teacher.
According to Mao Sivan, in the past, Duke Chheang Rath had a mental crisis, divorced his new family.
According to the police, the forensic experts concluded that the victim actually committed suicide by hanging himself with a hammock. The bodies of the victims are now being traditionally buried by their families at the house where the incident took place.
Please note that Duke Chheang Rath and Mrs. Nuon Suntory were married in 2017 and have a daughter as a bond.
