(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has announced an increase in the provision of additional allowances for pregnant women who are members of the National Assembly from August 1, 2023 to continue to support women during pregnancy, childbirth and after Birth until the baby is under 2 years old.
Garment factory worker Kuon Srey Touch, who came to give birth to her second child at Ang Duong Hospital with a PSC membership card, said she no longer had to pay for childbirth and hospital stay. He also received another 800,000 Riels from the Royal Government. The worker said that before giving birth, she also received 80,000 riel for a pregnancy test.
During the first nine months of 2023, more than 26,000 women came to Preah Ang Duong Hospital for prenatal check-ups and births, said Khuon Vandy. Ang Duong through the use of the S.S.S.
She stated that the UNFPA has provided a data automation program to the hospital, which is convenient for the hospital to enter the information of women to check and give birth in the hospital and send back to the UNFPA. Quick to pay government subsidies to pregnant patients.
Please note that after the pregnant woman has met the conditions. Will start receiving benefits in three stages, equivalent to 15 times, from pregnancy tests during childbirth to children under 2 years old.
* For the first stage, a woman who goes for four pregnancy tests, each pregnancy will receive 80,000 riels.
* The second stage at birth, which will receive an allowance of 800,000 Riels for one child, if in the case of twins receive an allowance of 1.2 million Riels, and if triplets will receive up to 1.6 million Riels Riel, as well as the direct allowance of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kattipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, an additional 5 million Riels.
