Prey Veng Provincial Administration Holds an Emergency Meeting to Prepare for the Prevention and Control of Avian Influenza
On the afternoon of October 10, 2023, Mr. Suon Somalin, Governor of Prey Veng Province, chaired an emergency meeting to prepare for the prevention of the spread of avian influenza in Prey Veng province. The meeting was attended by Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Governors, Departments around the provincial authorities of 13 districts of Prey Veng province.
On that occasion, Mr. Suon Somalin instructed the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to educate, guide, disseminate and prevent any movement of animals from one area to another and to conduct inspections to prevent the spread of bird flu from From region to region and from animals to humans.
At the same time, the provincial governor also introduced measures to prevent the spread of bird flu from bird to bird, from bird to bird, and in order to protect the lives of people, public health and social order, Prey Veng Provincial Administration would like to introduce to the Department Municipal, district, commune, sangkat and people in Prey Veng province must implement the following measures:
First, to strengthen the implementation of biosecurity measures in all poultry farms, poultry farms, poultry gathering places, poultry business places and poultry slaughterhouses, as well as establish surveillance and monitoring of bird health throughout the province and take timely action. In case of suspected bird flu.
Second, to increase the control of animal traffic and animal products in collaboration with local authorities at all levels and relevant authorities.
Third, to strengthen the prevention of the import of poultry and illegal poultry products that pass through the border and export, both outside the province and within the province or from one area to another, in cooperation with local authorities, especially the entry-exit authorities. Boundaries.
Fourth, all the circulation of birds and bird products from areas where there is an outbreak of bird flu or suspected bird flu, the competent authorities must conduct inspections in accordance with technical standards.
Sixth: Educate people not to eat sick or dead birds and all poultry for eating must be cooked well and wash their hands often with soap and water before eating and after direct contact with the poultry. Birds.
* 7, suspected cases of bird flu or people with fever over 38.5 degrees Celsius, cough, difficulty breathing and a history of contact with sick or dead poultry during the 14 days before the symptoms, please contact or report immediately Go to the nearest local authority.
In addition, Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Prey Veng Province, said that after receiving this information, he and his team and professional officers arrived at the location from 4 am to take shelter. All those animals to be tested for this bird flu.
In order to respond in a timely manner, the RRT-PHD-OD-HC team organized a working group to conduct educational activities to disseminate preventive measures through the distribution of micro-mobile education leaflets and health posts for follow-up from October 10. In 2023, there will also be active cooperation from the district governor, village chief, commune chief.
