According to the report, from January to September 2023, Cambodia's trade with the United States amounted to 7,078 million US dollars, of which Cambodia exported more than 6,897 million US dollars, down 2.1 percent. Imports were worth $ 181 million, down 27.8 percent.
The increase in Cambodia's exports to the United States confirms the improvement in trade between the two countries, and through these export figures, the United States has become an important export market for Cambodia.
Most of Cambodia's exports to the United States include clothing, travel accessories (suitcases, bags), bicycles, and other items. Cambodia imports from the United States such as cars, machinery, jewelry, cosmetics, electrical appliances and some consumer goods.
