This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech President Hun Manet announcing the official launch of the "National Strategy on Informal Economic Development 2023-2028" on the morning of October 10, 2023 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
He added that the people must be concerned about the rationale, contributions, penalties and obligations and benefits of entering the system. 2023-2028 also pays close attention to these issues to help people to target and do their best.
The Prime Minister explained, "This policy (National Strategy for Informal Economic Development 2023-2028) does not force informal people to participate in registration, but has the principle of encouraging registration through presentation. "Obviously the benefits for you to be more involved in this transition phase."
He stressed that the registration of the economy in this system is to provide the Royal Government with clear data, easy to set policies to support in a timely manner and especially in difficult times because the people of Cambodia. Faced with the same difficulties as when Kovid 19 already, and in the future there may be economic inflation and other problems, so the Royal Government will be easier to support people who do business.
It should be informed that the National Strategy for Informal Economic Development 2023-2028 has nine major incentives and favorable principles for small and medium enterprise owners if they are willing to register in the system economy, including:
First. Provide waiver of all fines and debts in 2023-2028 to medium and small enterprises through past non-compliance.
Second. Provide tax incentives for micro-enterprises for voluntary registration in 2023-2028 by waiving tax registration fees and update fees.
Third. Provide tax incentives for small enterprises for voluntary registration in 2023-2028 through: 1. Waiver of penalties and tax liabilities for non-compliance before registration 2 - Exemption Tax registration fee and update fee at the time of registration and 3- Income tax, income tax exemption and minimum tax for 2 years after registration.
Fourth. Provide tax incentives for medium-sized enterprises for voluntary registration in 2024-2025 through: 1-Exemption of penalties and tax liabilities for non-compliance before registration and 2-Exemption. Income tax, income tax exemption and minimum tax for 2 years under registration.
Fifth. Provide tax incentives for small and medium enterprises for voluntary registration in 2024-2025 by waiving the patent tax for 2 years after receiving the registration decision.
Sixth. Reduce the fee for providing business opening notice and registration of company book and payroll book for enterprise with less than 8 workers.
7th. Strengthen the self-inspection mechanism and strengthen the implementation of the inter-ministerial inspection team mechanism at the national level to ensure joint inspections at the same time and once a year (not more than once).
8th. Organize joint inspections and inspections at the same time and once a year at the sub-national level for all enterprises that have or have not registered or applied for licenses or permits.
9th. Establish legal standards, frameworks, mechanisms that provide legal status for small and medium enterprises, combined with benefits such as five-year exemption from administrative fees.
According to the Prime Minister, the launch of the "National Strategy for Informal Economic Development 2023-2028" is to contribute to the promotion of informal economic development in a sustainable and environmentally resilient manner. In Cambodia, the informal economy accounts for about 70 percent of total employment and 32 percent of GDP.
Introduction by Samdech Hun Sen President on the occasion of the official launch of the National Strategy for Informal Economic Development 2023-2028 this morning, October 10, 2023 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
He stressed that in implementing this national policy, the Royal Government will give high priority and assign the Ministry of Industry to act as a focal point in promoting the implementation and effective implementation of this national strategy for the benefit of the nation and the people. People.
According to Samdech Thep Dey, in order to succeed in implementing the "National Strategy on Informal Economic Development 2023-2028", the Royal Government has set out five strategic priorities:
1. Determining, adjusting and setting up mechanisms to facilitate access to the system: The Royal Government will deploy and strengthen management mechanisms and coordination between measures to be implemented by all relevant ministries and institutions to ensure safety and implementation; Editing procedures to the maximum.
2: Reduce the burden on compliance: The Royal Government will reduce the burden on compliance as much as possible, avoiding the establishment of many standards and strategies, and ensure predictability for both business and work.
3: Providing support and support to those who have entered the system: The Royal Government will strengthen and expand the scope of health equity fund as well as provide occupational safety support to provide health care to priority groups to be able to And be able to live in the system at a reasonable standard of living and not fall into poverty or risk life.
4: Capacity building and support for those who have entered the system: The Royal Government will improve the quality and ease of access to public services and other support, strengthening skills training, creating market access opportunities. Originally aimed at encouraging those who have entered the system to grow and be able to fully participate in the economy in the system.
