Samdech President Hun Manet: Both the economy inside and outside the system are Cambodians who demand the Royal Government to pay high attention (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia on October 10. This 2023 states that both the economy, both inside and outside the system, are Cambodians, which requires the Royal Government to pay high attention to help all of them.
This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Hun Sen presided over the official launch of the National Strategy on Informal Economic Development 2023-2028. This event was held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh this morning, October 10, 2023.
"Regarding informal and systemic work In the economic definition system, there are some different criteria, but what is the same is both offline and in the system," he said. But as Cambodian people, we have an obligation to work hard to help everyone, this is the main goal of the Royal Government.
Samdech President Hun Manet said that people outside the system, of course, his ability to earn a living, but he is also a big driving force for the national economy. Globally, more than 70 percent of job creation is informal, and in Cambodia, too, the scale of this consideration is important.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet stated that in the informal economy, according to the experience of the Royal Government, the people in this small informal economy are the most vulnerable people affected by economic problems and problems. Various crises.
"In the Kovid-19 era, we saw that the poor and the poor, especially those outside the system, were very vulnerable," he said.
Samdech President Hun Manet continued that the priority policy of the Royal Government since the 6th mandate and the previous mandate, and this 7th mandate is a priority goal for the Royal Government in implementing various measures immediately to help the people. Who live in poverty and hardship, which is an important principle.
Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet also said that in the past experience, the informal economy, problems due to unclear information management, so it is difficult to help people. Samdech continued that the management of this information to identify the people where and who to easily help.
Please be informed that "informal economy" means a system of trade or exchange of goods and services that is not required by law to be registered. The informal economy provides job creation, employment and income, but can have consequences for environmental management, food safety, tax collection and so on.
The official launch of the national strategy to help people outside this system, Samdech Prime Minister considered as the use of an arrow to shoot three animals, so as to reduce poverty and social inequality, strengthen economic and social resilience and promote growth. Economy.
The Prime Minister explained that the three animals that were shot by a single arrow were as follows:
First, reduce poverty and social inequality: Helping poor people to have a better life is to reduce the gap between the poor and those with a better life. Increase equitable development policies that promote poverty reduction.
Second, strengthening the socio-economic resilience: The informal and poor people are the most vulnerable, such as Kovid 19, the impact of inflation, so the government must find them to help them. Strengthen resilience by supporting protection policies and other benefits.
Third: Stimulate economic growth: Because the people outside the system is an important driver in the national economy, if the Royal Government helps them to grow, the national economy will also grow.
The Prime Minister added that although these strategic theories are good, but the actual results are important, so he instructed the relevant ministries and institutions to make efforts to successfully implement the "National Strategy for Informal Economic Development 2023- 2028. "
