This morning, Samdech Hun Sen Presides Over the Official Launch of the National Strategy on Informal Economic Development 2023-2028
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, October 10, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, presided over the official launch of the National Strategy. On Informal Economic Development 2023-2028. This event is held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
"Informal economy" means a system of trade or exchange of goods and services that is not required by law to be registered. The informal economy provides job creation, employment and income, but can have consequences for environmental management, food safety, tax collection, and so on.
"National Strategy for Informal Economic Development 2023-2028" is set out with the vision of informal economic development to grow and have access to the system and become an important driving force in improving the lives of the people. And can contribute to the maximum in achieving sustainable development, environment, resilience and crisis resilience.
This national strategy aims to enhance the protection and capacity building, productivity and resilience of the informal economy, as well as to promote and accelerate participation in the informal economy in order to ensure the resilience, predictability and advancement of the economy. Doing business, investing and doing business, occupation and livelihood in Cambodia.
To develop the informal economy in line with the above vision and objectives, this national strategy sets out the four main goals as follows:
The Informal Economic Development Strategy is one of the six priority policy programs of the new government.
These priority political programs are planned by the Royal Government to be implemented before the end of 2023 to ensure the benefits to the people.
