(Phnom Penh): Cambodia has been selected by the World Organization for Animal Health and the International Organization for Veterinary Medicine as a model country that has trained village veterinary agents according to world standards. Provides animal husbandry services and techniques in villages throughout the country.
"We are proud that the World Organization for Animal Health, as well as the International Organization for Veterinary Medicine, has chosen Cambodia as one of the countries in the world to conduct a study on the animal health training system," he said. In total, only four countries were selected for the study, including Cambodia, Burundi, Nigeria and South Sudan.
He said that the Village Animal Health Agency has played an important role in providing animal treatment services, vaccinations, and advice on local animal husbandry techniques that will help improve the livestock sector in Cambodia, help the family economy and National economy.
However, he noted that in recent years, animal health agents have declined significantly. Although the number of village animal health agencies is declining, the provision of services to village animal keepers is still good, despite some difficulties. Therefore, additional training of village animal health agents must be required to meet the needs.
Dr. Sorn San, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, said that the reason for the decline of village animal health agencies is because they are too old to continue to provide services, migration, change of occupation, especially in During the outbreak of Kovid 19 because livestock was reduced.
He added that while the number of village veterinarians has dwindled, more training is needed. Currently, about $ 19 million has been provided to development partners and the government to strengthen the training of village veterinarians.
According to Min Sophoan, in 2021, more than 9,000 village animal health agencies in Cambodia will provide animal husbandry services in villages across the country to reduce animal mortality and provide better breeding techniques. To help the family economy and the national economy.
However, he said that currently the village animal health agency does not have a regular training program yet. Therefore, he suggested that the government organize additional training programs regularly every three or five years to make them more aware of new diseases and promote the formation of associations so that they can be united.
