Mr. Chea Vandeth confirms his ambition to make mobile and internet services nationwide by 2024
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, on October 9, 2023, confirmed the Ministry's ambition to have telephone and internet services nationwide by 2024.
This confirmation was made on the occasion of Minister Chea Van Det's participation in the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on the construction of community technology centers in public high schools between the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Minister Chea Waddet stated, "In 2024, the Ministry has ambitions to make mobile and internet services available throughout the country Therefore, this telephone and internet service will help the digital revolution, The efforts of the Royal Government.
In addition, the Minister of Posts and Telecommunications said that without the telephone and internet service, the digital revolution would not be possible.
Minister Chea Van Det said that to build a digital government, economy, society and digital citizens is to build digital infrastructure, digital connectivity, set up digital technology and internet connectivity.
Minister Chea Vandeth said that the establishment of "Community Technology Centers" in public high schools is an important new catalyst with potential and potential to promote the development of a strong and conducive digital education ecosystem. Digital services in all fields.
Minister Chea Vandeth also said that the Ministry is currently reviewing the backbone network in the country, from Phnom Penh to all provinces, and is also monitoring from province to district to know about the network throughout. The country already has or remains, if any, is to be supplemented.
