The Embassy of Japan and the Ministry of Education find the winners of three groups of short films by Cambodian high school students to be screened at the Asia International Children's Festival 2023 in Japan
The discovery of the owner of this short film took place on the afternoon of October 9, 2023, on the occasion of the Embassy of Japan in collaboration with the Ministry of Education held the Asia International Children's Film Festival 2023 and the 12th Semi-Final Competition under the theme "What I want." With the participation of Ms. Sorn Marada, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information.
The three winning short films include:
First: The film titled "What I Want" produced by students from Pich Chenda High School, Battambang Province Second: The film entitled "What I Want Not for Myself" produced by students from Net Yong High School, Battambang Province, and the third: a film entitled "What I Really Want" produced by students from Sovanna High School, Takeo Province.
According to Rat Yaro, a representative of the first group of students from Pich Chenda High School, the selection of this short film is based on the true story of a boy who studied at Pich Chenda High School. For this story is to educate other young people to be good children, good students, good citizens in society.
Rat Yaro continued that on the occasion of going out to film in Japan as a Cambodian child, he was committed to spreading the sublime traditional culture of Cambodia to young people from other countries to better understand what is actually Khmer. The short film series "What I Want" features a pantyhose as well as a beautiful view of Cambodia.
2023 is the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Japan and Cambodia. The film competition will be an opportunity to build a bridge of friendship between Japan and Cambodia and further strengthen the bilateral relationship.
Please note that the purpose of this program is to select three best short films to compete in the Asian International Children's Film Festival among high school students from Japan and 10 other ASEAN countries, including East Timor.
Three teams of high school students with a total of nine members who won today's competition will be invited to Japan under the program JENESY2023 to participate in the finals of the festival in Joku Prefecture, Japan, which will take place on the 16th December 2023.
