China opposes and condemns actions that endanger civilians in Israel as well as in the Palestinian territories
BEIJING (Reuters) - China on Monday said it opposes and condemns any acts of violence against innocent civilians, both in Israel and in the Palestinian territories. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, October 9, 2023.
"China is deeply concerned about the recent escalation of the Israeli-Palestinian conflict," said Chinese Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Mao Ning. "Beijing is deeply saddened by the loss of life as a result of the violence and opposition, as well as condemns acts that endanger civilians."
"China opposes any action that escalates the conflict and destabilizes the region and hopes for a ceasefire and an end to the fighting as soon as possible," she said. Ms. Mao also called on the international community to play its role effectively and jointly promote efforts to ease the situation.
According to Mao, the way to resolve the Israeli-Palestinian conflict cycle is to resume peace talks, as the solution includes the implementation of a "two-state solution" and promote a comprehensive, accurate and speedy resolution of the issue. Palestine through diplomatic means so that the reasonable concerns of all parties can be guaranteed.
