Supreme Council of the Magistracy Releases Press Release on the Outcome of the 37th Session, Mr. Chiv Keng Nominated as President of the Supreme Court
(Phnom Penh): The Supreme Council of the Magistracy on the afternoon of October 9, 2023 issued a press release on the results of the 37th session under the highest presidency of His Majesty the King of Life Kingdom of Cambodia, President of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy.
The meeting reviewed and decided on seven agendas, the first of which was the decision to nominate Mr. Chiv Keng as the President of the Supreme Court.
The meeting considered, decided and consulted on 7 agendas with the following results:
Agenda 1: Review and decide on the appointment of the President of the Supreme Court and the decision on the transfer of the President, Vice President and some judges: The meeting agreed to nominate Mr. Chiv Keng as the President of the Supreme Court of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the transfer of the position of President 47 other Deputy Presidents and Judges at the Supreme Court, the Court of Appeal and the Capital-Provincial Court.
Agenda 2: Consultation on the transfer and appointment of prosecutors Some Deputy Prosecutors at the request of the Minister of Justice: The Meeting approved the transfer and appointment of 25 Deputy Prosecutors, Deputy Prosecutors and Deputy Prosecutors Pictures at the Attorney General of the Supreme Court, the Attorney General of the Court of Appeal and at the Attorney General of the Capital-Provincial Court.
Agenda 3: Review and decide on the request for 2 years unpaid leave of 1 Judge of Tbong Khmum Appeal Court: The meeting decided to allow Ms. Ros Bophana, Judge of Tbong Khmum Appeal Court to remain unpaid. Two (two) years from July 1, 2023 to July 1, 2025.
Agenda 4: Review and decide on the application to return to the original unit of Mr. Uth Samphors, former Deputy President of the Preah Sihanouk Court of Appeal: The meeting decided to allow Mr. Uth Samphos to return to the position of judge in the original unit and to nominate Position: Vice President of Preah Sihanouk Court of Appeal.
Agenda 5: Review and decide on the request for confirmation of 40 interns: Judges: Approved the request for approval of 40 interns by judges with the rank of Deputy Judge of the 4th level of the Judiciary from On June 24, 2023, he will be assigned to work at the Capital-Provincial Court.
Agenda 6: Consultation on the request for re-appointment within the framework of the Prosecutor for 16 Deputy Intern Prosecutors at the request of the Minister of Justice As the 4th Deputy Prosecutor of the Prosecutor's Office from June 24, 2023 and assigned to work at the Provincial Prosecutor's Office.
As a result, the meeting agreed to nominate as an intern judge and deputy prosecutor for internship and assign to internship in the court and the prosecutor of the provincial court.
Phnom Penh Capital Administration and General Department of Identification Hold a Registration Training Course by Notifying Health Centers to Officials
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration and the General Department of Identification of the Ministry of Interior this morning, October 9, 2023, opened a training course on the registration of civil status through the notification of health facilities using digital technology in 6 communes. Of Po Sen Chey District Administration, Phnom Penh.
The ceremony was presided over by Lt. Gen. Top Neth, Director General of the General Department of Identification, and Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
Separately, for the second time, this is a test run of civil registration through the notification of health facilities using digital technology in 6 communes of Po Sen Chey district.
The preparation of the new form is an important step towards strengthening the civil status management work (birth and death) in accordance with the Law on Civil Statistics, Statistics and Identification, which was promulgated on the 1st of this month. July 2023 and in line with the policy and vision of the Royal Government to modernize institutions and promote digitalization in public administration.
Once officially launched nationwide, the new form will facilitate citizens in applying for civil status documents and provide them with all the required documents in accordance with the purpose of the new law. "Registration ensures that everyone has a legal identity, guarantees respect for human rights, access to all kinds of services and is the basis for development planning and monitoring of social progress."
Ministry of Telecommunications and Ministry of Education jointly build community technology centers in public high schools
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, and Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, presided over the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on October 9, 2023. Construction of community technology centers in public high schools.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. and Mrs. leaders, civil servants, representatives of both ministries, as well as representatives of higher and higher education institutions, the private sector and the media, a total of about 270 people. The ceremony was held at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on the morning of October 9, 2023.
Ms. Hean Polyne, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, informed the objectives of the establishment of "Community Technology Centers" (CITs) in public high schools in Cambodia with three main visions:
(1): Participation in the implementation of the Pentagon Strategy - The first phase of the Royal Government, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, the Digital Economy and Social Policy Framework of Cambodia 2021-2035 and the Digital Government Policy of Cambodia 2022-2035 (2): Promoting Sector Industry Digital education and literacy; and (3): Supporting the digital human capital development process.
In addition, the principal of Hun Sen High School, June 1, said that through the initiative to establish a "Community Technology Center", the entire community will have the opportunity to acquire the necessary technology skills and services in the digital age.
Minister Chea Vandeth said that to build a digital government, economy, society and digital citizens through building digital infrastructure, digital connectivity, setting up digital technology, internet connectivity and the establishment of "community technology centers" in public high schools is a new catalyst. It is important to have the potential and opportunity to promote the development of a strong digital education ecosystem and to be conducive to digital transformation in all fields.
Minister Chea Vandeth emphasized that the signing ceremony really reflected the new progress between the two ministries in the digital transformation of education to continue to develop human resources, digital technology in building the economy and digital society. The wise leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron thanked the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications for initiating the establishment of Community Technology Centers to contribute to the promotion of literacy and digital skills and the integration of educational technology for digital education in both classrooms, schools and communities. Round.
In addition, this Memorandum of Understanding is very important in a timely and targeted manner that supports the development of digital education in order to promote growth, enhance productivity and the effectiveness of building the future of Cambodia's digital citizenship. This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron.
Please be informed that the construction of the Community Technology Center started at Hun Sen High School on June 1 in Param commune, Bati district, Takeo province, which is a leading high school in Bati district, Takeo province, and the high school principal received the second prize for good management throughout the country.
