This afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will preside over the closing of the filming of "Son Under the Full Moon Light"
The film "Son under the full moon", which is a historical film and reflects the struggles of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen in the cause of the motherland, has been completed.
The film "Son Under the Full Moon" is a film about the real life of Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit during the Lon Nol War, the coup d'etat of Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King, the escape into the Mackie forest during the genocidal period of Paul. Pot crosses the border into Vietnam to find patriotic forces to liberate the country from the Pol Pot regime.
This film shows the life story of Samdech Techo from his childhood, having to leave his parents and siblings in his hometown to study in Phnom Penh by staying with monks in Wat Neak Voan.
This historical film is about 52 episodes and took more than a year to shoot. The production team selected 103 key actors, at least 500 characters and 500 other troops to perform in the big scenes.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that the film related to this national historical event cost about 6 million US dollars to produce. The budget for the film is not the national budget.
