(Phnom Penh): Because of his love and desire to preserve traditional Khmer musical instruments, Chapey Oung Soeun used to hide his chapei on a palm tree during the Khmer Rouge era. In 2023, the elders will perform the chapei at the Chapey Dang Veng Festival all over the country.
Elder Chapey Oung Soeun said that he was 82 years old and that his ancient chapei was very old, 66 years old. The elder from Pursat province is the third winner of the Chapey Dang Veng National Festival, which was held in 2021.
Through Mr. Oung Soeun's chapei singing, the reason he wanted to keep this chapei was because of the slogan, "Culture is extinct." He was very happy to show his ability on such a big stage.
Please be informed that Chapey Dang Veng Theater is often held as a cultural event which is important to contribute to the preservation and promotion of Chapey Dang Veng Art, one of Cambodia's oldest intangible cultural heritage and intangible cultural heritage. Of humanity to remain immortal in the heart of every Cambodian child in order to maintain the rules of the Chapey Dang Veng art form to survive and prosper in the future.
In addition, the festival also provides an opportunity to learn from each other to strengthen the capacity and quality of the profession of Chapey Dang Veng artists to preserve the Chapey Dang Veng art form to ensure the succession of the next generation. And can take advantage of this sector to contribute to the development of the national economy and serve the needs of the masses.
