The AIDS Health Care Foundation Celebrates International Girls' Day 2023 under the theme "Expanding the Voices of Girls"
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian AIDS Health Care Foundation (AHF) has celebrated International Girls' Day (IGCD) 2023 at Kork Panchan High School, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh under the theme "Expanding the Voice of Girls" in order to empower Girls to take control of their lives and health and call on government leaders to promote more programs for girls and review policies that create equality for women and girls.
International Girls' Day (IDGC) 2023 was held on the morning of October 7, 2023 in the presence of Mr. Siv Sean, Deputy Director of General Education Office of Phnom Penh Department of Education, Youth and Sports, Dr. Chhim Sarath, Regional Director, Asia Foundation Health care for people living with HIV / AIDS and the participation of the principal, teachers, including 300 students.
Dr. Chhim Sarath said that the International Girls' Day 2023 is also to remind us that it is our responsibility to provide for the girls that they must receive and work together to Their lives are happier. When girls are given the opportunity to grow, it not only changes their lives, but also makes the community grow.
Girls and young women make up more than 50 percent of all people living with HIV worldwide, he added. They are also among the more than 500 million people who endure poverty, including harmful stigma and access to inadequate facilities and hygiene products that hinder their success.
Arrest of a mastermind who illegally encroached on state forest land in Stung Treng province
(Stung Treng): A mastermind was arrested by the joint police force at the location of the encroachment on state forest land in Ibo village, O'Svay commune, Borey O'Svay Sen Chey district.
During the inspection of the encroachment on state forest land, the joint police force arrested a person named Ouk Leak, male, 44 years old, Khmer nationality, farmer, his hometown is Sop village, Sop commune, Prek Prosop district. Kratie province, the mastermind of encroaching on tens of hectares of state forest land.
According to Ouk Leak's confession, the land above was previously encroached on with an area of 300 meters by 500 meters equal to 15 hectares at UTM 0636575 1532396 near O Khleang in Ibo village, O'Svay commune, Borey O'Svay Senchey district, Stung Treng province.
According to the forces operating directly, the crackdown on the above case is a joint effort on behalf of the Provincial Commission for the Suppression of Natural Resources Offenses in accordance with Circular No. 05.
After confessing to illegal encroachment on state forest land, the Forestry Administration decided to build a case under Article 97. It is punishable by a first-degree forestry offense punishable by five (5) to ten years' imprisonment. 10) years.
The suspect was sent to court according to the procedure.
