Cambodia Condemns Outbreak of Fighting in Israel and Calls on the International Community to Seek Negotiations (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, has expressed its deep regret over the outbreak. The fighting on October 7, 2023 in Israel.
In a statement issued on October 8, 2023, the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs urged the international community to redouble its efforts to facilitate meaningful dialogue and dialogue towards a stable and just peace. All parties need to engage in constructive dialogue to resolve the root causes of the conflict and find a solution that is acceptable to all parties.
In this statement, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stressed the importance of prioritizing the pursuit of peace, justice and security for all people in the region. All stakeholders need to work together to find a peaceful solution that ensures well-being and security for all.
The State Department also noted that the horrific escalation of violence had claimed the lives of hundreds of innocent people, including a Cambodian student in Israel. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation extends its deepest condolences to the families of the bodies of both sides who have lost loved ones.
Considering the safety of all civilians, including the Cambodian people, as a top priority, Cambodia calls on all parties to exercise the utmost restraint and seek ways to reduce violence and move towards a ceasefire with a focus on Protect civilian lives and adhere to international humanitarian law. Cambodia condemns all forms of violence and acts of terrorism.
