Today is Ben 9! Discover the history of Pchum Ben and Kan Ben, which are the traditions of the Khmer people
In ancient times, this festival was held to prepare monks for the rainy season in the pagoda for three months from the day of the rainy season to the day of the rainy season. According to ancient records, during the rainy season, heavy rains make it difficult for monks to roam. That is why the Buddhists organize this ceremony to supply the monks daily until the rainy day.
