The following is the Royal Decree: In the first eight months of 2023, Cambodia will create nearly 60,000 jobs.
The presence of this new enterprise may indicate that investors have confidence in the policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as a vision for business potential in Cambodia.
It should be noted that as of September 2023, there are 17,684 registered factories in Cambodia with a total of nearly 1.5 million workers, including factories in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products industries. There are 1,337 bags with a total of more than 830,000 workers.
As the Prime Minister of Cambodia in the seventh mandate, His Excellency Hun Manet also confirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia will hold a meeting with the private sector in November to improve the investment and business environment in Cambodia to increase competitiveness. And attract more investment capital and create new jobs for people.
In June 2023, the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) issued a sub-decree on the implementation of the Kingdom's investment law. Cambodia, which will provide an investment environment and the establishment of an open, transparent, predictable legal framework that is favorable for investment for socio-economic development.
At the same time, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is also pursuing the direction of maintaining and increasing employment and employment at home and abroad. On October 3, 2023, during a meeting with garment factory workers in Meanchey and Dangkor districts, HE Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, also presented the priority work progress that the Ministry must implement in 2023. Also.
In that, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training confirmed that it has set up a working group to develop a mechanism to evaluate and determine the criteria "an enterprise is a safe community" by consulting and cooperating with social partners to launch a competition campaign from 2024. This program will help motivate factories to increase competition in both the work environment and productivity in each factory.
