(Kampong Chhnang): Pity a grandmother who tried to save a little money to celebrate and solve her daily life and to buy medicine to cure herself, but was stolen in the blink of an eye, which made her feel sad Too much because the money he has been trying to save for months and years is gone.
Pot Nonn, 78, is a disabled woman who has been bedridden for more than five years and has been living with her granddaughter for more than five years. She asked her nephew to adopt her since she was a child. She now lives in Aleng village, Chrey Bak commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province.
She never dared to spend foolishly, for when she had a bad emergency, she got a little money to solve it. Taking this opportunity, she and her granddaughter also requested the authorities to help with the search, lest they find the person and get some money back to her, in this case, she did not blame anyone. This is the fault of the grandmother and granddaughter themselves who are negligent.
Separately, every time the gift was given to her, the commune authorities and the director of the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Former Youth and Youth Rehabilitation also came to register her to make a disability card for the payment of government subsidies twice. But it has been almost two years now and she has not received the card yet.
