Kan Ben Pchum Ben is one of the most important ceremonies in Buddhism since ancient times to provide an opportunity for the surviving descendants to dedicate their merits to the ancestors who passed away to the next world and to prosperity. Glory, which comes from its benefits, that is, believing in karma, merit and sin.
