Cambodia receives 175 industrial investment projects worth 1,800 million USD, an increase of 43 projects in the first 9 months
(Phnom Penh): In the first nine months of 2023, Cambodia received 175 investment projects in the industrial sector with an investment of 1.8 billion US dollars, an increase of 43 projects compared to 2022.
According to the Council for the Development of Cambodia, in the first nine months of 2023, it has approved companies to invest in 191 new projects with an investment of 3.7 billion riels, including 175 investment projects in the industrial sector. $ 8 billion, an increase of 43 projects compared to 132 in 2022.
Notable big projects are the project to build all kinds of steel plants of HUALE STELL, which is located in the special economic zone of the port of Sihanoukville with an investment of $ 40 million and can create 523 jobs.
Neak Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told Fresh News that this is a good sign that Cambodia has received increased investment in industrial projects at a time when the global economy has not improved, which shows the attractiveness of Cambodia to foreign investors and attract investors of the leadership in this mandate.
He observed that some investment projects are in the non-garment manufacturing sector, such as car assembly plants, electronics factories, tire factories, bicycle manufacturers and other components. Non-garment manufacturing investment projects are investments that help sustain the Cambodian economy to be strong and sustainable.
At the same time, investment in the mining and agro-industry has also increased significantly.
He added that through the visit of His Excellency Hun Manet to other countries, which met with various investors will be able to attract more foreign investment.
