Mr. Chhay Sophal successfully defends his PhD on "Facebook Influence in Cambodian Politics and Society"
(Phnom Penh): After defending in front of the evaluation committee with 7 PhDs, including Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, and Dr. Khek Virak, Director of the Cabinet of the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia. Mr. Chhay Sophal successfully defended his thesis on the afternoon of July 6, 2023 at the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
After studying for one year at the Royal Academy of Cambodia and studying and writing in accordance with the requirements of the Royal Academy of Cambodia for another 3 years, Mr. Chhay Sophal was finally successful on This.
Please note that among the more than 90 students in the 4th generation, Mr. Chhay Sophal is the second doctoral candidate who has successfully completed his doctorate.
Mr. Chhay Sophal, who is also the author of a well-known book, described that getting a doctorate at the Royal Academy of Cambodia was not easy, and he was very proud of what he could do, no matter how busy he was. Trying and being patient and managing your time well can lead to success.
He added that the thesis on "Facebook Influence in Cambodian Politics (2008-2021) - Case Studies in Phnom Penh" is a new and hot topic in Cambodian society and that this thesis is designed to analyze The influence of Facebook on politics and some social issues, as well as some other positive and negative effects on individuals, groups and society in Cambodia between 2008-2021.
As for the merits, Mr. Chhay Sophal has divided 392 titles into bibliographies, including: - Documents in Khmer: 13 titles, 63 research reports, 2 speeches, 201 articles, 14 articles, 14 Facebook accounts. Foreign language documents include: 12 books, 44 research reports, 39 newspapers and 3 Facebook social media accounts.
At the same time, the thesis also shows the results of Facebook's influence on law enforcement initiatives, law amendments, law enforcement and law enforcement, as well as law enforcement restrictions.
Based on the results of the research and conclusions in this thesis, Mr. Chhay Sophal made the following recommendations:
* For politicians and political activists
On the other hand, both politicians and political activists need to understand the literacy of the media and the literacy of the media and to be aware of false information, fake news, fake news and misinformation to avoid misunderstandings and confusion among the masses and Instigate social unrest and expose the dangerous issue of this information to political supporters and voters, as well as the general public.
* For political supporters, voters and the general public
Like many politicians and activists, use Facebook as well as other social media sites properly and take into account legal issues, increase your personal morale and do not take Facebook and other media. Other societies act as a haven for attacking and insulting each other.
Using Facebook and other social media without understanding the law can also lead to harassment, loss of honor and dignity, and can lead to fraud, loss of property, loss of political and economic benefits.
* For State Public Service Officers, Civil Servants and the Armed Forces
* For citizens
In addition, do not be quick to believe and get angry when you see bad messages related to yourself, your family and friends on Facebook, because the fake information of social polluters have been attacking Facebook and Social media. Before responding, consult and think carefully to avoid any loss, such as fraud, loss of property, loss of political and economic benefits.
* For professional journalists
* For national and foreign civil society officials and social activists
