The highlight of these significant achievements is the celebration of the 30th anniversary of the promulgation of the Constitution under the highest presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia.
His Excellency Dr. M. Chhun Lim highlighted the important achievements, including: 1. Cambodia maintains and respects the Constitutional monarchy, 2. Liberal democracy is the foundation of modern political order in Cambodia. Cambodia emerges as a society governed by the rule of law, a state that abides by the Constitution and the law;
His Excellency Dr. M. Chhun Lim described the following important achievements as follows:
The monarchy is closely linked and enhances the religion, culture, traditions and good traditions of the Kingdom of Cambodia for thousands of years. His Majesty the King and the Constitutional Monarchy have received the highest respect from all national institutions and the deepest allegiance of the Cambodian people throughout the country so that he can abide in the cold shadow of the nation as a symbol of national unity. And national sustainability.
Principle 1: The Khmer people are the masters of the destiny of the nation, all power belongs to the people, used through the National Assembly, the Senate, the Royal Government and the Tribunal. The three branches of government have separate powers, the legislature and the executive have the principle of balancing each other: the National Assembly gives confidence to form the Royal Government. In 12 months.
Principle 2: Cambodia operates a multi-party electoral system by maintaining multi-party diversity as a space for political freedom and ensuring participation in elections.
Standard Principle 3: Liberal, multi-party democratic politics has been rooted in Cambodian political culture and is evolving step by step as follows:
Step 1: National power is divided into sub-national levels to promote and promote sub-national democratic development based on the fundamental principles of respect for human rights and pluralistic liberal democracy.
Step 3: The National Election Committee has been reformed to a constitutional institution. In order to ensure trust in the diverse composition of the National Election Committee, the party with seats in the National Assembly shall be the direct organizer of the composition of this Committee and vote for confidence.
Step 4: This is a step to strengthen the order of political parties by defining the red line regarding the obligations of each political party to respect the Constitution and the law.
Step 5: In order to strengthen the spirit of patriotism by determining the qualifications to have only one Khmer nationality by birth for the position of the top leader of the national constitutional institution.
Step 6: To fill the gaps in the constitutional procedure to ensure that the nation's top institutions, especially the executive, operate smoothly and sustainably.
3: Cambodia is a society of the rule of law, a state that abides by the Constitution and the law.
* Principle 2: The judiciary is an independent authority that has the power to adjudicate all cases related to civil criminal cases, including administrative cases.
Issue 1: The progressive nature of the Constitution and the global trends of the new laws of Cambodia, which are influenced by the multicultural, global and highly technical nature, really require time for continuous and consistent interpretation through the strengthening of the education mechanism. Training (including inclusion in the curriculum on the basic principles of the Constitution) and dissemination to all relevant institutions to the masses.
Second, the level of general understanding of justice within the legal framework may remain challenging in practice due to the rapid political, economic and legal developments, while the public's limited awareness of legal rights regarding Use its power through the tribunal, which can lead to social justice gaps.
4: Cambodia implements the market economy system as a state, respects the protection of private property and social justice
The Kingdom of Cambodia implements a market economy by recognizing, respecting and protecting the private property regime. The state pays attention to implementing and promoting the policy framework for privatization, open trade, and promoting domestic and foreign investment by actively participating in regional economic integration and globalization, especially through ASEAN membership and the World Trade Organization. Mr.
Based on the fundamental principles of the market economy and the spirit of the Constitution, the private sector is considered a driving force, a development partner and the engine of economic growth, with the state acting as a regulator. In this role, the state builds laws and policies to promote development, promote entrepreneurship, fair competition, and provide hardware and software infrastructure, along with the private sector.
Please be informed that the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia is a historical achievement approved by the Constitutional Assembly on September 21, 1993, which His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk signed the Royal Kram.
The Constituent Assembly has re-established the traditional Khmer values (national, religious, monarchy) accompanied by fundamental modern constitutional values (democracy, human rights, rule of law), fully incorporating and detailing the contents of Annex 5. Of the Paris Peace Agreement.
The harmonization of the two values has created a cohesive and cohesive force in resolving political and legal issues while maintaining social harmony. The constitution has been amended 10 times and an additional constitution has been enacted to meet the real needs of society.
This statement was made on the occasion of the 30th anniversary of the promulgation of the Constitution by His Majesty the King on the morning of October 6. 2023.
The King expressed his deepest gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, the great and talented co-founder, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who took the initiative. To prepare the draft of the 1993 Constitution.
He said that after the draft was ready, a high-level delegation led by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo, including some members of the Legal Council, visited the Royal Palace in August 1993. Pyongyang of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea to pass on the latest knowledge about His Majesty the King Father of Cambodia "His Majesty the King" is the highest deity.
His Majesty the King of Life on Stone added that this co-founder is the supreme figure of our nation mentioned above, and some other dignitaries are still alive and some dignitaries have died and Already dead. Please respect the souls and souls of those dignitaries, go to death.
At the same time, he firmly believes that under the umbrella of the Constitution, all national institutions will continue to fulfill their duties with high responsibility to ensure the development of our nation to achieve the 2030 National Development Goals. And by 2050, become a strong and prosperous country, the Cambodian people will have a prosperous and prosperous life, live in peace, stability and eternity.
