This morning, His Majesty the King celebrated the 30th anniversary of the promulgation of the Constitution
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, October 6, 2023, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, pays homage to His Majesty the King wishes the King to celebrate the 30th anniversary of the promulgation of the Constitution.
During the ceremony, the King of Cambodia was invited by the Supreme Leader of the National Institution, Samdech as a national dignitary, Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, as well as leaders of the Royal Government and other relevant institutions. .
Please note that the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia during the Second Kingdom was 30 years old on Sunday, September 24, 2023. But the Constitutional Council has postponed the celebration to October 6.
After the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991, which was the result of negotiations between two Cambodian political figures, Samdech Norodom Sihanouk (His Majesty the King) and Samdech Hun Sen (then Comrade Hun Sen), Cambodia became aware of The first multi-party liberal democratic elections after more than three decades of civil war.
The first legislative elections took place from 23 to 28 May 1993, and a Constituent Assembly was established on 14 June 1993 to draft the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The first task of the Constituent Assembly at that time was to approve the establishment of the "Standing Committee for the Preparation of the Constitution" on June 30, 1993. After the drafting, the new Constitution was approved by the Constituent Assembly on September 21, 1993 at its second session and was signed into law by King Norodom Sihanouk, former King of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Official on September 24, 1993.
To date, the 1993 Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia has been amended 10 times by the National Assembly.
