WASHINGTON, Oct. 4 (Xinhua) - US President Joe Biden has admitted that he is concerned that the US political crisis could jeopardize military aid to Ukraine. While the United States is facing a domestic political crisis in Ukraine and its European allies, it is also concerned that the United States will not be able to afford or provide additional assistance to Ukraine in the future.
At the moment, this fear can only be a fantasy, as most politicians from the two major US parties continue to support Ukraine. However, it cannot be ruled out that this dream will not come true, especially after it was seen that both houses of Congress could keep the US government from escaping the shutdown. Suspension of new military aid to Ukraine.
Of course, one of the first things that may happen is that the balance on the battlefield in the Ukrainian war will change dramatically. Ukraine will not give up easily because what they are doing is "fighting for the life of the nation." But because Ukraine relies so heavily on military aid from the Pentagon, whether it wants to or not, it could put Ukraine in a difficult position.
Under this woman, China and Russia could use their diplomacy in neutralizing US allies and allies, sending a message: "Will the United States encourage the resistance until the rest of Ukraine? "Afghanistan is the last country, but eventually the United States will leave you in the limelight."
