(Kampong Chhnang): Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department this morning, October 5, 2023, officially launched a campaign to provide cervical cancer vaccine to 9-year-old girls throughout the province.
This campaign from October 5, 2023 onwards is also a new drug in addition to the 11 vaccines that the Royal Government has given to children across the country for free. Fees.
Taking this opportunity, the doctor also thanked the Royal Government of Samdech Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for his efforts to consider public health and bring a variety of vaccines to infants to children. 9 years old nationwide free of charge.
He also said that the cervical cancer vaccine, which is given in private hospitals, costs from $ 70 per needle.
On behalf of the parents and guardians of children throughout Kampong Chhnang province, he would like to thank the provincial governor, the Minister of Health, especially the Prime Minister, for always thinking about the well-being of the people by bringing this important health vaccine. People all over the country as well as people in Kampong Chhnang.
The Deputy Governor appealed to all parents and guardians of children to bring their children to get vaccinated by the National Immunization Program for everyone in schools, health centers or through the vaccination staff in the village according to the plan and By appointment of a health worker.
He stressed that all parents need to understand that this vaccine against cervical cancer will bring happiness to your baby for life. We take care of our children, we always want to see our children healthy, beautiful and happy, but when your child has cervical cancer, then everything will be lost, not to mention the beauty is completely lost.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor also encouraged officials, health workers and all development partners to work together to protect the health of all children in Kampong Chhnang.
The parents and guardians of the students who brought their children to be vaccinated against cervical cancer on that occasion also thanked the Ministry of Health for making the right and historically important decision to provide cancer vaccines. Cervical to a 9-year-old girl as a major preventive strategy towards the complete elimination of cervical cancer in the future.
They also expressed their deepest gratitude to Samdech Hun Sen, who was receiving a lot of work and support from the people in taking the lead from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the outstanding guide of Cambodia.
