Samdech Moha National Assembly President Khuon Sodary Appointed Mr. Mith Ty Mean, Deputy Director of the Cabinet, to Hold the 7th Blessing Ceremony at Wat Vimean Techea
(Phnom Penh): National Assembly President Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, has appointed Mr. Mith Ty Mean, Deputy Chief of Staff of the National Assembly President, to hold the 7th Ben Blessing Ceremony at Wat Vimean Techea, Wat Srah Chak, Srah Chak District, Daun Penh Phnom Penh on the afternoon of Thursday, October 5, 2023.
The ceremony was held in the Buddhist tradition by Mr. Mith Timan and many participants, including leaders, members of the Cabinet of the National Assembly, advisers, secretaries, as well as close relatives and Buddhists at the pagoda. Offering sacred objects, offerings, candles, incense, and flowers to the Preah Ratanatray, and performing rituals, listening to monks, chanting, and performing sermons.
Tomorrow morning, Friday, October 6, the 7th Kan Ben turn, HE Mith Timan and his team will bring food, alms and counting equipment to the monks to dedicate to the meritorious soul. Ancestors, ancestors who have passed away.
