General knowledge: The formation of the oceans on Earth
The role of the oceans The oceans play an important role in the Earth's environmental requirements and are also an important component of water bodies. Ocean evaporation is the largest source of air pollution, and ocean temperatures also determine the weather and winds on Earth. Life took place in the oceans about 3 million years before the appearance of life and plants on land, and the oceans were also an abundant source of oxygen.
