(Battambang): The General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs has cooperated with the Secretariat of the Battambang Provincial Drug Control Committee to organize a training course on "Strengthening the Capacity of Frontline Law Enforcement Officers" for Drug Enforcement Officers from Battambang Province. Banteay Meanchey, Pailin, Pursat and Koh Kong provinces.
The ceremony was held in the presence of General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Mr. Soeum Bunrith, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province. This training course is supported by the Office of the Thai Drug Control Board ONCB through the 2023 LOA project.
The General outlined the objectives of the training, including:
General Meas Virith wants to harmonize the community on the fight against drugs in the community, to have cooperation, support each other, eliminate discrimination and stigma, rescue drug addicts together, crack down on drug crime and eliminate Inactive in the local. In order to achieve timely and effective measures, General Meas Virith raised the slogan "3 Do 1 Report":
First, do not get involved means do not trade, distribute, do not be a backbone, do not conspire and do not use drugs - Do not secondly do not intervene means do not prevent the implementation of the law against drug criminals, even family, relatives or friends Third, do not excuse the meaning, do not relax the law enforcement for drug criminals.
General Meas Virith also continued to promote the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats, increase public forum activities and strive to make people more aware of the effects of drugs. In addition, continue to educate and encourage drug addicts to stop using and encourage them to seek treatment and rehabilitation in a timely manner.
General Meas Virith also requested all participants to take the knowledge and experience gained from today's training to disseminate to colleagues and turn into practical activities to increase and strengthen the work in accordance with the work direction of Deputy Prime Minister Neth. Savoeun, President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, and the high-level leadership recommendations of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who set out five key priorities.
