(Battambang): The Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Battambang Province organized the "Cambodian Elderly and International Day of the Elderly, October 1, 2023" under the theme "Helping the Elderly, Helping All of Us", the first Cambodian Elderly Day. 25th and 33rd International in the morning of October 5, 2023 at the meeting hall of the department.
The event was attended by Mr. Pheng Sethy, Deputy Governor, Representative of Mr. Sok Loo, Governor of Battambang, Mr. Phuong Sith, Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Battambang, Mr. Tum Vira, Director of the Cambodian Organization of the Elderly, relevant government officials and the elderly, attended by about 100 people. .
Mr. Tum Vira said that the Cambodian Organization for the Elderly has always cooperated and taken care of the director of the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Battambang Province by establishing the Association of the Elderly in some districts in Battambang province.
In Battambang province, there is the highest number of elderly people in the fifth place of all provincial capitals in Cambodia. In addition, the organization has cooperated with the Department of Social Affairs to establish associations for the elderly in eight provinces, including Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Tbong Khmum, Banteay Meanchey, Preah Vihear and Phnom Penh, with a total of 240 associations.
Mr. Pheng Sethy said that "Cambodian and International Day of the Elderly, October 1, 2023" organized by the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Battambang on October 5, 2023, on behalf of the provincial administration, please support and cooperate to create Characteristics on the work of the elderly in their lives.
He expressed his sincere congratulations as well as deep gratitude to the Cambodian elders throughout the country for their active contribution to the cause of territorial integrity, social development and especially a rare resource that can be mentioned. That the elderly are a living legacy that we can all rely on and seek help in the intellectual, spiritual, historical and social experiences of each society.
It should also be noted that in Cambodia, we have a good traditional culture that all children must care for and reward those who have ancestors, such as grandparents, parents who have shown great gestures for example. To the next generation.
In this regard, in order to express our gratitude to the precious merits of the elderly who have left behind many achievements and legacies, the Royal Government of Cambodia has been focusing on the work of promoting the welfare of the elderly, which aims to The elderly people in the country live well and have a high quality of life.
At the same time, the Royal Government has developed a number of policies that support and promote the elderly, such as the National Population Policy 2016-2030, the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025, the Health Care Policy and the National Health Strategy. For the health care of the elderly in 2016.
In particular, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has launched the "National Policy on the Elderly 2017-2030", which has been revised from the old 2003 policy. This is a valuable achievement for all of us Cambodians, especially the elderly.
In order to make these policies more valuable and better, it requires the joint participation of all relevant ministries, departments and institutions in implementing these policies in accordance with the guidelines of the Royal Government. Respond to the needs of the elderly at the grassroots level.
This is the most important thing for all of us to participate in. In addition, the Royal Government has established the Cambodian Sub-Committee for the Elderly in all capitals and provinces, with the provincial governor as the honorary chairman and deputy governor. Chairman and Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation as Permanent Vice President.
However, the intellectual challenges of the elderly in the country, especially in Battambang, remain a concern that we must all pay the utmost attention to and participate in finding appropriate ways to address those issues. Effectively and efficiently.
