First: Student Outcomes: Students' learning outcomes should be taken as a basis and Khmer language, mathematics and science subjects should be given priority.
Second, teaching and learning: To develop additional curricula such as: foreign language teaching, computer, basic life skills, and to organize after-school programs such as youth development programs, community and environmental volunteer programs, strengthen discipline and ethics, ethics and good behavior. Good educators and students.
Third, the involvement of the community and parents: Please call on parents, guardians and the community to help promote student learning and prevent school dropouts, and to encourage all children to attend school.
Fourth, the operation of the school administration: internal inspections and technical meetings, and the management and teachers are trained regularly.
Fifth: School Accountability: Teachers must adhere to professional ethics, teach at all hours according to the curriculum, and national and sub-national units must monitor schools to support and provide effective training to support Teachers.
In addition, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, on behalf of the Royal Government, also requested all guardians to be more active in educating their children to have good manners, to be worthy of the Khmer people with high civilization, virtue, morality and ethics, and to be grateful to him. Teachers who have trained Cambodian children to have knowledge, skills, abilities and talents as well.
Cambodia, Thailand plan to expand customer credit information sharing cooperation to promote more efficient lending
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia and the Central Bank of Thailand plan to expand cooperation to share customer credit information with each other to promote responsible and efficient lending.
Discussions at the meeting focused on the promotion of cooperation between the two countries in the past and the exchange of views on new initiatives to further expand cooperation to contribute to the growth of the banking sector and The economies of both countries.
Dr. Chea Serey said that the National Bank of Cambodia and the Central Bank of Thailand have strengthened good cooperation in many areas, such as exchanging visits, sharing experiences on professional work, receiving scholarships for National Bank of Cambodia officials to study. Higher education in Thailand and especially cooperation on cross-border payment system connectivity.
"Thailand is, in fact, the first country in Cambodia to have integrated cross-border payment and remittance systems, which has significantly contributed to supporting trade, investment and tourism in both countries," he said. Increase the use of national currency in the market in line with the goals of the ASEAN Economic Community.
She added that both central banks have been developing remittance systems for Cambodian workers working in Thailand to make transfers to families in Cambodia safer, faster and cheaper.
She also mentioned plans to expand cooperation for the sharing of consumer credit information between Cambodia and Thailand to promote responsible and efficient lending. As the two countries 'financial sectors continue to develop rapidly, the governor is optimistic that the two countries' central banks will continue to expand even richer cooperation in the future.
He added that this has not only strengthened the banking and financial system in Cambodia, but also contributed significantly to enhancing cooperation between the two countries, especially in the financial field.
Mr. Cherdkiat Atthakor also commended the leadership of the National Bank of Cambodia for its hard work in promoting the use of the riel through the introduction of various regulations and promotional campaigns, including the establishment of the Isanvarman Museum. Raise public awareness of the benefits of using the riel and the history of the Cambodian economy and currency.
