At the same time, those who give birth to twins or more will also receive additional support from Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the amount of 5 million Riels.
General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia Disseminates Customs Regulations and Procedures on Exports of Natural Stone to Promote Exports
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, on October 5, 2023, chaired a meeting on disseminating customs regulations and procedures on the export of stone products. Nature.
The participants included the President, Vice President and members of the Cambodian Granite Business Association, companies engaged in the business of processing and exporting stone, and many other customs and excise officials.
Dr. Kun Nhem informed about the policy of the Royal Government to adjust the export tax rate on processed stones in accordance with the content of Sub-Decree No. 299, dated September 29, 2023, simplification of customs procedures and procedures. A clear understanding of these tasks is key to proper implementation, increasing compliance and efficiency.
In addition, Dr. Director General also informed about the adjustment of some customs procedures and procedures to facilitate the export more easily and quickly.
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has also set up two hotlines that businesses / traders can contact for clarification or immediate resolution in case traders encounter problems related to the export of natural stone.
During the meeting, there was a lively Q&A program on the topic of the mining business, and Mr. Oknha Leng Rithy, President of the Association and a representative of traders in this field, thanked the Royal Government for its attention and submission. Issue policy measures to reduce taxes and other specific measures to help the business of processing and exporting natural stone to run better.
