(Pailin): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, disseminated the Ministry's four priority strategies to civil servants of Pailin Provincial Department of Rural Development and encouraged them to actively participate in achieving Cambodia's vision. High-middle-income people by 2030 and high-income people by 2050.
This announcement was made on the occasion of Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen meeting with leaders and civil servants of Pailin Provincial Department of Rural Development on October 5, 2023, with the participation of Mr. Ros Noeun, Deputy Governor of Pailin Province.
The Minister said that in order to contribute to the achievement of the Pentagon Strategy and Vision 2030 and 2050, the Ministry of Rural Development has strived to achieve its vision of improving the quality and values of the rural people in a sustainable manner. Economic, social and cultural aspects.
The Minister stated that the Ministry has four priority strategies:
First, to develop physical and transportation infrastructure by striving to raise the level of roads from red gravel roads to white paved roads and concrete roads so that people can access public services in all seasons and distribute economic growth to rural areas.
Second, improve the living conditions of rural communities in order for rural people to have a good attitude, live healthy and hygienic and comfortable.
Third, diversify rural economic activities through basic skills training to create jobs and employment in order to increase household economic income in rural areas.
The Minister continued to instruct the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Pailin Province that along with the achievements and achievements of the past, must continue to increase more achievements to contribute to achieving the vision of Cambodia to make middle-income people. Higher levels in 2030 and higher incomes in 2050.
Pailin Provincial Department of Rural Development must strive to fulfill its role as a good and honest technical staff to the provincial administration and cooperate well with relevant departments and authorities at all levels to promote the work of the rural development sector better.
The Pailin Provincial Department of Rural Development shall regularly review the monthly, quarterly, semi-annual meetings to evaluate the work based on collective principles.
