Senior officials of the Ministry of Public Works held a meeting to discuss and discuss the draft technical standards for road construction at the intersection of roundabouts and intersections.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Yit Bonna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on October 4, 2023, chaired a meeting of the Road Technical Working Group to discuss and discuss the draft technical standards for construction at intersections along roads. With the participation of relevant professional officers of the unit under his supervision.
The meeting was held to review the content of the design process and construction dimensions at roundabouts and intersections, where these technical standards are trained and documented by the country's Austroads Technical Team. Australia.
This draft book provides the necessary information and guidance for road designers to prepare detailed geometric drawings, attention to safety, traffic volume and consideration of future road widening requirements that are sufficient to facilitate the construction work.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn Attends the 45th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Agriculture and Forestry in Kuala Lumpur and Two Other Meetings
This meeting is held annually to discuss the progress and opportunities in the ASEAN Cooperation on Food, Agriculture and Forestry towards achieving food security, better market access, and agricultural productivity and resilience. Original.
Then, on the afternoon of October 4, 2023 in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attended the ASEAN-Japan Ministerial Meeting on Agriculture and Forestry.
The AJMCP seeks to contribute to achieving ASEAN food security through the development and dissemination of technologies, human resource development, and by supporting the implementation of ASEAN Regional Guidelines.
On the evening of October 4, 2023, in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn delivered a welcome address at the launch of the ASEAN Regional Food Innovation Program (CGIAR) with the participation of ASEAN Ministers of Agriculture and Forestry. And some development partners.
This regional program is in line with ASEAN's goal of increasing agricultural productivity and reducing food loss and food waste in ASEAN through the use of the latest research and technology that will strengthen the resilience of agricultural systems.
