On that occasion, Ms. Long Disannara expressed her sincere congratulations to all the Chapey Dang Veng artists who won in today's festival. In particular, she encouraged the young artists who did not receive the award and asked them to continue their efforts to contribute to the promotion of the performing arts to be more sustainable.
"The Chapey Dang Veng Festival is not only a platform for competitions, but also a place to meet, learn, measure and share experiences and knowledge," she said. Therefore, the main goal of organizing the Chapey Festival now is to provide opportunities to study the strengths and weaknesses in order to strengthen the capacity and promote the field of performing arts to grow further.
During a courtesy call and discussion with President Hun Manet on the afternoon of October 4, 2023, Ms. Lyou Caro Rodriguez Bario informed the President about the invitation of the President of Cuba to visit Cuba.
The Ambassador expressed strong hope that President Hun Manet will pay an official visit to Cuba at the invitation of the President of Cuba and that all Cubans will be ready to welcome him warmly.
In response, the President gladly accepted the request and confirmed the same intention, with the President finding a suitable time in the future.
In addition to discussing the above issues, President Hun Manet and Mr. Lyou Caro Rodriguez Bario also discussed relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Cuba.
The Ambassador reaffirmed the position of the Cuban government and people towards Cambodia that Cambodia is a good friend of Cuba, always helping each other at all times and in all circumstances. Although the geography of the two countries is far apart, the warm hearts of the two nations are always close.
The ambassador also noted the good relations and cooperation between the two countries in many fields, including health, agriculture, and other potential areas. She also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for its close cooperation during her diplomatic mission in Cambodia.
On behalf of the Cuban government and people, the Ambassador commended the Royal Government of Cambodia for sending Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron, High Representative of Cambodia, to the G77 + China Summit in Havana in mid-September 2023. Come here.
On that occasion, Samdech Hun Sen also praised the historical relationship between the two countries, especially in the most difficult circumstances of Cambodia after the liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, Cambodia at that time did not have many friends. Cuba has become a good friend, and this friendship continues to this day and continues to strengthen and expand.
