(Phnom Penh): Tour operators in Siem Reap have high expectations that Siem Reap will be able to attract more tourists from South Korea to visit the province, as from October is the season to visit more.
Philip Set Kao, president of the Siem Reap Tourism Club Association, told Fresh News that the launch of direct flights between Siem Reap and Incheon, Korea, was good news, as he expected Korean tourists to return. Siem Reap is back in large numbers, while Korean tourists have been the largest source of visitors to the province.
He said that since the outbreak of Kovid, until now, Korean visitors in Siem Reap have not recovered due to the lack of direct flights to Siem Reap.
He said that between 2010 and 2015, Korean visitors led the way in visiting Siem Reap. But then it slowed down a bit, bringing Chinese visitors back in the lead.
He said that before the outbreak of Kovid 19, there were some direct flights from Seoul to Siem Reap, and from this country also brought tourists from other countries such as the United States to visit Siem Reap. Also.
"Tour guides seem to be busier, receiving more tour guide bookings from May to September," he said. In fact, I received bookings for about seven groups, up from two last month. Now, from November to April, I get an average of 5 to 6 bookings per month. This does not take into account local guests.
However, he said that in order for tourists to come and visit Cambodia again and want to come to Cambodia again, stakeholders must work together to prepare for the orderly infrastructure, clean environment, security and good order to make the guests happy. .
At the same time, he asked the immigration service staff at the airport and at some border crossings to be friendly and welcoming, because in the past, he observed that some immigration staff have inappropriate gestures and strong faces. Place guests.
Cambodia is expected to receive around 4.5 million to 5 million international tourists for the whole of 2023.
