The Acting Provincial Governor stated that during the 1960s and 1970s, the Kingdom of Cambodia under the leadership of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk participated in helping Vietnam in the cause of national unification and territorial integrity in the 1970s. 80 Vietnam also participated in helping Cambodia in the cause of liberating the Cambodian people from the genocidal regime of Democratic Kampuchea.
The Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Monument in Sihanoukville was built during 1984, located in Village 3, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, and was renovated for the second time in 2016 and opened on July 22. 2017 Presided over by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Mr. Nguyen Fu Chung, Secretary General of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam and
The Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Monument was erected as a testament to the gratitude and remembrance of the Cambodian people for their sacrifices, for the cause of the unification and territorial integrity of Vietnam during the 1960s and 1970s, and as a testament to the gratitude and remembrance of the workers. Of the Vietnamese army and people for the cause of liberating the Cambodian people from the genocidal regime of Democratic Kampuchea in the 1970s and 1980s.
