Phnom Penh Governor Orders National Armed Forces to Investigate Explosives, Prevent Gangsters in Schools and Inspect All Entertainment Clubs to Suppress Crimes, Especially Drugs
(Phnom Penh): Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command, Mr. Khuong Sreng, ordered all competent forces and 14 district authorities to set up a commission to inspect all accommodation and entertainment clubs in Phnom Penh to strengthen security. Strongly prevent various crimes, especially drugs and all forms of human trafficking.
Mr. Khuong Sreng made such a call during the meeting of Phnom Penh Unity Command on the afternoon of October 4, 2023 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and the 14 Khan authorities must establish a committee to inspect all accommodation and entertainment clubs in Phnom Penh to strengthen security to prevent various crimes, especially to prevent trafficking. Drugs and human trafficking in all its forms.
"The commission must leave immediately and the inspection must be documented and signed by the owner of the largest shareholder, not allowing the manager to sign instead," he said. "This work must be grasped. If we can not grasp this statistic, what can we do?"
Mr. Khuong Sreng added that in addition to the above measures, the deployment of forces to check national weapons, explosives, prevention of gangsters in schools, cracking down on gambling at the grassroots level is also important that must be implemented effectively with the strengthening of security. Prevent all kinds of crimes in complex areas 24 hours a day to keep people warm.
