Putin to travel to Kyrgyzstan next week for first overseas visit since ICC arrest warrant issued
Russian President Vladimir Putin will travel to Kyrgyzstan next week for his first foreign trip since the International Criminal Court (ICC) issued an arrest warrant for him. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, October 4, 2023.
Russian President Vladimir Putin has rarely left Russia since the war of aggression erupted in Ukraine in February 2022. The last time Putin traveled abroad was in December last year, when he visited Kyrgyzstan as well as Belarus, Moscow's closest neighbor and ally.
