(Siem Reap): The water situation is now stronger than in 2014 as the team of the Department of Water Management, Forestry and Infrastructure of the APSARA Authority is very busy to control and avoid the water flowing from the upper part to the Angkor resort area.
Phoeun Sokhim, director of the Department of Water Management, Forests and Infrastructure, said that as of October 4, the water level in the Angkor resort area was rising sharply. In order to prevent flooding of the temple area, according to the instructions of the Director General of the APSARA Authority, the officials opened the water gate and prepared to avoid it in time. In fact, the APSARA Authority controls the water completely and there is no risk.
Mr. Phoeun Sokhim said that the water was diverted to the main sluice gates, such as O Khlot, O Roka, etc., dropped into Stung Puok, Stung Preah Srok, and some were added to Kasindhu and Baray in the Angkor resort area.
Mr. Phoeun Sokhim confirmed that the water situation now is stronger than in 2014. However, the APSARA Authority can manage this situation without worrying about flooding the temple area and Siem Reap city, as the capacity of the newly built sluice gates and the restoration of a large number of ancient water systems serve this water management work.
