(Ba Phnom-Prey Veng): Senior Minister Prum Sokha, Chairman of Ba Phnom District Working Group and his colleagues on the afternoon of September 29, 2023, visited in person at the back of people's houses to mourn the families of four workers in Rong Damrey commune. Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province, who lost his life in a traffic accident that overturned a truck carrying workers in Theay commune on Sunday night, September 24, 2023.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister and his team expressed their heartfelt condolences and condolences to the families of the four workers for the loss of a beloved family member in this unexpected accident.
The four workers who lost their lives in the accident were Hai Ratana, 35, Siet Samai, 32, Hun Srey Nath, 22, and Mei, 26. All four are workers at the 5-star fertilizer factory in Samrong Thom commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province.
On the day before the incident, a group of nine workers rented a car to go to the wedding of a colleague in Teuk Thla commune, Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province, when they returned on the street in the dark and heavy rain. Four people were killed and five others were slightly injured when a car overturned and fell into a deep ditch.
Senior Minister and Chairman of Ba Phnom District Working Group brought 1.6 million Riels in donations, supplies, food and budget to each family of the deceased. For the other 5 workers with minor injuries, they received 300,000 Riels each from the district working group.
Afterwards, the Senior Minister and his team inspected the scene, requesting the local authorities and the above-mentioned specialized authorities to investigate, take practical measures and put up signs to prevent such traffic accidents.
In the afternoon of the same day, at the CPP headquarters in Ba Phnom district, Senior Minister Prum Sokha, Chairman of Ba Phnom District Working Group, chaired a closed-door meeting to review the work in September and discuss the direction of further work.
