Phnom Penh Capital Hall Plans to Expand Drainage System to Avoid Flooding by Rain
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration is preparing to expand the drainage system, drainage canals from small to large, install bigger pumps and build new pumping stations to avoid flooding in Phnom Penh.
This was stated by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh during the meeting to plan for investment in infrastructure, sewer system and drainage system to avoid flooding in Phnom Penh with the 14 district governors and relevant departments on the morning of October 4. This 2023.
Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that "the arrangement of drainage system, canal, water release was good until it was praised by the international community and His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister." "However, we still have some challenges that require us to work together to find solutions to avoid flooding during heavy and intermittent rains."
He added that the purpose of this meeting is to gather information about the drainage system in all corners to find more new measures to lead to better water release in Phnom Penh and long-term use, especially the diversion of waterways. Kampong Speu Province Do not come to Phnom Penh.
The Governor of Phnom Penh underlined that under the guidance of His Excellency Hun Manet, Phnom Penh within 4 years must develop good underground infrastructure to avoid the threat of flooding. In this work, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will meet with the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh and the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Phnom Penh to prepare an inter-ministerial plan to continue to implement this work.
He also mentioned that the drainage system should be improved, especially the expansion of drainage canals from small to large, the installation of larger pumping stations and the installation of new pumping stations. While the people of Phnom Penh are civilized, the Phnom Penh administration will prepare a large project to deal with the flooding in Phnom Penh for 20 to 30 years.
At the same time, Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, confirmed that the construction of the sewer system in Phnom Penh by 2022, we have built a sewer network with a length of more than 924 km and will continue to build a sewer system. The important thing is to keep it in the reservoir to release the water quickly.
