In the instruction received by Fresh News this morning, October 4, 2023, Deputy Prime Minister Sokha noted that there are some gaps and irregularities that result from negligence in the performance of duties. Put out all these instructions.
The following are the 7 points of advice of Dr. Aphisandandit Sar Sokha:
* First: to close all illegal corridors within its jurisdiction. If it is necessary to study, research and evaluate the economic and social potential of the existing port, then propose to the Ministry of Interior to have a study base and suggest to the management to decide on the establishment of an official border gate.
* Second, measures must be taken to strengthen the management and control of passengers, goods and means of entry and exit across the border in order to prevent and suppress all kinds of cross-border crimes, especially to strengthen the responsibility for security, safety, public order and Order at border gates within its jurisdiction.
* Third: Remind the competent authorities standing at all border gates to immediately stop the issuance of irregular passports and the collection of informal fees from workers and the general public when they cross. Entry and exit through border gates, contrary to the spirit of agreements with neighboring countries, as well as the laws and regulations in force of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Fourth, to continue to provide public services and border card services to the people without discrimination, along with the management of statistics and the flow of people in and out across the border clearly, and strive to address the challenges that arise in The border gates are within their jurisdiction.
* Sixth: Continue to educate, guide, disseminate and raise awareness among the people, especially those living in the border areas, to better understand the procedures of border crossing and encourage them to cooperate and report on all issues. Irregularities in border areas and at border crossings with neighboring countries.
At the same time, Mr. Abhisandibandit, Deputy Prime Minister, also urged to pay attention to research and intervene to the victims when they receive information that they are all cheating abroad.
"I would like to appeal to all stakeholders, especially the border provinces of Thailand, Vietnam and Laos, to investigate, and especially the victims, most of them young women," he said. 18 years old. "So if there is smuggling through brokers or in groups along some international borders or gateways, please check."
Dr. Sar Sokha claims that this is a case of human trafficking, which has already happened in some European countries, but now it is starting to spread again. However, in the case of finding that Cambodians abroad are falling into this trap, the Cambodian authorities have also successfully intervened in a series of days, apparently a few days ago, they helped six Cambodian workers in Laos.
Please be reminded that on September 30, 2023, the Cambodian Embassy in Laos received information on Facebook regarding the case of seven Cambodian women who posted a message on Facebook seeking help. The seven women were tricked into coming to work in Laos' Bor Keo province and fled the workplace after problems with their employer, who planned to sell them to a third country.
After receiving this information, the Cambodian Embassy in Laos immediately requested the cooperation of the Lao authorities to rescue the seven Cambodian women. At the same time, His Excellency Hun Manet also instructed Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, to urge the Cambodian Embassy in Laos to pay close attention to this issue in cooperation with the Lao authorities.
As of October 1, 2023, six Cambodian women have been rescued and are in a safe and caring place. Meanwhile, the embassy has been cooperating with the Lao authorities to continue to rescue another Cambodian woman.
