(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration plans to build two more bridges across the river, from Prek Pra to National Road 2 and 60 meters to the Choeung Ek Development Zone.
According to the Governor of Phnom Penh, it is believed that after the completion of these two bridges, the above area can be resolved better and there will be no more traffic jams.
This statement was made by Mr. Khuong Sreng on the occasion of bringing a meeting on security and safety to the senior leaders of the Royal Government on the afternoon of October 3, 2023, with the participation of the Capital Commission. The Capital Gendarmerie Command, the forces of the 14 Khan Inspectorates and the 14 Khan Governors under the Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the meeting was held to find ways to solve traffic congestion, especially to facilitate the management of the leadership smoothly and reduce discrimination from people traveling on the road.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said: "Around this issue, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has made great efforts to build a concrete bridge on the Koh Nora cable from Koh Pich to Koh Nora in Chbar Ampov and Chamkarmon districts with plans to build two bridges. The other place crosses from Prek Pra to National Road 2 to 60 meters of Choeung Ek Development Area. After the construction of these two bridges, the above area can be solved better and there will be no more traffic jams.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also confirmed that although the construction of the Monivong flyover has been completed, the site is still facing congestion due to heavy traffic flow from National Road No. 1.
Mr. Khuong Sreng continued that as a step to solve traffic problems at the above point. He advised the police force to strictly prohibit large trucks from entering Phnom Penh on National Road No. 1, especially from Niroth 3 to Chbar Ampov Bridge, because we already have a detour for them. The Phnom Penh Capital Administration must immediately notify them so that they know the information and stay away from this congested area.
