Japan sees record September high temperature in 2023 since recorded (Video inside) (TOKYO) It is the hottest day on record since 125 years ago, with this year's temperature expected to be the hottest in human history. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, October 3, 2023.
The average temperature in September was 2.66 degrees Celsius higher than normal, the highest level since 1898. Across Japan, in September, 100 out of 153 observatories broke the average temperature record, including Tokyo at 26.7 degrees Celsius, Osaka at 27.9 degrees Celsius and Nagoya at 27.3 degrees Celsius. "An average temperature rise of 2.66 degrees Celsius is not uncommon and poses a high risk."
2023 is expected to be the hottest year in history due to climate change, with countries such as Austria, France, Germany, Poland and Switzerland declaring September to be their hottest month on record. Photo: AFP Lt. Gen. Lim Sokhaksmey sends congratulatory message and congratulates HE Sok Monorom on his appointment as Assistant to HE Pen Vibol, Deputy Prime Minister
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department of the General Commission of the National Police, sent a message of congratulations and congratulations to HE Sok Monorom, who has been appointed as Assistant to HE Pen Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister. Equal to the Director General.
