(Phnom Penh): A group of Cambodians raised about $ 1,205 to do charity work for the people of Morocco who were affected by the earthquake on September 8, 2023.
Seth Mohamad Sis, Secretary of State for the Office of the Council of Ministers, initiated a fundraiser to provide humanitarian assistance to the people of Morocco through the Chansu Yu Charity.
Through a call on social media, about 61 Cambodians took part in this transcontinental humanitarian activity and raised $ 1,205. Funds were diverted to the Chan Suyu Charity in Morocco, and the organization also donated food to the affected Moroccan people.
At present, the aid package has been distributed to the people of Morocco, and on the aid package, the image of the Cambodian flag is highlighted. Through this aid package, although small in size, it also shows the heart of the people of Cambodia to share the difficulties with people around the world.
The representative of the charity Chan Suyu expressed his deep gratitude to the Cambodian people for sharing their difficulties with the people of Morocco.
Seth Mohammed Sisi has stated that he has not yet completed the fundraiser for the people of Morocco. At this time, he continues to receive donations from philanthropists, and when more will be sent to the charity Chan Suyu.
Ratanakkiri Constituency Deputies and Kan Ben Provincial Commissioner 4th Round at Wat O Cheng, Kon Mom District
On the morning of October 3, 2023, Mr. Kith Try, Member of Parliament for Ratanakkiri Constituency, and Brigadier General Im Phany, Acting Commissioner, Representative of Major General Ong Sopheap, Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Commissioner, and several police officers attended the meeting. Ben 4th turn at Wat O Cheng, Kon Mom district.
On that occasion, the Ratanakkiri MP said that the Kanben Festival was held in accordance with the Buddhist tradition, with great joy in this Kanben Festival. Every year, all Buddhists worship the ceremony. Kan Ben, an ancient tradition that lasts for 15 days at all pagodas throughout the country.
He continued that under the right leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister made the country peaceful, developed in all areas, both Buddhist and imperial.
Kan Ben Pchum Ben is one of the largest festivals of all Buddhism. The ceremony lasts for 15 days, from the 1st of Roach to the 15th of Roach, which is Pchum Ben Day. During the 15 days of this religious festival, Buddhists near and far at the foot of the pagoda regularly serve food to the monks, with the pagoda committee taking turns to supply the monks with food until the end of the Pchum Ben festival.
Please note that in the 4th Kan Ben ceremony, they collected 3,620,000 Riels and $ 720 for use in the temple. Charity program "My Library" continues to provide students at Prey Tom Primary School for study, research and increase knowledge
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Dr. Try Chanthuch, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Planning and Vice Chairman of the Board of Directors of Asia-Europe University, led the Asia-Europe University Working Group, Kaosung National University of Science and Technology and the Kiwanis Association to bring donations, materials and books. Read and equip a 1-room library at "Prey Tom" Primary School in Prey Tom Village, Prey Khmum Commune, Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province.
This is the third time that the "My Library" program has supported students in remote areas after helping students in Kandal and Kampong Speu provinces.
Dr. advised all students to study hard from elementary school to high school and continue to higher education to complete the basic reading in the study as a proverb says that reading more increases intelligence.
Knowledge is an invaluable asset that can help you to get out of ignorance and achieve prosperity, not only to change your life, your family life and your community, but also to contribute. Reduce poverty and change the face of the nation.
Mr. Suon Vanna, Principal of Prey Tom Primary School, thanked the donors and considered the current support to alleviate the difficulties for students in finding documents for reading, research and to improve the reading of students in Here for the better.
