Samdech Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has considered three things: First, what the people have received and must continue to give it to them. Second, think that after the formation of the Royal Government, we need to expand to help. Distressed people. Thirdly, in addition to what we personally help in addition to the budget, what do we do to facilitate him so that he can easily work and have a better life.
Samdech Manibodi Hun Manet added that the Royal Government also aims to ensure that all 9 million people receive health care services and the Royal Government plans to spend nearly 100 million dollars per year, which is what the Royal Government Plans to expand to help people. The Royal Government is not only taking care of what is already there, but also expanding it.
Samdech Hun Manet added that the Royal Government has provided vocational training to 1.5 million people at a cost of $ 36 million per year and increased annually. The Royal Government has also launched a program to help the agricultural market with $ 100 million per year, which the Royal Government spends.
Samdech continued, "The abolition of taxes, the payment of various taxes for the sale of people through baskets in the markets across the country, the state continues not to take this tax." "In the past, there was chaos in some markets, worrying about taking taxes through baskets. The state has no policy to take it. Authorities at all levels have to be careful.
Please be informed that while the General Department of Taxation strengthens revenue collection for the development of the society, ensures transparency and fair competition, the Royal Government also pays close attention to facilitating the investment environment as well as improving the living standards of the people. Introduce a series of incentives in almost every field.
To help business owners and citizens, the General Department of Taxation has provided a number of incentives through the introduction of fiscal incentives, including:
* Abolition of the contract tax and turnover tax to end the complex problems of people who run small businesses just to make a living and to eliminate the hiding place of taxpayers who are included in the self-declaration regime
* Define some of the supplies as non-VAT supplies, including education, electricity and clean water for the people to use, unprocessed agricultural products and garbage collection services. This mechanism aims to improve livelihoods and Welfare of the people
* Adjusting the amount of patent tax to be paid to encourage small enterprises to do business
* Abolition of slaughter tax to help reduce the cost of meat, which is the basic food for subsistence, as well as alleviate the daily life of the people to another level.
* Introduction of simple accounting rules to facilitate small taxpayers in small business or family business operations
* Several reductions in the payroll tax base through the subsequent increase in the minimum level of taxable salaries and the portion of taxable income to ensure that public servants and workers - Employees who receive a minimum wage or salary are not subject to payroll tax.
* Elimination of tax on means of transportation for some vehicles, such as motorcycles, tricycles, water vehicles, tractors and some similar machinery to reduce the burden of the general population.
* Stamp tax incentives for the acquisition of property or possession of real estate within relatives
* Abolition of stamp duty on legal documents on company formation
* Adjustment of stamp duty, except for the application of some legal documents, such as applications related to education, application for employment, civil status certificate, etc. And
* Adjusting monthly interest rates for tax rebates and late payment of tax arrears to adjust interest rates according to market conditions, ease the burden on the private sector and facilitate trade.
In addition, the Royal Government has introduced a number of tax incentives in key areas, including:
* Securities sector - tax incentives for the securities sector, in particular the exemption of income tax of 50% of the total income tax payable for 3 years, tax debt relief, and 50% withholding tax deduction Interest and dividends from holding and trading securities
* Financial sector - Temporary suspension of value-added tax (VAT) on non-financial services - Pre-tax deduction on interest payments on microfinance institutions' foreign loans Stuff
* Education - Tax exemption for educational institutions, including income tax exemption, including income tax relief and minimum tax, value added tax, and withholding tax on interest and dividends until 2028
* Tourism - Exemption of tax obligations for travel agents and tour operators
* Construction sector - Allowing construction enterprises to pay tax according to the actual calculation of each project in advance - Measures to support the development of construction and real estate in Borey
* Real estate sector - Property tax exemption for real estate in certain geographical areas - Incentives for real estate sector, especially tax exemption, stamp, transfer of ownership or tenancy of all types of houses worth less than or equal to $ 70,000 and term increase When paying tax as a package for a housing developer
* On September 28, 2023, the General Department of Taxation decided to allow property owners to pay only taxes, with the exception of administrative penalties (additional tax and interest) on property tax and unused land tax. Until the end of 2023. "
* In addition, there are tax incentives for many other important sectors.
In addition, on September 20, 2023, the Royal Government approved the National Strategy for Informal Economic Development 2023-2028, which includes a number of fiscal facilitation measures to support the informal economy, which the General Department of Taxation It is preparing the necessary legal documents to promote implementation.
The Royal Government-Private Sector Forum, which will take place in November 2023, is chaired by Samdech Mani Hun Manet in order to listen to opinions and suggestions from the private sector.
The remarks of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet were made on the occasion that Samdech continued to visit nearly 20,000 more workers, which is the fifth meeting in the new government. The meeting took place in the geographical territory of Dangkor and Meanchey districts of Phnom Penh on the morning of October 3, 2023.
"In November, when you meet the private sector, you will know what benefits the government provides in this difficult situation for the private sector so that the private sector can survive to create jobs for you," he said. Khmer all over the country. ”
The Royal Government-Private Sector Forum is held once a year by the Royal Government of Cambodia as a dialogue mechanism led by the Prime Minister of Cambodia and with the participation of ministers from all ministries, institutions, governors of all capitals and provinces. Private in all fields, Ambassador to Cambodia and representatives of some international institutions.
This forum provides an opportunity for the private sector to raise challenges and suggestions to the Royal Government to review and take appropriate action to resolve, and all decisions in this forum are considered by the Council of Ministers.
Please be reminded that on the occasion of chairing the first plenary session of the new Council of Ministers of the 7th mandate, Samdech President Hun Manet announced that he will chair the 19th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum in November to continue to support the private sector as a driving force. Of economic growth.
