Currently, Cambodia has the capacity to generate 3,464 megawatts of domestic electricity from solar power, hydropower, biomass, coal and oil, and the highest demand for electricity is currently only around 2,400 megawatts. This means that Cambodia has the capacity to generate more energy than needed, so we do not have a shortage of electricity.
