Minister Chea Randet Asks Ministries to Establish Their Own Technology System to Easily Provide Services to Citizens
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Randeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, on October 2, 2023, requested all Ministries and Government Institutions to establish their own technology systems to facilitate the provision of their services to the people and companies in need. Services.
Minister Chea Randet confirmed that in the near future, ministries and institutions will have a digital transformation unit, in accordance with the principles of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. According to Minister Chea Randet, this sub-decree may be implemented in the next two to three months.
The proposal was made on the occasion of Mr. Chea Randet's participation in the official launch of the Digital Skills Development Program and the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Awareness and Development. Digital expertise between the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and six partner higher education institutions on September 2, 2023.
Minister Chea Randet stated, "We are preparing a sub-decree for all ministries to have a digital transformation unit At present, some ministries have a technology department and some ministries do not, so after the sub-decree goes out to all ministries. Must have. ”
At the same time, Minister Chea Randet stated that in line with the Royal Government's first pentagon strategy, increasing the development of digital skills human resources is an indispensable and important step for Cambodia to become A country with a digital economy and a highly efficient digital administration.
In addition, Minister Chea Randet said that the Royal Government has identified five key forces: people, roads, water, electricity and digital technology. In this regard, the implementation of digital human capital is the first force to prepare for socio-economic development. Digital and Industrial Response to Industrial Revolution 4.0.
This strategy reflects the long-term thinking of the Royal Government in setting the goal of building a digital social economy to be the driving force of new economic growth, as well as contributing to the promotion of competitiveness and promoting economic and social diversification in Cambodia.
All 15 members of the UN Security Council voted overwhelmingly on Monday (New York time), with 13 countries voting in favor of a Kenyan-led mission in Haiti. Two countries, Russia and China, have abstained, citing concerns over unrest in Haiti caused by foreign incursions.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, October 3, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, continued to visit nearly 20,000 more workers. The fifth meeting with workers in the new government took place in the geographical area of Khan Dangkor and Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
On this occasion, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet spoke for about 2 hours, the following are the main contents of Samdech:
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet said that this morning, Samdech was pleased to meet the workers.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party does not abandon the workers.
* Samdech Mani Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party does not give up politics to help the people.
* Samdech President Hun Manet stated that the wages of workers are not enough, but the Royal Government is committed to increase the workers every year.
* President Hun Manet stated that wages in Cambodia are higher than some countries in the region and that in 2024 there will be no wage increase.
* President Hun Manet said that it is a good thing for workers in Cambodia, whose wages are higher than some countries and get an increase in 2024.
* President Hun Manet stated that high labor costs could be a barrier to attracting new investors to Cambodia.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet thanked the workers for their support of the 2024 wage increase.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the Prime Minister's allowance of $ 2 is an incentive for employers to accept.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet called on landlords not to increase rent in 2024.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government is willing to pay millions of dollars per month in electricity bills to alleviate the burden of workers.
During his visit to the United States, Samdech Hun Sen met with 58 US businessmen.
* President Hun Manet stated that in the future, many American companies will come to study investment in Cambodia.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that for more than 40 days, the Royal Government has done a lot of work for the people.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet was outraged by the story of the opposition group accusing Kannitha of selling his head after explaining the tax issue.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that foreign opposition radio groups are trying to incite people to hate the government
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that there are 13 taxes in Cambodia that the Royal Government collects.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the issues of the people, Samdech must pay attention to all. But the problem of the people is Samdech to speak separately, the tax starts from the interview of Mr. Kong Vibol, Samdech to the relevant institutions as interpreters.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that Samdech monitors all the problems of the people, but Samdech urges the relevant authorities to examine and solve. Is it necessary for the Prime Minister to come forward and solve everything?
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that some tasks were handled by Samdech himself, while others were handled by Samdech for ministries and institutions to solve.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet questioned whether he wanted the Prime Minister to be the spokesman for the Ministry of State Institutions?
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet reminded that when meeting with the Prime Minister of Thailand, Samdech asked the two countries' Ministries of Culture to resolve the issue of building temples in Thailand.
Responding to comparisons with the Royal Government of Thailand, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government does not have a lot of money, but does not let people go hungry.
* President Hun Manet stated that about $ 1.2 billion will be spent to support people affected by the Kovid-19 crisis and inflation.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government is studying to expand health care services to about 9 million people at a cost of tens of millions of dollars per year. The government will spend $ 100 million on agriculture.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that Samdech advised the Siem Reap Provincial Governor and relevant authorities to attract tourists to Siem Reap.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the issue of livelihood and economic challenges of the people were considered from the beginning.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that in November 2023, in a meeting with business people, the Royal Government will present interventions to solve economic problems in Cambodia.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the new Royal Government has not made a new tax law. Samdech President Hun Manet said that the new government has not increased the tax rate.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government continues its policy of not taxing small sales in the market.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet praised the efforts to collect taxes, but must reduce the procedures so that they do not overlap and do not overdo it.
