(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, October 4, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, continued to visit nearly 20,000 more workers. The fifth meeting with workers in the new government took place in the geographical area of Khan Dangkor and Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
Dr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that a total of 18,099 workers, including 689 pregnant workers, attended the meeting under the chairmanship of Samdech Mani Hun Manet. According to Heng Sour, the workers who participated in the event came from 22 factories, including: 18 garment factories, 2 travel products and bags, 1 shoe sewing machine and 1 umbrella factory.
According to the Minister of Alumni from Japan, Phnom Penh currently has 9,590 factories and employs a total of 665,000 workers, with a total salary of more than 2 billion US dollars. One year. There are 735 garment factories employing a total of 340,000 workers, earning more than $ 1 billion a year.
In the last four meetings, His Excellency Hun Manet presented the policy of the Royal Government in the new legislature, especially the Pentagon strategy - the first phase, which is a strategy to focus on job growth and improve people's lives. Citizens for the better.
In the previous meeting, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet pointed out six priority tasks to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to be implemented effectively in 2023. The six jobs include:
The Prime Minister also introduced the action plan for the next two years to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to focus on the implementation of four other priority tasks, including:
4: Promote the skills recognition test program, which is an opportunity for workers, both domestic and foreign, to have a skills certification certificate to show their ability and skill level.
In addition, at the time of childbirth, a worker receives 800,000 Riels for one child, 1.2 million Riels for twins and 1.6 million Riels for triplets. The triplets will also receive 5 million riels separately from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Separately, the implementation of the new subsidy policy of the Royal Government from August 1 to October 2, 2023, there are 10,062 women workers, civil servants, contract workers, 9,685 children. A total of 40,393 people went for prenatal and postnatal check-ups and vaccinations. In just two months, the government has spent $ 3 million on this sponsorship program.
Mr. Heng Sour emphasized that this support is a testament to the consideration of improving the health of mothers and young children to contribute to solving the problem of malnutrition of young children from infancy to 2 years old and Promote the physical and mental growth of young children, as well as help ease the burden of workers.
