Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by His Majesty the King Hun Manet, has launched the six priority policy programs of the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, focusing on improving the living standards of the people.
The six priority policy programs of the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy include:
* Program 2: Vocational and technical training for young people from poor and vulnerable families across the country,
* Program 3: Establishment of the National Social Assistance Program for Poor Families, Vulnerable Groups in Poor Families and Vulnerable Families in Times of Economic Crisis and Emergencies,
Program 4: Introduction and promotion of the implementation of the informal economic development strategy to be able to participate in the informal economy,
Program 5: Introduction of coordination mechanisms and financing programs aimed at boosting production, marketing and maintaining the balance of prices of key agricultural products at a reasonable level and
* Program 6: Deployment of agricultural technical officers to all communes with agricultural activities throughout the country to promote agricultural productivity and assist farmers 'families in promoting their agricultural products and to establish farmers' associations in In the countryside.
