He added that the land in that area is in Chhouk Sor commune, Kampong Tralach district, the Forestry Administration has requested to manage 400 hectares of state forest land since 1989. He said that although all the land has now been settled by villagers since 1979, he will ask the upper level to take control of the 400 hectares of land, but this case depends. On the decision of the Royal Government as well.
The letter also stated that in October 2015, the Kampong Tralach District Administration received a letter from the Director of Forestry Administration of Kampong Chhnang, No. 373, dated October 5, 2015, requesting the district to participate in solving the problem. The 400-hectare plantation is located in O Rong and Stok Lech villages, Chhouk Sor commune, Kampong Tralach district.
The district administration also confirmed that the nursery land was actually borrowed from the people, with the clarification from the village, commune, district and relevant documents confirmed by the district land officer as documented. Comes with built-in.
Finally, the two families, who are the real owners of the land and have been affected for more than 20 years, raised their hands to ask the leaders at all levels and all relevant units to help solve and provide justice. To their family of up to 23 members. At present, they do not have land to build houses, only land here, and to distribute their children and grandchildren to build shelters when they are not old.
