National Authority for Combating Drugs Holds Training Course on "Capacity Building of Frontline Law Enforcement Officers" from Preah Vihear, Stung Treng and Oddar Meanchey Provinces
(Preah Vihear): The General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs has opened a training course on "Strengthening the Capacity of Frontline Law Enforcement Officers" for drug law enforcement officers from Preah Vihear, Stung Treng and Oddar Meanchey provinces.
This ceremony was held on the morning of October 2, 2023 in the presence of General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Mr. Vat Paranin, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Preah Vihear Provincial Drug Control Committee. . This training is supported by the Office of the Thai Drug Control Council (ONCB) through the LOA 2023 project.
On that occasion, General Meas Virith highlighted the objectives of the training, including:
First, strengthen the capacity of law enforcement officers at the forefront of relevant units to investigate, prevent and suppress the trafficking of illegal drugs and chemicals more effectively.
Second: Establish good cooperation among officials of relevant units / institutions to share information and experience in enforcing the law effectively and safely.
Third, strengthen cooperation with neighboring countries through the BLO border liaison mechanism.
General Meas Virith wants to harmonize the community on the fight against drugs in the community, to have cooperation, support each other, eliminate discrimination and stigma, rescue drug addicts together, crack down on drug crime and eliminate Inactive in the local.
In order to achieve timely and effective measures, the General raised the slogan "3 Do 1 Report":
* First, do not get involved means do not trade, distribute, do not be a backbone, do not conspire and do not use drugs * Do not secondly do not intervene means do not prevent the implementation of the law against drug criminals, even family, relatives or friends * Third, do not excuse, meaning do not relax the law enforcement of drug offenders "1 report back" is to report to the authorities about drug hiding places, drug processing facilities, etc.
In addition, the general also reminded the authorities to continue to promote the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats, increase public forum activities and strive to raise awareness of the effects of drugs. In addition, continue to educate and encourage drug addicts to stop using and encourage them to seek treatment and rehabilitation in a timely manner.
The General Secretary requested all participants to continue to share the knowledge and experience gained from today's training to disseminate to colleagues and turn into practical activities to increase and strengthen work in accordance with the work direction of Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun. The President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and the high-level leadership recommendations of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who set out the five key priorities.
