Ministry of Public Works Introduces 9 Points to Participate in Disaster Management for Public Works and Transport
(Phnom Penh): In response to the floods that may affect the lives of people, crops and road-bridge infrastructure, which requires thorough and timely response measures to prevent and manage Potential Risks Eventually, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has issued nine guidelines aimed at co-ordinating disaster management for the public and transport sectors.
1. Participate in disseminating disaster situations and collecting comprehensive information from the National Committee for Disaster Management.
2. To coordinate with relevant ministries and institutions and authorities at all levels to carry out disaster response and rehabilitation operations.
3. Urgently deploy forces to repair and connect roads and bridges in case of road-bridge disconnection (traffic cut-off) in order to ensure traffic sustainability and to request the Ministry of Expenditure Guarantee Policy in a timely manner. Time.
4. Install traffic signs and safety signs in flood-prone areas to avoid possible accidents to road users and passengers.
5: To cooperate with local authorities at all levels and relevant departments to prevent floods, prevent heavy transport vehicles passing through flood-affected areas, and disseminate information to citizens, travelers and other transport companies. .
6. To cooperate in using the means and equipment of the relevant unit to be ready to participate in search and rescue interventions if necessary.
7. To rehabilitate the road-bridge infrastructure under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which was affected by the floods and flooding of the Mekong River.
8. Participate in mobilizing assistance in means, facilities, human resources and finance from development partners, national and international organizations in cooperation with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
9. To report and report on the situation regularly to the Ministry for immediate action.
