(Pursat): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, accompanied by Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Director General of the Ministry and Department of Rural Development of Pursat Province, on the morning of October 1, 2023, inspected a red gravel road connecting Pursat city to Kandeang district, which was cut into 3 pieces, damaged a total length of 2,350 meters.
It should be noted that the floods in late September and early October affected 11 provinces, damaging infrastructure and structures, including Siem Reap, Stung Treng, Tbong Khmum, Pursat, Mondulkiri, Kampong Thom, Preah Vihear, Kandal, Kratie, Takeo and Sihanoukville. . Separately, throughout Pursat province, 25 rural roads were flooded, equal to 268 kilometers, of which 38 kilometers were completely submerged.
The Minister instructed the leadership of the Provincial Department of Rural Development, in cooperation with the local authorities, to make emergency repairs for the people to cross temporarily when the water recedes and to consider rebuilding the damaged roads.
Afterwards, Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, with the participation of Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Mr. Yin Saven, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, as well as the accompanying delegation, met and discussed separately with the leaders and civil servants of the Provincial Department of Rural Development. Pursat and Kampong Chhnang provinces.
