(Siem Reap): Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, on behalf of Mr. Prak Sophoan, Provincial Governor, and his wife, together with provincial officials, on October 1, 2023, brought the relics to the monks at Wat Aranh Sakor in Siem Reap City. Siem Reap to join Ben with Buddhists in the second round of the traditional Khmer Pchum Ben festival.
It should be reminded that Kan Ben and Pchum Ben are one of the major traditional festivals of Cambodia from ancient times to the present. At the same time, the Cambodian people always celebrate this festival without interruption, except during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Preah Vihear Tohak Kim Huot, Chief Preacher of Wat Aranh Sakor, said that the Pchum Ben ceremony has three meanings:
First, made to dedicate to the parents, grandparents, relatives of the seven generations who have passed away, especially to the ghosts of hell, whether relatives or others.
Third, to contribute to the promotion of their national religion, to contribute to the preservation of traditions, customs, and special culture in order to create unity and solidarity.
