It should be noted that on the morning of September 30, 2023, the Cambodian Embassy in Laos received information on Facebook regarding the case of seven Cambodian women who posted a message on Facebook seeking help. . The seven women were tricked into coming to work in Laos' Bor Keo province and fled the workplace after problems with their employer, who planned to sell them to a third country.
After receiving this information, the Cambodian Embassy in Laos immediately requested the cooperation of the Lao authorities to rescue the seven Cambodian women. At the same time, His Excellency Hun Manet also instructed His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, to urge the Cambodian Embassy in Laos to pay close attention to this matter in cooperation with the Lao authorities.
As of October 1, 2023, six Cambodian women have been rescued and are in a safe and caring place. Meanwhile, the embassy has been cooperating with the Lao authorities to continue to rescue another Cambodian woman.
