(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions (CWLCU), which has more than 20,000 members from the textile, garment, footwear and bag industry sectors, has expressed its appreciation and gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by His Excellency Hun Manet. For the benefit of workers and strive to increase the minimum wage for workers, despite the world, including Cambodia is in crisis.
The Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions (ICTU) has stated that it has closely monitored the process of negotiating the minimum wage of the National Council for Minimum Wages, a tripartite mechanism, from the first meeting until the 28th. This September 2023.
