The National Committee for Road Safety calls on road users to pay more attention to preventing and preventing traffic accidents on the occasion of Kan Ben, Pchum Ben
(Phnom Penh): The National Committee for Road Safety calls on the public as road users to pay more attention to the prevention and prevention of road accidents while driving on the occasion of Kan Ben, Pchum Ben, Khmer tradition. From September 30 to October 15, 2023.
The National Road Safety Committee would like to express its sincere gratitude to the vast majority of road users who are willing to respect and enforce the Road Traffic Law actively while contributing to the reduction. Reduce the loss of life, injuries and property damage due to road accidents in the past.
However, road accidents have been threatening road users, causing tragedy, loss of life, injuries and property damage on a daily basis, and are always on the rise during festivals with heavy traffic. Disrespect the law, negligence or lack of understanding, tolerance.
In this regard, on the occasion of the celebration of Kan Ben, Pchum Ben, Khmer tradition, which will take place from September 30 to October 15, 2023, the National Road Safety Committee calls on the public as road users. Please pay attention to increase the spirit of participation in the prevention and prevention of road accidents driving vehicles in the following measures:
First, reduce the driving speed according to the law and according to the actual situation, such as town, school, bumpy road, curved road, intersection, slope, narrow road or slippery road, etc. The main cause of accidents is speeding.
Second, the right of way at the intersection must be respected by driving at a reduced speed and the driver must be allowed to drive on the right of way.
Third, before overtaking, make sure that the empty road ahead can be safely overtaken, avoiding risky overtaking that could eventually lead to a traffic accident.
Fourthly, for passenger cars or trucks, please do not load people or goods beyond the legal limit, especially passenger cars must not load people on the roof and do not increase travel costs on this occasion.
Fifth: Check the technical characteristics of your vehicle before traffic.
Sixth, drivers and passengers, please wear seat belts properly and regularly. Seventh, all motorcyclists and passengers must wear helmets properly, whether traveling near or far and at all times. Always remember that a helmet can help prevent head injuries or can save lives.
8th: Do not drive under the influence of alcohol or drugs and always remember the slogan if you drink alcohol, do not drive. Drunkenness can cause the driver to lose consciousness, lose consciousness, be unable to drive safely, and be prone to traffic accidents.
Ninth: When driving, adhere to good manners, ethics and mutual tolerance to avoid accidents or traffic jams.
The National Road Safety Committee would like to express its hope and trust in the public vigilance in implementing this call to bring safety and happiness to the family on the occasion of Kan Ben, Pchum Ben, National Tradition. Let happy days become sad days.
