Samdech Thep Hun Manet Calls on Stakeholders to Promote the Welfare of the Elderly
The organization of the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly, October 1, 2023, aims to promote effective protection aimed at improving the well-being of the elderly, and the day also demonstrates its important role. The importance of the elderly, the ancestors who created useful resources and provided innumerable knowledge, skills and experiences for the next generation.
Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet considers the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly as a day to commemorate the merits of Cambodia's elderly, ancestors, grandparents, parents and grandparents who have built and left a precious legacy for their children. This generation and the next.
On the Day of Gratitude to the Elderly, Samdech Hun Sen called on all stakeholders to work together to improve the well-being of the elderly.
The President's appeal is as follows:
1. The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of the Cambodian National Committee for the Elderly, all ministries, institutions and competent authorities at all levels must increase their attention and support by all means to improve the well-being of the elderly.
2: All ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations at all levels, please pay attention and support by all means when visiting the local level, please visit and support the elderly, especially the elderly with disabilities. Difficulties in the community.
3: All ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations and all organizations, please facilitate the existing Cambodian Association of the Elderly and please continue to support the intervention to promote the establishment, strengthen and expand the Association of the Elderly in the local community to increase The spirit of solidarity helps each other among the elderly in the Kingdom of Cambodia, especially the elderly, the disabled, the elderly, the poor and helpless.
4: Cambodian Red Cross, Radio and Television Foundation, Development Partners, Philanthropists, National and International Non-Governmental Organizations, Please Continue to Increase Humanitarian Aid Support Activities in Food, Material, Budget, and Technology to Provide Welfare Services for the Elderly Difficulties in terms of living and health, both physical and mental.
5: Professors, teachers in public and private educational institutions, please continue to pay attention to provide moral education and good traditions to all students to respect the elders and care for the elderly, which is a good tradition of the nation. Our Khmer.
6: Every family in each community, please continue to strengthen the morals and good traditions of our Khmer, especially to educate children and the younger generation to respect the advice of parents, grandparents and respect the elders.
7: Let all our compatriots work together to nurture the elderly, the elderly, the disabled, the poor, the homeless, to have a suitable place to live in each community, to be able to build a center for the elderly, especially in pagodas, temples, religions. That can help provide shelter or food as much as possible.
8: All public and private radio and television stations, as well as all news agencies, please help to widely disseminate the achievements and achievements that the elderly have left for the next generation, as well as for society as a whole, and to promote activities that Show care and promote the well-being of the elderly in our Cambodian society. Today Ben 2! Discover the history of Pchum Ben and Kan Ben, which are the traditions of the Khmer people
(Phnom Penh): Workers at some factories in Phnom Penh see that the $ 4 wage increase for 2024 is not much, but it is a good thing for them at a time when the world, including Cambodia, is facing And the global economic crisis.
After 20 rounds of talks on September 28, 2023, the minimum wage for workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags sector has been found in 2024. The minimum wage for 2024 is $ 204 per month. Of that, $ 2 is an agreement between the employer and the workers, and another $ 2 is provided by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Hun Manet.
Workers working in a number of factories in Phnom Penh have expressed satisfaction with the outcome of the wage negotiations. They understand that the extra $ 4 is not much, but at a time when the world is in crisis, raising wages is a good thing.
Touch Srey Nich, a worker at the Gon Yang Label garment factory, expressed satisfaction with the pay rise. For Touch Srey Nich, having a job now is important for him today. Srey Nich did not want a big pay rise and the factory had to close.
The other two workers at Canadia Park Garment Factory, Ying Yi, also agree with Srey Nich. Ms. Chanthou and Ms. Champa found that the increase of $ 4 in 2024 is a good thing. They will be paid more than they are now when there is overtime. Chanthou and Champa also see that in the current situation, demanding higher wages is not a good thing.
Wage negotiations for 2024 are one of the toughest. Originally, the factory owners intended to raise only $ 1. However, under the coordination of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, especially the urging of His Majesty the King Hun Manet, the factory owners agreed to increase it to $ 2. The increase of $ 2 by Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet is seen as a small amount for the workers, therefore, Samdech also added another $ 2.
The workers see that the struggle to raise wages and increase wages by Samdech Hun Sen Manet is a manifestation of Samdech's high feelings and concern for the well-being of workers and the desire for livelihood. Theirs better.
Despite expressing satisfaction with the $ 204 wage increase in 2024, the worker also asked Hun Manet to set out measures to prevent an increase in room rates. They rent accommodation.
It should be noted that Cambodia currently has 1,332 factories in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags industry and employs about 840,000 workers with an annual income of nearly $ 3 billion.
Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, claimed that the current wage increase makes Cambodia the only exporter of garments, shoes, bags and other items that have raised wages for workers.
Heng Sour said that the minimum wage and other benefits combined, regardless of overtime, workers can earn between $ 221 to $ 232 per month.
