Romania says signs of renewed air violations during Russian drone strike on Ukraine
BUYAPADA: Romania's Defense Ministry says there have been signs of violations of its airspace during a Russian drone strike overnight on neighboring Ukrainian civilian infrastructure. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Saturday, September 30, 2023.
The Romanian Defense Ministry has confirmed that the Romanian army's radar surveillance system has identified a violation of national airspace with a signal to Galati. So far, no fragments have been found on Romanian territory, and the search is continuing this Saturday.
In the past, NATO and Romanian officials have said there was no evidence that Russia's attack near the border was a deliberate attack on Romania, but considered it "careless and destabilizing".
After withdrawing from the Black Sea grain deal in mid-July, Russia began attacking Ukrainian ports and warehouses across the Danube via Romania, a major alternative export route. The wreckage of a Russian drone was found three times in separate Romanian territories this September, posing a security risk as NATO members vowed to protect each other.
