(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mean Sati, a member of the NEC, reminded Cambodians living in communes who have just reached the age of 18 as of December 31, 2023 (born before or born on January 1, 2023). 2006) and those who have not yet registered to vote or have moved to a new commune / sangkat to register to vote. Vote name.
Mr. Mean Sati made this call as he chaired a meeting with stakeholders to announce the start of the voter list and voter registration review, voter registration procedures, filing, receipt and resolution of complaints related to Voter Registration 2023.
On that occasion, Mr. Mean Sati stated that the examination of the 2023 voter list and voter registration will last for 19 days from the first day until October 19, 2023 at the commune hall and some locations in the commune. Neighborhood. This work is done every day, including Saturday and Sunday morning from 7:00 to 11:30 noon and in the afternoon from 2:00 to 5:30 pm.
If the address on the Khmer Nationality Identity Card is in the commune where the people are living and apply for registration, the Voter Registration Team will arrange for registration in accordance with NEC procedures. If the address in the Khmer identity card is different from the commune / sangkat where the citizen is applying for registration, the citizen must bring a family book or residence book or a certificate of residence in the commune / sangkat that applies for registration.
Regarding the receipt and settlement of complaints related to voter registration, HE Mean Sithi stated that any person or representative has the right to complain to the Commune / Sangkat Council or the NEC or the Constitutional Council on any issues. Involved in voter registration if there is evidence of irregularities as stated in the election law, regulations and procedures for reviewing the voter list and annual voter registration and / or internal regulations of the NEC.
He added that the mechanism and authority to file, receive and resolve complaints related to voter registration have three levels: Commune / Sangkat Council, NEC and Constitutional Council, and the decision of the Constitutional Council. It is a final decision to close the protest route.
Finally, on behalf of the NEC, Mr. Mean Sati called on the people to check the voter list and register to vote and sincerely hope that through joint efforts and with high responsibility will achieve success. A house was completely electrocuted in Po Sen Chey district, killing a retired officer, and the police used more than 10 water trucks
(Phnom Penh): The case of a house fire caused a surprise at 23:40 on September 29, 2023, at the point of the concrete road in Tek Panho village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that in accordance with the order of Major General Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner. Instructed the specialized force of the Office of Fire Prevention, Rescue and Rescue to pay close attention to the rescue operation in a timely manner.
Upon receiving the order, Colonel Prohm Yorn led the fire brigade directly to all targets in Phnom Penh to intervene and spray water in time to prevent the fire from continuing to the houses of the people. Nearby.
In the above operation, the specialized police force used 12 fire trucks, including 08 fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Office, used 8 water trucks and 4 auxiliary vehicles from the 70th Brigade. Use water.
Colonel Prohm Yorn confirmed that in the case of the fire above, the stone structure under the tree on the size (6 meters by 12 meters) burned completely and will not cause the fire to spread to the neighbor's house.
For the above case, the specialized police force took full control at 12:00 midnight on September 30, 2023. The incident left one person dead in the house and the cause was an electric shock. Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth and Japanese Ambassador meet to discuss ways to further enhance cooperation
(Phnom Penh): At the Office of the Council of Ministers, HE Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, on September 29, 2023, received Mr. UENO Atsushi, Ambassador of Japan to the Kingdom of Cambodia and his colleagues. And discuss work.
At the same time, the Ambassador also congratulated and expressed optimism that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, headed by His Majesty the King Hun Manet, will continue to ensure peace, prosperity and development for the people of Cambodia. And expressed its strong commitment to contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts in socio-economic development.
The Ambassador praised the efforts and long-term vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia and considered Cambodia as a model country in terms of the evolution of the banking payment system.
In response, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister, stated that Japan is a good, close and loyal friend of Cambodia in all circumstances and highly appreciated the good relations and cooperation in the fields of politics, diplomacy, economy, trade, society, technology and Recent developments.
He said that Cambodia and Japan have a long-standing relationship, and 2023 is the 70th anniversary of diplomatic ties between our two countries. At present, the relationship and cooperation between the two countries have been constantly strengthened and expanded and upgraded to a comprehensive strategic partnership.
Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth expressed his deep gratitude to the Government of Japan and the people of Japan for their contribution to the socio-economic development and development of Cambodia from the search for peace to the rehabilitation and development of Cambodia.
The Permanent Deputy Prime Minister highlighted the possibility of strengthening cooperation with the Government of Japan in improving the effectiveness of governance, building a strong public institution that responds to the needs of the people, and especially in drafting laws and establishing legal frameworks. Consistent, efficient, easy to implement and support socio-economic development.
As a way forward, in the context of the global challenges of socio-economic transformation and the uncertain geopolitical situation, the Permanent Deputy Prime Minister and Ambassador expressed confidence that Cambodia and Japan will continue to strengthen ties for For the benefit of the people of both countries, even in difficult circumstances.
Finally, the Permanent Deputy Prime Minister reiterated his gratitude to the Ambassador and Government of Japan, in particular for their assistance to the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) and Support the legacy project of the Legal Documentation Center related to the ECCC. The Ambassador expressed his pleasure to continue the development cooperation of Cambodia.
