(Phnom Penh): The Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprises has requested the Royal Government to amend the Royal Decree on the Establishment of the Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprises in line with the current context, as this Royal Decree is almost two decades old.
The proposal of the Chamber of Commerce and Industry was made by Mrs. Oknha Keo Mom, Chairman of the Board, on the occasion of Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Technology, Science and Innovation, allowing a courtesy call and discussion on the afternoon of the 30th. September 2023.
The Minister strongly supported and agreed to this proposal, stating that he would appoint a professional officer to do this work.
He said that if he wanted the Royal Decree to be updated, he also asked Duke Keo Mom to work with relevant officials of the Ministry of Industry on how to organize this organization in the future, and he would ask the head of the Royal Government to know. Also.
Tycoon Keo Mom said that there are four points that the Chamber of Commerce and Microfinance proposed to the Minister of Industry in this meeting, including:
1: Propose the establishment of the Cambodian Business Center, which will be a gathering place for locally produced Cambodian products for the Chamber of Commerce and micro-enterprises to promote and sell widely on both national and international levels, requesting the Ministry of Technical Support of Production Have a definition.
2. To request the Legal Officer of the Ministry of Industry to amend the Royal Decree establishing the Chamber of Commerce and Industry Microfinance, which has been in place since 2005.
3. Request the Ministry of Industry to coordinate the integration of the Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprises to participate in the working group of the Royal Government Forum with the private sector.
