In addition, Mr. Eang Sophalleth stated that the production of large quantities of plastic waste, combined with limited control measures, has caused many environmental problems, such as: air pollution, greenhouse gas emissions by burning plastic waste, affecting human and animal health. By increasing the presence of microplastics in public water sources and endangering biodiversity from large amounts of plastic waste in seas and oceans.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth added that in response to the strong growth in the use of plastic materials, especially plastic bags in the past, the Ministry of Environment, in collaboration with relevant ministries and institutions, has introduced measures such as: increasing special taxes on imports of products and 7% to 10% plastic material and charge for plastic bags (400 Riel per bag) in supermarkets and business centers in order to reduce the use of plastic bags.
At the same time, he stated that in order to continue to introduce and implement measures to reduce the use of plastic bags, the Ministry of Environment in the seventh mandate of the Royal Government has set the priority work is to raise awareness and participation of the people. Aims to change the attitudes and living habits of Cambodians in a clean, green and carbon neutral environment.
(Pursat): From September 27 to 30, 2023, Pursat province has been suffering from floods caused by flooding in some areas in Veal Veng district, Phnom Kravanh district and continue to flow to attack housing infrastructure. And the homes of some people living along the canals of rivers and streams in Pursat and Kandieng districts.
In this situation, His Excellency Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, has been leading the overall force, the total mobility, the leadership at all levels, civil servants, the Armed Forces and the youth of all divisions. The force intervened to stop the flood, evacuate the people to safety and bring food to distribute to the people who are drowning everywhere.
According to Mr. Keo Vay, Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Pursat Province, this morning, September 30, 2023, the floodwaters are currently attacking Pursat City and Kandieng District by overflowing the river. Stung Lech, red gravel roads, schools, hospitals, pagodas and houses of some people who live along the canals of the river on the outskirts of the city and there are leaks cutting off some bridges and roads.
According to the preliminary report of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee on the impact of rainfall in Pursat province as of September 29, 2023, the flooding caused flooding in 4 cities / districts, including: Veal Veng district, Phnom Kravanh district. Pursat city and Kandeang district and affect 21 communes / sangkats and 69 villages.
It should be noted that on September 29, 2023, HE Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management and Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister of Mines and Energy and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group, were present yesterday. Pursat inspected the situation directly and jointly set out measures to help the affected people.
This is in response to the recommendation of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who instructed the relevant provincial governors to monitor and grasp the impact of floods in their localities, especially to pay attention to rescue people. Citizens and property of the affected people.
