(Kampong Chhnang): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, said that from September 1 to 30, 2023, 1,262,605 students participated in the campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags" issued by the Ministry of Environment.
Minister Eang Sophalleth made this remark during the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Environment and the Cambodian Red Cross, Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration, Pursat Provincial Administration, Kandal Provincial Administration and launched a campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not Do not use plastic bags "Kampong Chhnang on September 30, 2023.
The Minister of Environment said: "This campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags has been supported and implemented by school management, teachers and students in general education institutions in some provinces. Subsequently. In fact, in almost a month, nearly one million students from more than 9,000 schools in 20 capitals and provinces have volunteered for the campaign.
At the same time, Mr. Eang Sophalleth said that from September 23, some private sector, especially 15 garment factories in Phnom Penh, Kandal and Svay Rieng, with more than 7,500 workers also began to volunteer. With the Ministry of Environment to implement the campaign not to use plastic bags at least one day a week.
It should be noted that the campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags" began on September 1, 2023, initially organized in 44 schools across the district in Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province. There are 549 teachers, 263 females and 18,735 students, 9,353 females. To date, this campaign has been continuously implemented in schools in all capitals, provinces and factories.
Ministry of Environment, Cambodian Red Cross, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat and Kandal Provinces sign MoU and launch a campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags" in Kampong Chhnang
(Kampong Chhnang): The Ministry of Environment, in collaboration with the Cambodian Red Cross, Kampong Chhnang, Kandal and Pursat Provinces, signed a Memorandum of Understanding and launched a campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags" in all schools throughout Kampong Chhnang.
