Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al sets out 15 priority directions for land management, urban planning and construction in the new legislature
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, outlined 15 strategic priorities of the Ministry for the 7th mandate in a meeting with the civil servants of the Ministry of Land Management. Urban planning and construction on the afternoon of September 29, 2023.
The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction will continue to work on the key tasks for the seventh legislature in response to the priorities set out in the Pentagon Strategy, the implementation of the CPP's political program for nation-building and defense in 2023. 2028.
Based on the priorities of the pentagon strategy in the fourth pentagon, the fourth angle, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction focuses on 15 policy priorities, including:
1: Work to develop more realistic policies and implement them towards results
2: The work of preparing the legal framework by reviewing, improving, supplementing and updating the legal documents more fully in accordance with the new context and realistic, consistent, especially the preparation of some important draft laws, including: 1: Land law by Must be completely redefined, 2: Law on Land Management and Urbanization as a new law ever, 3: Law on housing as a new law ever
3: Building modern public institutions and administrations that allow the daily work system to run automatically and efficiently
4: Promoting modern public services and data management to provide fast, transparent, efficient, convenient and reliable services
5: Land registration work to continue to provide land titles to the people quickly to be the basis of economic resources and security of land tenure
6: Land management in accordance with the direction of socio-economic development, effective and sustainable, especially in accordance with the economic corridor, based on conservation areas, heritage areas, agricultural areas, industrial areas, residential areas, public lands for conservation, land for public parks, green areas, etc. .
7. Development of urban planning through the development of cities, towns, cities, districts, Khans, communes, sangkats throughout the capital-province in accordance with the concept of clean cities, smart cities and desirable cities.
8. Contemporary Khmer architecture by promoting the construction by using more Khmer style, modern Khmer style, contemporary and more active movement to promote Khmer architectural style as well as strengthen the quality and safety of construction.
9: Housing work by arranging suitable housing to live in and have a harmonious environment through the preparation of house models for basic use, as well as the preparation of rural towns, housing improvements, old villages and housing models for new locations.
10: Inspection and internal audit to achieve the objectives of building a modern public administration, orientation of work more appropriate to public functions, increase work efficiency, especially to improve the quality of services and increase efficiency in resolving land disputes quickly and clearly. Ready to get registered fast
11: Housing, social land concessions through sustainable housing development, social land, especially agricultural production, social protection system, education and health services, as well as social services that can support community development, especially sustainable livelihoods and the family economy.
12: International cooperation framework in the spirit of the best interests of the people
13: Human resource development through further capacity building on technical skills as well as leadership management for more active participation in modern administration and institutional capacity building
14: Raising awareness in the field of land management, urban planning and construction to further enhance Cambodia's prestige on the international stage, which allows the national and international community to have more trust in Cambodia and provide more comprehensive information and knowledge to the public.
15. Work on political security and economic security by strengthening cooperation between all development partners and ASEAN partners in order to maintain a multilateral position and balance domestic and foreign policy, and strive to resolve issues that may affect stability. Politics.
