IOM Cambodia to Establish Digital Health Cooperation with Ministry of Health
Her statement was made during a courtesy call and discussion with the Minister of Health, Professor Chheang Ra, on the afternoon of September 29, 2023 at the Ministry.
The Head of Mission informed the Minister that IOM has been cooperating closely with the National Center, relevant departments, national programs, supporting the Ministry of Health in formulating national policies on migrant health and contributing to the development of the National Strategic Plan on Immigrant Health 2022-2030. .
Through the above national policy and national strategic plan, IOM has supported the operation of a number of national and sub-national migrant health technical working groups, including supporting the establishment of a sub-national health technical working group for migrants. Phnom Penh, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey.
The Minister thanked the IOM for its contribution to the health of migrants in Cambodia and requested the IOM to further strengthen and expand this cooperation beyond the health of migrants in Cambodia, such as disease research. Infections that can occur on immigrants to Cambodia, single health work, tuberculosis, AIDS, and digital health work.
In response, the IOM Mission Chair expressed her excitement at the support of the Ministry of Health, especially the Minister, stating that the proposal was a key recommendation for the IOM. The action plan continues to work with the Ministry of Health, promising that she will soon establish this digital health cooperation with the Ministry based on the experience of the IOM, a UN body.
Please be informed that in this meeting, she also congratulated and wished the Minister on the occasion of gaining the trust of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate to be appointed Minister of Health.
