North Korean leader Kim Jong Un this week, through a parliamentary session, told his people about his ambition to ally with countries in the face of the United States in the "new Cold War" and even show the world. He wants to increase the production of nuclear weapons. Pyongyang considers itself a country within the circle of nuclear powers.
The North Korean state news agency KCNA reported at a summit of the North Korean People's Assembly that North Korean lawmakers had unanimously approved a clause in the new constitution to "guarantee the country's right to freedom of expression." "Make and develop, prevent war and maintain peace in the region and the world by developing nuclear weapons rapidly and at a high level."
In a speech to the National Assembly, Kim Jong Un said, "North Korea's policy of building a nuclear force is based on a" permanent state law that no one is allowed to oppose. " All ". Kim stressed the need to "move forward with work for increasing nuclear weapons production and diversifying the means of nuclear strikes."
Kim pointed to what he described as "an increasing threat posed by US hostility and the expansion of US military cooperation with South Korea and Japan." North Korean leaders have accused the United States, South Korea and Japan of co-creating a new NATO in Asia, a cause of war and aggression.
Kim said the expansion of US military cooperation with South Korea and Japan was indeed the worst threat and it was not a rhetorical or imaginary threat.
The North Korean leader urged North Korean diplomats to "further strengthen solidarity with the nations that stand up against the United States and against Western hegemony strategies."
In response to what is happening in North Korea, the South Korean Unification Ministry, which oversees relations with North Korea, said North Korea's constitutional amendment reiterated Kim Jong Un's will still not. Abandon its nuclear weapons program and North Korean leaders, as well as its relentless commitment to further increase its weapons arsenal.
In a statement, South Korea said it would continue to expand its military cooperation with the United States and Japan and work more closely with other international partners to increase pressure on North Korea. Legs to give up its nuclear ambitions.
