Minister Neth Pheakdra Reminds Journalists to Increase Capacity to Strengthen Work Efficiency and Public Confidence
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, presided over the final visit of the Mekong-Lanchang Journalists' visit program under the theme "Joint River and Common Future" organized under Mekong-Lan Cooperation. Chang this morning, September 29, 2023 in Sihanoukville.
Mr. Neth Phatra on that occasion said that Mekong Lan Chan has six countries that share river water. In addition, there are a number of other countries that are partners in order to protect the conservation of the Mekong River that we share. He called on these countries to continue to strengthen cooperation in disseminating and exchanging views and sharing true information against false information to avoid hostility.
At the same time, the Minister reminded journalists to work hard to strengthen their capacity to ensure work efficiency, that is, journalists must have the ability to report true information and produce rich, high-quality, clear and comprehensive information to fight fake news. He considers fake news to be a global problem that needs to be addressed together.
He added that the Ministry of Information has set out three priority missions: 1: Information security issues, 2: Providing quality information and 3: Information that is safe and reliable.
Meanwhile, in response to the current situation of journalists, the Minister gave three perspectives, including: all must be under the roof of the law, collect ideas as input to compile a professional code of conduct, which is a common practice and the perpetrators. Be responsible before the law.
He also instructed all journalists to adhere to the manners, attitudes and dignified character, to be worthy, respectful and valued by the people around them, and to act as true informants from the people to the government and from The Royal Government to the people.
