Acting Head of State believes that the new Royal Government of Cambodia and Thailand will continue to take care of the historic achievements that the previous Royal Government has worked together (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State Cambodia has expressed confidence that the new Royal Government of Cambodia and Thailand will continue to pay attention to the historic achievements that previous governments have worked together to achieve.
He said this on the afternoon of September 28, 2023, when he received Thai Prime Minister Setha Thavisin at the Senate on the occasion of the Prime Minister leading a delegation to pay his first official visit to Cambodia.
On this wonderful occasion, the Acting Head of State expressed his pleasure to receive information on the success of the talks between the Prime Ministers of the two countries on the morning of September 28, 2023. Samdech is confident that the new governments of the two countries will continue to take care of the historic achievements that previous governments have worked together in the past.
Samdech encouraged the new governments of the two countries to continue to promote and coordinate existing mechanisms to implement effectively, especially trade between the two countries to achieve the target of 15 billion US dollars in bilateral trade. In 2025.
At the same time, the Acting Head of State is confident that the new governments of the two countries will continue to explore new mechanisms for the causes of the two countries' progress to bring prosperity, prosperity, peace and long-term stability between the two countries. As well as for regional and international.
The Acting Head of State brought to the Prime Minister of Thailand a royal message of greetings and deep respect for His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia and His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia and The Cambodian leadership addressed the King and Queen and to all the top leaders of the Kingdom of Thailand.
The Acting Head of State expressed his appreciation and congratulations for the socio-economic development of Thailand and wished all the best to the King and Queen and the national leaders and people of Thailand for their development. The country is getting stronger, more prosperous, more advanced and more prestigious on the international stage.
On behalf of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Her Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, and on behalf of His Majesty the King, the Acting Head of State extended his warmest welcome to the Prime Minister of The Kingdom of Thailand, which led the delegation, paid its first official visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Acting Head of State congratulated Setha Thavisin on his election as the 30th Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand by the Thai Parliament and was approved by the King of Thailand. Ordained to be the Prime Minister.
On that occasion, Mr. Setha Thavisin expressed his deep gratitude to the Acting Head of State for taking the time to meet with him and the delegation. The Prime Minister expressed his pleasure to pay his first visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia. He hopes that in the future, the two countries and peoples will further enhance relations and cooperation with each other.
The Prime Minister briefed the Acting Prime Minister on the outcome of a meeting between His Excellency and His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia on diplomacy, investment, national defense and labor issues in Cambodia. Thailand to make it easier for workers to stay and work.
The Prime Minister expressed his pleasure that the two kings had good relations. Among them, Princess Maha Chakrei Sarinthon provided scholarships to more than 2,000 Cambodian students studying in Thailand.
The Prime Minister hopes that in the future, investment between the two countries will increase more than currently planned. At the same time, he is confident that from now on, the two countries will have better relations and cooperation in industry, economy, technology and other fields. Army unveils results of 13th Indo-Pacific Army Commander-in-Chief Conference in New Delhi
The roundtable discussion, which was attended by the Commander-in-Chief of the Army and representatives of the Commander-in-Chief of the 30 countries in the Indo-Pacific region, focused on 1: Strengthening mutual cooperation, 2: Role Of military diplomacy in crisis mitigation; 3: The need for self-reliance for army modernization; 4. The role of the army in maintaining regional security and stability.
In each bilateral meeting, all counterparts discussed and agreed to promote cooperation activities on all existing mechanisms and focus on a number of priority tasks, including: 1: Exchange visits or study visits for officers at all levels, 2: Training, 3: Joint exercises in counter-terrorism and disaster relief operations, 4: Expertise exchange, and 5: Cooperation on mine action in humanitarian work.
