In order to organize the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly on October 1, 2023, and to disseminate to the Cambodian people of all ages to better understand the meaning of this day, Samdech Hun Sen introduced the organization of this day as follows: Under:
1: The theme of the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the 25th International Day of the Elderly, October 1, 2023, is defined as "Helping the elderly is helping us all."
2: The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of the Cambodian National Committee for the Elderly shall cooperate with the Ministries, Development Partners, Non-Governmental Organizations and relevant international organizations to celebrate the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly on October 1, 2023. Celebrated.
3. The Capital and Provincial Administration must organize the celebration of the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly on October 1, 2023, creating conditions for government officials, the Armed Forces at all levels, monks, clergy, grandparents and the people. All ages have contributed to the new normal trajectory to increase awareness of the importance of the National Policy on the Elderly 2017-2030.
5. In accordance with the health measures, all ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations shall meet with the elderly in accordance with the national policy on the elderly at the local level of pagodas, temples, and religions by bringing generous donations to help the elderly. Disability, poverty, helplessness, etc.
8. The Ministry of Information must introduce all public and private media to widely disseminate the content of activities on the occasion of the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly, October 1, 2023.
10. The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, the Cambodian National Committee for the Elderly and the National Committee for Organizing National and International Festivals shall introduce this circular and summarize the work results to the Royal Government.
