The success of the Bakong system is becoming a model for the development of digital systems in many countries.
(Phnom Penh): The success of the National Bank of Cambodia's payment system is becoming a model for the development of digital systems in many countries. In fact, the system is helping to quickly increase the reputation of Japanese company Soramitsu and make this company. Received projects from several central banks to develop digital payment systems in the style of Bakong system.
This development reflects the right decision of the management of the National Bank of Cambodia to use blockchain technology to develop the Bakong system through collaboration with the innovative company Soramitsu, and demonstrates the modernity and high security of the Bakong system. Transfer money from one bank to another easily and quickly.
The prominence of the Bakong system established by the National Bank of Cambodia has often been highlighted on the international stage by leaders of major financial institutions and elites in major countries.
The positive evolution of the Bakong payment system has made Soramitsu one of the potential companies to develop digital payment systems in Asia. The company has rapidly expanded its operations around the world, including in the United States and Switzerland. With a total of 150 employees.
In addition to the existing success, the National Bank of Cambodia is continuing to develop the Bakong system for remittances and cross-border payments, and has made significant progress. In fact, the National Bank of Cambodia has successfully connected cross-border payment and remittance systems with Thailand, China, Malaysia and Laos, while connections with Vietnam and India are set to be launched in the near future.
The National Bank of Cambodia has already signed bilateral Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs) with countries such as Fiji, Solomon Islands and plans to sign MoUs with Myanmar, East Timor and Rwanda to expand cross-border payment connectivity. Extensive.
"The will of the young leaders of the National Bank of Cambodia in their 30s and 40s, combined with the innovative ideas of newly established Japanese companies, has brought a wide range of financial services benefits to the people of Cambodia," he said. "In rural areas where bank branches are not yet operational."
