Veal Veng, Kandeang, Phnom Kravanh and Pursat districts almost every year during the rainy season when heavy rains often cause flooding in some areas along the river in Pursat province. Pursat Provincial Governor Khoy Rida visited the affected areas and put in place measures to prevent accidents to the lives of the people. In particular, lead the authorities and forces to prevent the saliva of the Pursat River to avoid serious impact on people's homes.
On the morning of Friday, September 29, 2023, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, and Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister of Mines and Energy and Chairman of the Royal Government Assistance Team, visited Pursat province. Pursat to check the situation directly and jointly put out measures to help the affected people.
Khoy Rida said the flooding in Kandeang and Pursat districts was due to heavy rains two days ago in the Cardamom Mountains and flooding in Veal Veng district. After the rains receded in the upper part, the water flowed into the Pursat River and partially flooded in Pursat city and Kandieng district.
Senior Minister Kun Kim assessed that if there was no more rain in the upper part, the flood situation in Pursat and Kandieng districts would be alleviated in the near future. However, under the order of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, he and all relevant authorities continue to monitor the situation and put in place some measures to avoid serious consequences. In particular, protect the lives of the people.
Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked the authorities and the armed forces for their joint efforts to help the victims. The Senior Minister also instructed the relevant authorities to continue to strictly follow the orders of the Prime Minister to help the people affected by the floods this rainy season.
According to the report of Pursat province, the flood affected 4 cities / districts, including: Veal Veng district, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat city and Kandieng district, affecting 21 communes / sangkats and 69 villages.
