The celebration of the Wildlife Alliance came after local authorities organized a celebration of the anniversary of the establishment of the Stung Areng and Indigenous Ecotourism Community on September 26, 2023. Located in Chumnab Commune, Thmar Bang District, Koh Kong Province.
The event was presided over by Mr. Sok Sothy, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province, Ms. Dr. Sou Vanna Gonlet, Executive Director of Wildlife Alliance, and was attended by Mr. Pheng Phal, Deputy Governor of Thmar Bang District, Village, Commune Authority and members of Stung Areng Ecotourism Community. And especially the indigenous people, as well as more than 400 participants.
The purpose of this celebration is to promote and preserve the indigenous identity and heritage of the Chung indigenous community, to link the cultural identity of the Chung indigenous people together with the tourism activities of the Stung Areng ecotourism community to attract tourists. National and international visitors to the Areng area, which contributes to increasing the income of the people in the three communes.
