Garment wages in Cambodia higher than 5 countries in the region
(Phnom Penh): According to a report from the International Labor Organization, Cambodia has the highest wage in the garment sector than five other countries in the region.
In 2023, in Cambodia, workers will receive an average wage of $ 217 to $ 259 per month, excluding overtime and other benefits, including benefits from the National Social Security Fund. Wages are higher than in Vietnam, Sri Lanka, Bangladesh, Laos and Myanmar.
According to Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, the increase makes Cambodia the only exporter of garments, shoes, bags and other items that have raised wages for workers.
It should be noted that Cambodia currently has 1,332 factories in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags industry and employs about 840,000 workers with an annual income of nearly 3 billion dollars.
