Economist: Although the wages of workers in the garment sector increased by 4 dollars, but the price is huge, now both Cambodia and the world are experiencing economic crisis
(Phnom Penh): Economic analysts say that although the wages of workers in the garment sector increased by 4 dollars, which seems to be a small amount, but the price is high because now Cambodia as well as the world is experiencing economic crisis and employers. Is being affected by declining exports.
Wages for workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags for 2024 have been achieved at $ 204, of which the National Minimum Wage Council has voted $ 202 and Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia. An additional $ 2, which increases wages for 2024 by $ 4, compared to $ 200 in 2023.
Cambodia is the only exporter of these products in Asia that has raised the minimum wage for 2024. According to Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor
He said that although the wage did not meet the needs of employees and union representatives, as well as the current market price situation, but in difficult times, Cambodia can negotiate to raise wages is a good result and Accept all together.
He understands that this is a base salary that is appropriate for the current situation, because if combined with the wages that workers work overtime will be able to get more. At the same time, raising wages at this level will make employers more receptive and able to continue working together harmoniously while they are being affected by declining orders.
He noted that compared to neighboring countries such as Laos, Myanmar, Bangladesh, etc., see the wages of Cambodia has the highest rate. If the economic situation changes for the better, wages in Cambodia will increase even more.
He added that negotiations to raise wages in this circumstance could also satisfy overseas buyers, as the government has taken into account the well-being of workers.
Please be informed that the National Minimum Wage Council has negotiated 20 times from 20 August 2023 to 28 September 2023, based on the principles of democracy, friendship and co-operation. Transparency and win-win operations. Spokesman of the Ministry of Economy: In 2023, the Royal Government is ready to use the $ 672 million budget for social and economic interventions, including $ 350 million for poor families
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Meas Sok Sen San, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, confirmed that the Royal Government led by His Majesty Hun Manet has taken into account the lives and livelihoods of the people. The government has set aside $ 672 million for social and economic intervention, including $ 350 million for poor families.
He added that in 2023, the Royal Government is ready to spend $ 672 million on social and economic interventions, including:
* $ 350 million in cash aid for poor families and family package support * $ 60 million in cash for vulnerable families during inflationary pressures * $ 100 million in cash for labor infrastructure for job creation infrastructure * Budget To contribute to the development of economic growth strategy of $ 46 million * $ 39 million to support the rehabilitation and development of the Ronta Ek area.
"In the $ 672 million budget for social and economic intervention in the first six months of 2023, we have spent about $ 508 million to improve people's lives," he said. "People will stimulate economic growth."
At the same time, according to the National Council for Social Protection, for the welfare and convenience of the people, the Royal Government spends $ 930 million per year on social protection in Cambodia.
In the past, in the field of social assistance, the Royal Government of Cambodia has implemented national social assistance programs such as:
1: Cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old, as of July 2023, there are a total of 325 679 beneficiaries,
2: School feeding program with a total benefit of approximately 300,000 students in 1,113 target schools, which includes school feeding program using community-based agricultural products with a total of 110,645 students ,
3: Scholarship program for poor primary and secondary students with a total benefit of 263,751 students, 4: Large-scale post-closure cash social assistance program in Phnom Penh, Takhmao city, Kandal province and Preah city Sihanouk of Sihanoukville with 129,666 beneficiary families,
5: Labor cash program covering 20 target provinces
6: Allowance program for workers whose contracts were suspended during the Kovid-19 crisis, with about 400,000 workers benefiting from more than 700 factories in the garment, tourism and film industries.
