Pursat Provincial Department of Water Resources issues notification on the rising water level of Pursat River
(Pursat): After observing the weather conditions, it was found that on September 23, 2023, a low pressure system occurred across the Kingdom of Cambodia.
According to an active pressure forecast (located in the South China Sea), the upper low pressure system will move into the Cambodia-Laos border and continue from east to west along the Dangrek Mountains. The active low pressure movement as described above may occur in the northeastern highlands, northern highlands and northwestern central lowlands with moderate to heavy rainfall from September 26-28, 2023.
In Pursat province, the water level of the Pursat River has risen to an alarming level.
In order to be prepared for natural disasters and floods along the river in Pursat province, the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology would like to inform that after monitoring the weather conditions, it was raining in the mountainous area. Cardamom, the Arai River and the Thom River are high on the Pursat River. The influence of the above river will cause the Pursat River to gradually increase and may cause flooding in Pursat province.
According to the above weather conditions, the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology would like to inform the authorities of municipalities, districts, communes, sangkats at all levels and people throughout Pursat province, especially people living along the Pursat and related rivers, please pay more attention. High to avoid any possible accidents and be prepared to find a safe place to evacuate vulnerable people.
