Workers and employers all satisfied with $ 204 wage increase in 2024
(Phnom Penh): The workers' side has expressed satisfaction with the increase in the minimum wage in textiles, garments, footwear and travel products and bags for 2024, which has been increased to 204 US dollars per month. Employers, on the other hand, are also happy to accept this figure, although orders in 2023 are down 19 percent.
Workers' Wages for 2024 have been increased by US $ 4, of which US $ 2 has been approved by the National Council for Minimum Wages (through elections) and US $ 2 has been approved by His Majesty King Hun Manet. More. This means that the minimum wage for workers in 2024 will increase to $ 204 per month and will be implemented from January 1, 2024 onwards.
After concluding the discussion on the afternoon of September 28, 2023, Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and a representative of the Royal Government, confirmed that the amount of 204 US dollars, including other benefits, workers will receive an average of $ 221 and up.
Kim Chansamnang, a representative of the workers' side, said that the workers were satisfied with the $ 204 minimum wage. "The wage increase is to get more for the workers, but we also need to look at the competition with the same export partners, because if we demand a higher wage increase, it will affect the competition of the workers," he said. Cambodia.
However, union representatives also requested that the Royal Government, as well as the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, help reduce costs, retain workers' benefits, and curb rising prices for other daily necessities, such as rental housing. Clean water, electricity, goods for food and so on.
The workers also raised 15 points, including related to the connection of clean water and electricity is not enough for workers to stay, and proposed a reasonable price that can help reduce Workers' expenses.
Mr. Nang Sothy, the representative of the employer (boss), said that the employer is in a position to accept the $ 2, while the Prime Minister also added another $ 2. He said that the increase in wages also has some impact, such as increasing the cost of each product, but also received a compromise on reducing logistics costs from the Royal Government.
"Orders from Cambodia in 2023 are down 19 percent from 2022, while the major markets for Cambodia are Europe, the United States and Japan," Nang Sothy said.
Minister Heng Sour also stated that raising the minimum wage is important, but the next important thing is to try to reduce the burden of workers 'costs, because if the wage increase and not reduce workers' costs. Will make workers less money.
"The ministry will work with relevant stakeholders to reduce workers' costs and work with local authorities to curb rising rents to ensure higher wages," he said. The rest do not go up, but have to spend it all.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Closes a New Framework Training Course
(Banteay Meanchey): On the morning of September 28, 2023, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Sithi Loh presided over the closing ceremony of a new framework training course on the spot and handed over a certificate to the Municipal Police Inspectorate. 9 districts to work in the 9 local administrative police stations of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police
Please be informed that the closing ceremony of the training course at this place, there were a total of 184 participants, 55 females, who completed the one-month course from August 28, 2023 to September 28, 2023 at the Police Commission. Banteay Meanchey Province.
