(Phnom Penh): The World Bank is committed to continuing cooperation with the Ministry of Rural Development on the maintenance and construction of rural infrastructure, such as providing additional funding for better rural road maintenance projects.
In order to be in line with the first phase of the pentagon strategy of the new government, the Ministry has been pursuing its vision of improving the quality and quality of life of the rural people in an economically, social and cultural way through programs. Its four priorities are:
1. Develop physical and transportation infrastructure to better expand rural roads to improve people's economy through the transportation of agricultural products and services to bring rural areas closer to cities.
2. Improve the living conditions of rural communities so that people have access to clean water, maintain good hygiene and live comfortably.
3. Diversify rural economic activities, increase household income through basic skills training to be able to create other occupations in addition to agricultural occupations.
4. Strengthen administrative and general affairs support services by strengthening institutions at both the national and sub-national levels to improve the efficiency of working for the people better and faster.
She went on to mention cooperation on past development projects, some of which are currently underway, and pledged to continue further cooperation, such as providing additional funding for better rural road maintenance projects.
Cambodia has drafted a five-year strategic plan for the development of Chinese language education and sent it to the Chinese side.
(Phnom Penh): Under the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Education of the People's Republic of China on "Development of Chinese Language Curriculum in Public Secondary Schools in Cambodia", Cambodia has prepared a draft Five-year strategic plan for the development of Chinese language education (2023-2028) and also submitted to the Chinese side.
This was confirmed by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, when he received a Chinese delegation from the Center for Cooperation and Exchange of Chinese Languages to pay a courtesy call and discuss work on September 28. 2023.
During the meeting, Dr. Deputy Prime Minister stated that after the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Education of China on "Development of Chinese language curriculum in public secondary schools in Cambodia. »The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has already worked hard to achieve the following results:
In addition, the Deputy Prime Minister requested the Chinese side to expedite the selection criteria for Chinese language teaching contractors, to prepare for the Chinese language test when recruiting Chinese language teaching contractors, and to expedite the review of strategic plans. Development of Chinese language education for 5 years (2023-2028).
In response to the request of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Chinese side agreed to provide additional subsidies for Chinese language teaching contractors, to organize Chinese language tests for Chinese language teaching contractors, as well as to exchange experiences. Involves teaching Chinese to contracted officials teaching Chinese in both Cambodia and China.
Taking this opportunity, the Deputy Prime Minister also thanked the Chinese delegation of the Chinese Center for Cooperation and Exchange for the past cooperation and strongly hoped that the Chinese language curriculum in public secondary schools in Cambodia will Works smoothly and efficiently.
