By Chao Chak Smok, Phnom Penh, September 28, 2023 Opinion: Despite the global crisis, the Royal Government of Cambodia still strives to increase workers' wages
(Phnom Penh): The global crisis caused by Kovid 19, the war in Ukraine and the trade competition of the superpowers have left many countries facing economic uncertainty and economic deficits. This has led to a drop in orders for Asian clothing, footwear, bags and accessories manufacturers.
In such a situation, the producer countries have also decided to suspend the increase in wages for workers for the last two to three years.
For Cambodia, workers receive an average wage of $ 217 to $ 259 per month, excluding overtime and other benefits, including benefits from the National Social Security Fund.
For the Royal Government of Cambodia, in addition to efforts to increase wages and other benefits, and also strive to reduce the costs of workers in the following:
From 2018 to August 2023, workers have been treated many times and many cases without payment, a total of more than 13.6 million cases, equivalent to nearly 382 million Dollars.
Separately, for those who have twins, get an extra 400,000 Riels and 3 twins get an extra 800,000 Riels. In addition, the triplets received an additional 5 million riels from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
Currently, female workers who take 90 days of maternity leave will receive up to 120 percent of their wages, of which 50 percent will be paid by their employers and 70 percent will be paid by the Socialist Party.
This highlighted the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to the living conditions of workers through a mechanism to increase their wages and reduce their monthly expenses to boost people's livelihoods. Better. This also clearly shows the goodwill of the policy of the new government of the new legislature led by Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, focusing on life and work for the people.
