Construction worker slips and falls from 3-storey building, seriously injured in Por Sen Chey district
(Phnom Penh): A construction worker slipped and fell from a three-story building, causing serious injuries while standing on a wall. The above incident happened at 3:35 pm on September 28, 2023 at the construction site on the concrete road, Tek Panha village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the victim, 28-year-old Chap, a construction worker, was staying at a construction site at the scene and was born in Siem Reap province. Prior to the incident, the victim went up to the third floor and stood on the scaffolding and while working, suddenly slipped and fell backwards.
At that time, he was very lucky to fall on the roof of the house of the people next to him, so he did not endanger his life, only to suffer serious head injuries. Immediately after the incident, the victim was taken down by colleagues and taken to a private clinic.
