Heavy rains in northern Vietnam flood many roads in Hanoi
HANOI: Heavy rains have been pounding northern Vietnam on Thursday, causing flooding and traffic jams across Hanoi. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, July 28, 2023.
Vietnam is a country prone to severe rainstorms and floods. According to Vietnamese government statistics, 451 people were killed or missing last year due to natural disasters such as floods and landslides. Floods have become an increasingly common problem in Hanoi, as roads and drainage systems find it difficult to support a rapidly growing population.
