The Prime Minister of Cambodia and Thailand strongly believe that the cooperation between the two countries will be stronger and stronger (Video inside) That the cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand will be stronger and stronger, as well as bring greater benefits for the two nations and peoples of the two countries.
This confidence was expressed in the bilateral working meeting between Samdech Hun Sen and Mr. Setha Thavisin this morning, Thursday, September 28, 2023. This morning, Setha Thavisin began an official visit to Cambodia. This is the first official visit abroad after he received the confidence of the Thai Parliament on August 22, 2023.
Mr. Setha Thavisin's visit to Cambodia was warmly welcomed by Samdech President Hun Manet. Samdech President Hun Manet and Mr. Setha Thavisin received the trust of the parliaments of their respective countries on the same day. During the day, the two prime ministers also called to congratulate each other. The gesture demonstrated the relationship and closeness between the two prime ministers.
In this morning's face-to-face meeting, Samdech Hun Sen warmly welcomed Mr. Setha Thavisin and the high-level delegation to Cambodia. The Prime Minister praised the Thai Prime Minister for choosing Cambodia as his first country for his official visit as Thai Prime Minister.
The President also reiterated his congratulations to Mr. Setha Thavisin, who was elected Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand on the same day as the election of the Prime Minister.
Mr. Setha Thavisin also expressed his deep gratitude for the warm welcome and hospitality of the fraternity and also personally congratulated Samdech Thipadei who was elected as the Prime Minister of Cambodia for the 7th term of the National Assembly.
At the same time, the two leaders also instructed the relevant ministries and institutions of the two countries to continue to discuss and cooperate for the fruitful cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand for the benefit of both parties.
Please note that Cambodia and Thailand established official diplomatic relations on December 19, 1950. The relationship was discontinued in 1962 and reconnected in 1991. Cambodia and Thailand share a border of about 817 km. Khmer provinces bordering Thailand include: Koh Kong, Pursat, Battambang, Bailin, Banteay Meanchey, Preah Vihear and Oddar Meanchey.
Cambodia currently has a total of 43 border crossings with Thailand to facilitate people-to-people travel, trade, trade, economy and transportation between the two countries. These 43 ports include six seaports, 11 international gates, one bilateral gate, and 14 border gates.
The traditional friendship, good neighborliness and close cooperation in all fields between the two countries have been constantly strengthened and expanded and reached the level of "partnership, peace and prosperity."
Cambodia and Thailand aim to achieve $ 15 billion in joint trade by 2025.
Through this relationship, Thailand is also a country that has provided many scholarships to Cambodian students. From 1995 to March 2023, Princess Maha Chakrei Sirindhorn's Royal Education Support Project has a total of 3,240 Cambodian students receiving scholarships for bachelor's, master's and doctoral degrees, 11 from TICA; 19 others.
As of July 2023, there are 1,528 Cambodian students studying for bachelor's, master's and doctoral degrees in Thailand.
Cambodia and Thailand also have many other areas of cooperation in security and defense, culture, health, tourism, agriculture, employment and vocational training.
To begin with, the President extended a warm welcome to Mr. Setha Thavisin and a high-level delegation to the Kingdom of Cambodia and to select Cambodia as the first country for his official visit as Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand. .
The Prime Minister also expressed his congratulations once again to Mr. Setha Thavisin, who was elected Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand on the same day, coinciding with his election as Prime Minister.
In response, Mr. Setha Thavisin expressed his deep gratitude for the warm welcome and hospitality of the fraternity and also personally congratulated Samdech Thipadei, who was elected Prime Minister of Cambodia for the 7th term of the National Assembly.
Before concluding the talks, the two leaders strongly believed that the Cambodian-Thai cooperation would be more prosperous and stronger.
