Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Assigns Officials to Study Key Rivers at Koh Sotin and Srey Santhor Districts to Further Construction and Prevention of Landslides
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on September 28, 2023, led relevant officials and local authorities to inspect the banks of the river that collapsed in Koh Sotin and Srey Santhor districts.
After the inspection, the provincial governor convened a meeting and assigned professional officers to start studying the collapsed riverbanks to prepare for construction projects to prevent river bank collapses in those areas.
Separately, in Srey Santhor district, there are two facing banks. But these two places have to be studied in Meanchey commune first as the second priority package because they are related to roads, that is, if you want to break up those places, it will cut off the entire communication system in Srey Santhor district. In Koh Andet commune, Srey Santhor district, it is the third priority package.
According to the provincial governor, the construction project to prevent the river bank from collapsing is to use sandbags because it costs less money and is as good as stone or concrete, but not as clean.
According to the provincial governor, the construction time after the study and on the project of the river bank, the above-mentioned challenging areas can start construction in early 2024. Cambodian Red Cross meets with the Ministry of Environment to organize a campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags"
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Red Cross, with Luang Men Norodom Monineath Sihanouk as the Honorary President and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen as the President, on the afternoon of September 27, 2023, held a working discussion with the Ministry of Environment on organizing the campaign. Reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags" which is done online.
The meeting was chaired by Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, and Mr. Ngov Borina and Ms. Mom Thany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment.
During the meeting, the First Deputy Secretary General emphasized that the Cambodian Red Cross will participate in the campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags" on September 30, 2023 in Kampong Chhnang. In the spirit of the Phnom Penh Declaration of the National Association of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies in Southeast Asia and the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategic Plan.
Meanwhile, the First Deputy Secretary General and the leaders of the Ministry of Environment also discussed future cooperation, focusing on three priority tasks: first: reducing the use of plastic, second: replanting trees. By increasing the forest cover by 60% by 2050 and 3: Improving the livelihood of the community by finding other livelihoods that can provide income for the people to avoid deforestation as a source of income.
Ms. Men Neary Sopheak also reminded that the Cambodian Red Cross is everywhere for everyone and the Cambodian Red Cross has always played an important role as an assistant to the public authorities in the field of humanitarian to help the vulnerable and vulnerable. In the 25 capitals and provinces of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
