(Kampong Thom): Leaders of the Ministry of Mines and Energy and professional officers of the General Department of Mineral Resources on September 27, 2023 inspected and studied the operation of a gold mining business in Sochet commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province. From the news that the company has caused some disturbances and problems with people living around the area.
The inspection and study on the gold mining business was led by Mr. Ouch Bora, Secretary of State, Mr. Ing Depola, Director General of the General Department of Mineral Resources, Department of Mines and Energy and officials of the Ministry of Mines and Energy with the participation of local authorities at the provincial level. Districts, communes and villages.
Mr. Ouch Bora said that the inspection of the gold mining business of Let Cheng Mining Development Co., Ltd. to check two points: * Point 1: About the progress of the company's operations by checking the company's compliance. On the technical characteristics and safety of the mine and the environment * Point 2: Related to various problems with people living near the mine.
Mr. Ouch Bora added that in addition to the monitoring and inspection, the Ministry has also been conducting regular monitoring with officials at the site from the Ministry and the Department of Mines and Energy.
After the inspection, Mr. Kong Sitha, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Mineral Resources, emphasized that the company really complied with the production and business plan, adhering to the technical and safety standards and the environment without any accidents. Any happened inside the mine and there was no leakage of waste that affected the people and the environment around the area.
In addition, in connection with the claim that nearly 200 families are in a land dispute with Let Cheng Mining Development Co., Ltd., Mr. Prak Min, the chief of Sochet commune, confirmed that no such case occurred. That no.
The commune chief said that not only are there no land disputes with the people, the company also understands that the people can put the pump in the company's license.
The commune chief added that the people in this area always run a family gold mine in the rainy season, currently there are about 105 places in the company's license location. He said that the Ministry of Mines and local authorities always come down to explain the illegality and danger that may occur from this anarchic activities.
With a happy smile, Hin, a resident of the area, said her family could earn thousands of dollars a month to make ends meet, as she and her husband worked for the company, earning an estimated monthly income. $ 900 and additional income of children working for this company.
According to Ing Depola, the mining sector is a natural resource that is more unique than other natural resources, so it must be developed in a sustainable, transparent, efficient, effective, harmonious and prosperous way for the economy, society and nation. Thinking about the impact on the environment and society, how to minimize the impact.
Mr. Ing Depola added that the Ministry has conducted a thorough study before issuing a license to any company, evaluating the experience, reports, achievements, business plans, business plans and finances of the company. For the location to be provided, there must be an environmental impact assessment study with the support of the Ministry of Environment, local authorities and citizens.
