Law on the Establishment of the Ministry of Inspection and the Establishment of the Secretariat of State for Border Affairs in Conformity with the Constitution (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council has already decided that the Law on the Establishment of the Ministry of Inspection and the Law on the Establishment of the Secretariat of State for Border Affairs is in accordance with the Constitution. .
On September 28, 2023, the Constitutional Council convened a plenary session chaired by Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, to review and finalize the request of Samdech NA President Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly, to review the constitutionality of the two laws. .
As a result of the meeting, the Constitutional Council unanimously decided:
1. The Law on the Establishment of the Ministry of Inspection, which was approved by the National Assembly on September 14, 2023 at the first session of the National Assembly, the seventh legislature, and the Senate reviewed and gave its full opinion on the form and concept of the law without amendment and consideration. As a matter of urgency, the fourth extraordinary session of the Senate on September 21, 2023, was declared unconstitutional.
2: The Law on the Establishment of the Secretariat of State for Border Affairs, which was approved by the National Assembly on September 14, 2023, at the first session of the National Assembly, the seventh legislature, and the Senate reviewed and gave its full unanimous opinion on the form and concept of the law. The fourth extraordinary session of the Senate on September 21, 2023, was declared in accordance with the Constitution.
