(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration is urging all officials to make efforts to learn about the management of registrations or digital identification in order to make that management more effective and contribute to maintaining social security.
This morning, September 28, 2023, a joint meeting was held on the registration of civil status through the notification of health facilities using technology. Digital at Phnom Penh Capital Hall. The meeting was chaired by Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor, Representative of Mr. Khuong Sreng and Lt. Gen. Ouk Chay Panhara, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Identification, Ministry of Interior.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Keut Chhe said that the registration of registers using digital technology is very important and also in line with the pentagonal strategy of His Majesty Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia for the seventh mandate.
He said that the management of civil registration or digital identity system is very important, if well managed, the national economy and national security will run smoothly and better, but if not managed, it will lead to insecurity. In society. Therefore, officials under the administration of Phnom Penh must strive to learn on the management of civil status or identification through this digital technology system.
According to Mr. Keut Chhe, learning to register through the notification of the health center using the above digital technology will help officials gain knowledge for themselves and take this knowledge to contribute to the motherland. More of us.
