(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, called on all residents to be careful and take care of their personal and children's safety during the rainy season to avoid drowning, electric shock as well as protection from animals. Unnatural venom stings or bites.
At the same time, the provincial governor also advised residents to prepare some food and medicine for first aid to avoid serious accidents during the current flood.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak made this appeal when he inspected the flood situation and visited people in their homes and safe places in Chhouk Boeung village, Chhouk commune in Prasat Sambo district, which was severely flooded in the area. Some on September 27, 2023.
The governor said that the Kampong Thom provincial administration has also prepared a working group of professional officers of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to inspect and assess the impact on people's rice crops to provide rice seeds for cultivation after the flood.
He added: "We look at the actual situation now, the people affected by the flooding of their homes, they went to a safe place or their plantation to avoid the eventual danger."
On behalf of the provincial authorities, Mr. Nguon Rattanak called on all people to be more careful and pay attention to personal safety, maintain cleanliness, even if people have lived with the floods for many years and please Follow the information of the National Committee for Disaster Management through the number 1294 when you call to get information about the flood situation in time.
