This statement was made by the Minister of Environment during a meeting with leaders and civil servants of the General Department of Policy and Strategy on the morning of September 27, 2023 at the Ministry.
The Ministry must prepare an internal action plan, review the external action plan and seize the opportunity for Cambodia to move towards clean, green and sustainable based on the capabilities of Cambodia, especially the leaders and officials of the Ministry of Environment. The Ministry itself has highly skilled human resources who can do environmental work on the international stage, showcasing work, raising funds from projects without losing independence, sovereignty and ownership.
Addressing the meeting, the Minister of Environment urged the Department of Policy and Strategy to break down the Royal Government's strategic plan and launch an action plan that responds to both the government and the needs of the people.
Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development recommends seven points to improve nutrition and food security in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ouk Rabun, Senior Minister, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development and Chairman of the National Committee for the Promotion of the One Village, One Product Movement, made seven recommendations to improve the food security and nutrition sector to achieve its goals. Two of the goals of sustainable development are to end hunger, achieve food security, improve nutritional status and promote sustainable agriculture.
Senior Minister Ouk Rabun encouraged stakeholders and citizens to participate:
* 7th. Continue to invest in new discoveries and technologies, and strengthen research, collection, analysis, compilation, dissemination and use of data on the cultivation of markets, agricultural products and food security and nutrition to better decision makers, planners and related strategies. Which enables us to effectively monitor progress and determine approaches to appropriate implementation.
The recommendation of Dr. Ouk Rabun was made at the Consultative Workshop on Analysis of Nutrient Deficiency in Cambodia on September 27, 2023, which shared the results and findings from the analysis of malnutrition. Malnutrition in Cambodia and some recommendations to stakeholders to intervene in a timely manner to improve food security and nutrition in Cambodia.
Malnutrition and malnutrition are signs of economic change and predict even greater challenges in the future, including non-communicable diseases.
Malnutrition in early childhood not only affects children's health and mortality, but also affects children's mental development, learning and future productivity, and the result is not only the family economy. Not only that, but it has also affected the entire national economy.
