Siem Reap Provincial Authority Launches Environmental Clean-Up Campaign in Siem Reap City to Celebrate World Tourism Day 2023
(Siem Reap): Mr. Prak Sophoan, Governor of Siem Reap Province, on September 27, 2023, led a campaign to clean up the environment in Siem Reap to celebrate the World Tourism Day 2023 under the theme "Tourism and Green Investment" with the participation of officials Government officials around the province, as well as students from various schools, many national and international partner organizations.
This environmental clean-up campaign to ensure attractiveness for natural green tourism destinations and promote development in line with the needs of national and international tourists to celebrate World Tourism Day under the theme "Tourism and Green Investment".
Provincial Governor Prak Sophoan said that the organization of the campaign to clean up the city environment today in order to inspire the movement of the people, the armed forces, government officials at all levels, students to participate in cleaning, improving the beauty of cities, towns, rural areas. Pagodas, schools, hospitals, factories, enterprises and markets aim to contribute to building a Cambodian society with a clean and beautiful environment.
Mr. Prak Sophoan continued that the quality of the environment, the beauty of the city, the public welfare need to be taken into account. Waste management must know how to pack and sort all kinds of waste such as recyclable waste (scrap), organic waste, hazardous waste and other waste to turn some waste into economic value and reduce the amount of waste in public places.
He also expressed his pride in running an environmental clean-up campaign in Siem Reap to celebrate International Ozone Day and World Tourism Day 2023 under the theme "Tourism and Green Investment" in this beloved tourism province. The year has been fruitful and there has been an even greater involvement from stakeholders as well as public schools, sub-national administrations, the private sector, and local communities.
Through this joint action, it is also a message to spread awareness of the importance of a clean environment in all homes, villages, public places, proper storage and management of waste, good hygiene, to make this tourist province green and beautiful. Fresh air, rivers and all streets are comfortable, attract tourists and provide well-being to national and international guests and get ready to celebrate World Tourism Day 2023.
