(Phnom Penh): More than 1 million students in more than 1,000 schools across the country took part in a campaign to reduce the use of plastic and vowed, "Today I will not use plastic bags." This was stated by Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment on Monday, September 25, 2023, during a meeting with leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Environment.
The Minister stated that this is a success that the campaign has covered throughout the country, and the above results show the attention to participate in reducing the use of plastic bags from all stakeholders, including government institutions, the private sector, local authorities at all levels. Classes as well as teachers and students in schools across the country.
In addition, about 10,000 workers at more than 10 factories in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville participated in a campaign to reduce the use of plastic under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags", which set to start from September 22, 2023.
Please note that the Ministry of Environment has launched a campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags under the theme "Today I do not use plastic bags" under the initiative of HE Dr. Eang Sophalleth on September 1, 2023 to improve the well-being of the people. Cities and localities should be further improved as well as boosting the national economy by promoting the use of local products instead of plastic bags.
The campaign started in 44 schools in Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province and was attended by more than 18,700 students. The campaign is currently being implemented in schools in the capital and other provinces across the country.
The Minister of Environment stated that the campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags requires the participation of all stakeholders, including government institutions, the private sector, development partners and civil society, as well as teachers, students in schools and especially workers. In factories, enterprises and people, this campaign can be successful, efficient and effective.
