During the meeting, General Sar Thet stated that all leaders and officers of the Economic Crimes Police Department must improve their quality and ability to fight economic crimes in order to show responsibility to the Royal Government. Like the well-being of people across the country.
In order to carry out the professional work effectively, General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner General, made five recommendations to the Economic Crime Police Department, including:
* First, to build a practical plan in accordance with the new situation and the progress of the society, as well as a clear division of duties and responsibilities to implement the plan effectively.
* Third: Improve the professional capacity to research, investigate and suppress economic crimes to the root.
* Fourth: Promote ownership in research, investigation and suppression, especially the crime of smuggling, tax evasion that leads to loss of national budget revenue, substandard or unlicensed drugs and substandard food that seriously affect the well-being of the population. Citizens.
* Fifth: Increase cooperation with stakeholders both inside and outside the country in the fight against economic crime to be active.
