1: Public and Financial Services Decentralization Reform Program Phase 2 - Sub-program 2 aims to contribute to Cambodia in improving the efficiency of sub-national officials to make it easier for people to access public services by focusing on 1 : Improving sub-national planning and budgeting, 2: Strengthening revenue and expenditure management, and 3: Strengthening sub-national administrative capacity.
The program is expected to cost a total of US $ 40 million, a full ADB concessional loan led by the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development.
Skills Development Program for the Future Economy - The first sub-program aims to improve current and future employment rates through policy reform and project investment to strengthen skills development. The program will strengthen training in environmentally friendly industries as well as increase resources for developing skills that respond directly to job requirements.
The program is expected to cost a total of US $ 131.30 million, including an ADB concessional loan of about US $ 100 million, led by the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
The signing ceremony now reflects the ADB's strengthening and expanding cooperation, support and trust in the Royal Government of Cambodia by the ADB.
Overall, the purpose of the two newly signed programs will be to effectively respond to the policies of the Royal Government of the Seventh Legislature of the National Assembly, especially the Pentagon Strategy - Phase I, which the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Hun Manet Recently announced for implementation recently.
The Deputy Prime Minister also recalled that the ADB had provided a total of US $ 4.9 billion in co-financing, including US $ 4.4 billion in concessional loans for implementation. 137 projects / programs and grants totaling approximately US $ 568 million to implement 70 projects / programs.
