Cambodia, Turkey expand scope of health cooperation
(Phnom Penh): During a working meeting and courtesy call held on September 25, 2023 between the Minister of Health, Professor Chheang Ra and the Ambassador of the Republic of Turkey to Cambodia, Ms. Ulku Kocaefe, both sides The two sides pledged to expand cooperation in the field of health. The meeting was held at the Ministry.
The Minister thanked the Government of the Republic of Turkey through the Embassy of the Republic of Turkey in Cambodia, which has always had good diplomatic relations and contributed to the improvement of the health care system in Cambodia.
In response, the Ambassador congratulated and wished the Minister on the occasion of gaining the trust of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate to be appointed Minister of Health.
The Ambassador requested the support of the Ministry of Health in the preparation of the agreement on health cooperation between the two countries and informed that the Ministry of Health of Turkey requested the establishment of cooperation with the Ministry of Health of Cambodia in the training of human resources, public health. Hospital management and research.
The Minister welcomed and thanked for the request for cooperation and requested the technical officials of the Ministry of Health of the two countries to discuss the cooperation agreement as soon as possible.
The Ambassador pledged to strengthen cooperation, support the Ministry of Health's priority plans, and help expand the scope of Cambodia-Turkey bilateral cooperation in the field of health through close cooperation with the Ministry of Health's technical working group.
