Opinion: The real national development process is not on the lips of the extremist opposition!
(Phnom Penh): Recently, especially during the time when Cambodian leader Samdech Manet was in the United States, there was a handful of criticism from extremist opposition groups on some aspects of their attacks on Cambodian leaders. That is not recognized as a clan government and accused of painting that the president did not consider the interests of the Cambodian people.
They compared the new leaders of the neighboring countries to the presidents, boasting that they were all talented and good, and devalued their leaders. They protested against the presence of the president on American soil, declaring that they had been very successful in opposing the leaders of their own country.
Millions of Cambodians have made it clear that they will choose their leaders by deciding to cast their ballots on July 23, 2023. The vast majority of Cambodians of voting age enjoy free, fair, transparent and non-violent elections.
Moreover, the results are clear and indisputable, with both national and international observers as witnesses: more than 84% of the people went to the polls and more than 82% voted for the CPP. The will of the majority of the people is to support and elect the Cambodian People's Party, which had a candidate for Prime Minister Hun Manet as Prime Minister at that time.
So, is it fair between a group of extremist monkeys who speak out against the leadership of Samdech Thipdey, while more than 82% of the Cambodian people choose to trust and fully support Samdech? If all these extremists use their brains to think a little, they will find the right answer that the word true democracy is a majority vote, not a minority vote with traitors fleeing the country and doing fraudulent politics. The people behind it come as a base.
On behalf of the Cambodian people, we are deeply saddened by the extremist opposition who insulted the leader who was born out of the choice, love and support of a Cambodian kingdom, and even insulted the Samdech by comparing it with the leaders of other countries. Absolutely acceptable.
We are not hurt by their immoral words and anarchy, but we are hurt by their attacks on our leaders, falsehoods, deception of the masses, despite the fact that the President since taking office as Prime Minister, Samdech Kom Work hard for the cause of the nation and the people.
In just one month, Samdech has achieved great achievements for the nation and the people of Cambodia, such as the introduction of new policies in addition to the old policies, efforts to reform and rehabilitate all sectors to be more vibrant and more effective. The benefits have reached the hands of the Cambodian people, especially the poor, Samdech always thinks all the time.
The Royal Government's efforts to serve the people and promote progress for the nation have not been mentioned by the extremist extremists at all. The values and diligence of the leaders of their homeland.
Is such an act worthy of being born? If they were born a little, they would not insult, trample on the face and honor of their country, destroy their country's interests in any form without fear. In fact, the actions of those extremist opposition groups are not unusual if we look at the background of their bosses.
Their bosses have used this kind of immoral policy against Samdech Techo Hun Sen many times before, when Samdech was the Prime Minister, even though Samdech Techo had pardoned them many times, they They still do not give up their undemocratic power grabbing ideas.
Therefore, we must join together in all sections of the social cell to join our Royal Government in the common goal of promoting the nation to grow beyond what we are now without having to worry about extremism. Popularism that aims to destroy our nation.
By: Pov Thidavann
(Phnom Penh): The issue of democracy and human rights in Cambodia is one of the issues raised by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, in a meeting with the Secretary-General of the United Nations, the Deputy Secretary of State for the United States and the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Australia. .
Democracy and human rights in Cambodia have always been divided between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations, as well as the United States and Australia.
On the sidelines of the 78th United Nations General Assembly in New York, President Hun Manet also met with UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres, Deputy Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs Victoria Nuland. US and Australian Foreign Minister Penny Wong.
Please be reminded that according to the post on the social media of Samdech Hun Manet highlighted that in the meeting with the Secretary-General of the United Nations on September 22, after listening to the explanation of the President on democracy and human rights. To the Secretary-General of the United Nations, expressing satisfaction and confirming that the United Nations continues to support Cambodia's development program.
In addition, in his speech at the 78th General Assembly of the United Nations on September 22, 2023, His Excellency Hun Manet also highlighted the political maturity in Cambodia and the courage of Cambodia. Cambodians in the exercise of democratic rights.
Samdech Hun Sen highlighted that the process of building democracy in Cambodia has also progressed steadily. In July this year, Cambodia successfully held general elections with 18 political parties contesting more than 8.2 million people. The turnout was 84.59 percent, the highest since the 1993 UN General Assembly.
