Kan Ben - Pchum Ben is one of the major Khmer festivals. Traditionally, Cambodians have been celebrating the Kan Ben-Pchum Ben festival every year since ancient times. However, this festival, as well as other Buddhist traditions and customs, was completely abolished during the Pol Pot regime between 1975 and 1979.
According to the records of the history of the Khmer festival, this Kan Ben and Pchum Ben festival was organized by our people to pray for the blessings of Kosal Phal Bon to the parents, the rich, the ancestors, the family, the 7 relatives who passed away. To the next world. This year's Kanben-Pchum Ben festival will run from September 30 to October 14, 2023. Touch San, 101, Chan Yun, 90.
