A visit to review the past cooperation that the Ministry of Information of Cambodia and the Voice of Vietnam have done in the past and to review more recent cooperation in the field of information of the two countries.
Minister Neth Pheaktra said the visit would strengthen ties and cooperation between the two sides. The past and present cooperation between the Ministry of Information of Cambodia and the Voice of Vietnam has yielded good results.
At the same time, the Minister focused on strengthening the capacity of professional officers and developing human resources in journalism and exchanging work experience in technical fields.
Minister Neth Pheaktra also thanked the Vietnamese side for helping Cambodia with technical equipment, radio and television, including: a mobile car, a television and a mobile car radio.
Do Tien Sy, Director General of the Voice of Vietnam, said that the Voice of Vietnam has cooperated with various media agencies on every continent and various national broadcast stations, including the Ministry of Information. Cambodia is the most intimate and effective relationship.
Do Tien Sy, Director General of the Voice of Vietnam, said: “In the future, our two sides will continue to exchange information on politics, economy, society and culture. We are ready to exchange technical experts with Cambodia. "We are confident that our relationship will continue to develop and contribute to the assertion of a better and closer relationship between Vietnam and Cambodia."
At the end of the meeting, the two sides signed a memorandum of understanding between the Ministry of Information and the Voice of Vietnam on information and media cooperation.
